window.OSAP_FT=window.OSAP_FT||{};window.OSAP_FT["12"]={"https://theconversation.com/labor-slumps-to-new-lows-in-two-victorian-polls-296132":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:16Z","sha":"517ae165afd5f576da27facfca33e4438ac01e54d1909f7ec20009792427bda8","read":"https://theconversation.com/labor-slumps-to-new-lows-in-two-victorian-polls-296132","bytes":181453,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Labor slumps to new lows in two Victorian polls","by":[{"n":"Adrian Beaumont","r":"Election Analyst (Psephologist) at The Conversation; and Honorary Associate, School of Mathematics and Statistics, The University of Melbourne"}],"pub":"2026-11-10T05:15:26Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["With less than three weeks until the November 28 Victorian election, a DemosAU poll has Labor’s primary vote plunging seven points since September to just 18%, only one point ahead of the Greens. The Resolve poll isn’t as dramatic, but Labor’s 22% is still an equal record low."]},{"k":"p","s":["In both polls, the Coalition would easily win the election with 55–56% of the two-party vote against Labor. In all recent polls, the Coalition has gained to take a big lead. They are likely to win a majority of the 88 lower house seats in their own right. The graph below shows how bad the polls have become for Labor."]},{"k":"p","s":["If the DemosAU poll is accurate, Labor is facing a near-total wipeout, losing left-wing inner city seats to the Greens and other seats to the Coalition and One Nation. Liberal preference recommendations between Labor and the Greens could be important."]},{"k":"p","s":["I believe the recent poll movement is because people are now focusing on the state election, and they want Labor out. Labor has governed in Victoria for the last 12 years and 23 of the last 27."]},{"k":"p","s":["This article also includes a Victorian Pakenham seat poll and two more federal polls."]},{"k":"h","s":["DemosAU Victorian poll"]},{"k":"p","s":["A Victorian ",["DemosAU and PremierNational poll","https://www.heraldsun.com.au/news/victoria/state-election/coalition-surges-to-5644-lead-as-victorian-labor-faces-catastrophic-state-election-wipeout/news-story/cfd77a95d33cd90b152b633f1f4642cb"]," for The Herald Sun, conducted October 30 to November 5 from a sample of 1,562, gave the Coalition 33% of the primary vote (up three since the ",["mid-September DemosAU poll","https://demosau.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/DemosAU-Report-Victoria-Poll-September-2026.pdf"],"), One Nation 21% (up one), Labor 18% (down seven), the Greens 17% (up three) and all Others 11% (steady)."]},{"k":"p","s":["After preferences, the Coalition led Labor by 56–44, a four-point gain for the Coalition. On these primary votes, one of Labor or the Greens would make the final two in most seats, surpassing One Nation on the other left party’s preferences."]},{"k":"p","s":["Labor premier Ben Carroll’s net positive score slumped 16 points -30 (47% negative, 17% positive). Liberal leader Jess Wilson’s was up five points to +13 (38% positive, 25% negative). One Nation state leader Warren Pickering’s was down two points to -20 (43% negative, 23% positive). Greens leader Ellen Sandell was at -20 (38% negative, 18% positive)."]},{"k":"p","s":["In a three-way preferred premier question, Wilson had 36%, Carroll 28% and Pickering 19%. Wilson led Carroll by 48–30 head to head. Some figures are from ",["The Poll Bludger","https://www.pollbludger.net/2026/11/09/demosau-labor-18-coalition-33-one-nation-21-in-victoria/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Victorian Resolve poll"]},{"k":"p","s":["A Victorian ",["Resolve poll","https://www.theage.com.au/politics/victoria/half-of-victorians-open-to-a-one-nation-coalition-as-carroll-faces-labor-wipeout-20261109-p61cjv.html"]," for The Age, conducted November 2–7 from a sample of 1,000, gave the Coalition 30% of the primary vote (up two since the early October Resolve poll), One Nation 23% (steady), Labor 22% (down three), the Greens 13% (down two), independents 6% (up two) and others 7% (up two). This is tied with January 2025 for Labor’s worst primary vote in this poll."]},{"k":"p","s":["No two-party estimate was provided, but analyst ",["Kevin Bonham estimated a Coalition","https://x.com/kevinbonham/status/2119683731883749870"]," lead over Labor by about 55–45, a three-point gain for the Coalition."]},{"k":"p","s":["Carroll’s net likeability was down five points to -16, his worst since he replaced Jacinta Allan as premier in late July. Wilson’s has improved in each poll since July and is now at a record high of +24 (up one since October and up 11 since July). Pickering’s has also improved in every poll since August and is now at +9 (up one since October and up nine since August)."]},{"k":"p","s":["In a three-way preferred premier question, Wilson had 35% (up six), Carroll 21% (down one) and Pickering 15% (up one)."]},{"k":"p","s":["By 48–38, respondents were comfortable with the Coalition governing in partnership with One Nation, but by 50–38 they were not comfortable with Labor governing with the Greens."]},{"k":"h","s":["Victorian Pakenham seat poll"]},{"k":"p","s":["Pickering is One Nation’s candidate for ",["Pakenham","https://www.abc.net.au/news/elections/vic/2026/guide/pake"],", which Labor won by 50.4–49.6 against the Liberals at the 2022 election. A ",["TKW Research/DemosAU","https://www.heraldsun.com.au/news/victoria/state-election/one-nation-poised-to-win-first-victorian-lower-house-seat-amid-pakenham-poll-surge/news-story/0ee84fdba88eed1dda2f35b5f3c60135"]," poll for The Herald Sun, conducted November 4–8 from a small sample of 484, gave Pickering 40% of the primary vote, the Liberals 24% and Labor 14% with no other candidates listed."]},{"k":"p","s":["Despite Pickering’s 16-point lead on primary votes, he’s tied after preferences at 50–50 with the Liberals, indicating a strong flow of Labor and other preferences to the Liberals. Seat polls are unreliable."]},{"k":"h","s":["Candidate nominations for the election"]},{"k":"p","s":["Candidate nominations for the Victorian election closed on Monday. ABC election analyst ",["Antony Green said there are a total","https://antonygreen.com.au/vic2026-candidate-numbers-at-close-of-nominations/"]," of 734 lower house candidates for the 88 seats, an average of 8.3 per seat. That’s down slightly from a record 740 candidates in 2022."]},{"k":"p","s":["Labor, the Coalition, One Nation, the Greens and the Victorian Socialists are contesting all 88 seats and Family First 71, with 91 independents."]},{"k":"p","s":["The upper house has eight regions that each return five members for a total of 40 seats. The scrapping of group ticket voting has resulted in the number of upper house candidates plunging from a record 454 in 2022 to 303, the lowest since 2010. There are an average of 12.4 groups per region, down from a record 22.2 in 2022."]},{"k":"h","s":["Federal Spectre poll"]},{"k":"p","s":["A national ",["Spectre Strategy poll","https://static1.squarespace.com/static/67cd0be72bb18b3c88b9af04/t/6af0f31063b80c7df5dd8a75/1794175760382/Political+Update+November+26-+Spectre+Strategy.pdf"],", conducted October 28 to November 3 from a sample of 2,093, gave One Nation 28% of the primary vote (up two since the ",["mid-July Spectre poll","https://static1.squarespace.com/static/67cd0be72bb18b3c88b9af04/t/6a66a724a5b0f842d4f3f3b2/1785112356745/Political+Update+July+26-+Spectre+Strategy.pdf"],"), Labor 25% (down three), the Coalition 24% (up one), the Greens 13% (up one) and all Others 10% (down one)."]},{"k":"p","s":["By respondent preferences, Labor led One Nation by 52–48, a two-point gain for One Nation. The Coalition led Labor by 53–47, a four-point gain for the Coalition."]},{"k":"p","s":["Anthony Albanese’s net favourability was down 14 points to a record low of -25 (54% unfavourable, 29% favourable). Angus Taylor’s was up five points to -2 (29% unfavourable, 27% favourable). Pauline Hanson’s was down three points to -4 (45% unfavourable, 41% favourable)."]},{"k":"p","s":["In a three-way preferred PM question, Albanese had 34%, Hanson 30% and Taylor 22%."]},{"k":"h","s":["Morgan poll"]},{"k":"p","s":["A national ",["Morgan poll","https://www.roymorgan.com/findings/10377-federal-voting-intention-november-9-2026"],", conducted October 26 to November 8 from a sample of 2,574, gave Labor 25.5% of the primary vote (down 0.5 since the mid-October Morgan poll), One Nation 24.5% (up two), the Coalition 22% (down 1.5), the Greens 15% (down 0.5) and all Others 13% (up 0.5)."]},{"k":"p","s":["By respondent preferences, Labor led One Nation by 54–46, a one-point gain for One Nation. Labor led the Coalition by 51–49, a 1.5-point gain for the Coalition. By 2025 election preference flows, Labor led the Coalition by 52.5–47.5, a 0.5-point gain for the Coalition."]},{"k":"p","s":["Morgan’s polls are taken over a fortnight. Weekly breakdowns had Labor leading the Coalition by 51.5–48.5 in late October, but only by 50.5–49.5 in early November."]},{"k":"h","s":["Essential poll: additional questions on Melbourne Cup"]},{"k":"p","s":["Additional questions on the Melbourne Cup from the ",["late October Essential poll","https://essentialreport.com.au/reports/28-october-2026"]," were released on Cup Day (November 3). On interest level, 68% (up 13) said they had low or no interest, 23% (down three) moderate interest and 9% (down nine) high interest."]},{"k":"p","s":["On betting, 46% (up six and up 11 since 2024) said they’re not interested in the Cup and won’t place a bet, 25% (up one) said they rarely bet on horse races, but would watch the Cup and place a bet, 17% (down one) said they would watch the Cup but not bet and 12% (down six) said they regularly bet on horse races."]}],"chars":6919},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/democratic-republic-of-the-congo":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T16:30Z","sha":"8762ac8dee605ed25f0c0604bf34d6db2269fc3d2c3cbad1180995963bf10568","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/democratic-republic-of-the-congo","bytes":104957,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Democratic Republic of the Congo travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-03-05T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-10-08T13:20:38+01:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["Your travel insurance could be invalidated if you travel against advice from the Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO)."]},{"k":"h","s":["Areas where FCDO advises against travel"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Areas in Kinshasa Province"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["The districts of N’djili and Kimbanseke in Kinshasa city south of the main access road to N’djili airport, in Nsele commune"]},{"k":"li","s":["The N1 road in Kinshasa Province, between and including Menkao to the west, Kenge to the east, the border of Mai-Ndombe province to the north, and 10km to the south"]},{"k":"hs","s":["DRC-Central African Republic border"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to within 50km of the border with the Central African Republic."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Eastern DRC"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to the provinces of:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Haut-Uélé and Ituri, including the entire DRC-South Sudan border"]},{"k":"li","s":["North Kivu"]},{"k":"li","s":["South Kivu"]},{"k":"li","s":["Maniema"]},{"k":"li","s":["Tanganyika"]},{"k":"li","s":["Haut-Lomami"]},{"k":"hs","s":["South-East DRC"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to Upemba National Park. If you choose to travel to Upemba National Park against FCDO advise, notify the park authorities about your travel plans."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Territory in Mai-Ndombe Province"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to the Kwamouth territory of Mai-Ndombe Province. This is between, and including, the towns of Kwamouth, Bandundu and the southern border of Mai-Ndombe province."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Kisangani airport"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to Bangoka International Airport, Kisangani due to multiple drone attacks in the area of Kisangani airport."]},{"k":"p","s":["See details about ",["why FCDO advises against travel","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/democratic-republic-of-the-congo/regional-risks"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Security situation in DRC"]},{"k":"hs","s":["North and South Kivu"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are in North or South Kivu and judge it safe to do so, and if routes are available, you should leave."]},{"k":"p","s":["M23 rebels and Rwanda Defence Forces (RDF) have captured the cities of Goma and Bukavu and the surrounding areas in North and South Kivu. M23 rebels and RDF captured the city of Uvira in December 2025, and then withdrew from the city in January 2026, though clashes continue in the surrounding areas. The situation remains highly unstable and unpredictable. Routes to depart Uvira, Goma and Bukavu are limited and may change at short notice."]},{"k":"p","s":["The border crossings between Rwanda and the DRC at Gisenyi-Goma and Ruzizi-Bukavu could close at short notice."]},{"k":"p","s":["Goma and Bukavu airports have been attacked and commercial flights are no longer operating from the airports."]},{"k":"p","s":["Support from the UK government is severely limited outside Kinshasa. You should not assume that FCDO will be able to provide assistance to leave the country in the event of serious unrest or crisis."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Tshopo Province"]},{"k":"p","s":["On 23 May, there were multiple drone attacks in the area of Kisangani airport. These incidents have led to disruption to flights. The security situation remains unpredictable, and further disruption is possible."]},{"k":"h","s":["Ebola"]},{"k":"p","s":["On 17 May, the World Health Organization (WHO) declared the Ebola (Bundibugyo virus disease) outbreak in DRC a ",["Public Health Emergency of International Concern","https://www.who.int/news/item/17-05-2026-epidemic-of-ebola-disease-in-the-democratic-republic-of-the-congo-and-uganda-determined-a-public-health-emergency-of-international-concern"],". The outbreak is highly active, evolving and geographically widespread."]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel to DRC read ",["Ebola Disease in DRC","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/news/909/ebola-disease-in-drc-and-uganda"]," and ",["general information on Ebola and similar diseases","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/68/viral-haemorrhagic-fever"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are in DRC read ",["how to reduce your risk from Ebola","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/democratic-republic-of-the-congo/health"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Some countries have additional health screening requirements or entry restrictions for travellers arriving from, or who have recently visited the DRC. ",["Check entry requirements","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/"]," for any destination or transit country before travelling."]},{"k":"h","s":["Help and support in DRC"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read FCDO advice on how to deal with a crisis overseas."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Getting help in DRC"]},{"k":"p","s":["For help in an emergency from the British government, telephone: +243815566200"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["‘Getting help’","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/democratic-republic-of-the-congo/getting-help"]," for more information on other ways to get help in DRC."]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact FCDO in London"]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/democratic-republic-of-the-congo/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in the Democratic Republic of the Congo (DRC) set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["DRC Embassy in the UK","https://www.ambardc.london/c/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["Your passport must have an ‘expiry date’ at least 6 months after the date you arrive in DRC."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must have a visa to visit DRC."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Applying for a visa"]},{"k":"p","s":["Apply for a visa through the ",["DRC Embassy in the UK","https://forms.ambardc.london/visa/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Allow at least 2 to 3 weeks for application processing."]},{"k":"p","s":["Some types of visa applications are referred to Kinshasa for a decision. In these cases, if you submit a letter of invitation from the person or organisation you’re visiting, stamped by the Ministry of Foreign Affairs in Kinshasa, you may speed up the process."]},{"k":"p","s":["Consider getting a long-term visa if you are planning to stay in DRC for a considerable period. When you apply for or renew a long-term visa, DRC authorities need a ‘consular certificate’ as part of the application. The British Embassy in DRC can issue a consular certificate for you."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Checks at border control"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you have a Rwandan or Ugandan immigration stamp in your passport you may have some difficulties on arrival, but it should not prevent you from entering DRC."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re crossing regularly between Rwanda and DRC you may have immigration difficulties if you have not regularised your residency status."]},{"k":"h","s":["Ebola"]},{"k":"p","s":["You may encounter health screening measures, such as being required to fill in a passenger locator form on arrival and departure and temperature checks, including at airports."]},{"k":"p","s":["Some countries have heightened health screening for travellers from DRC. ",["Check entry requirements","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/"]," for the country you’re travelling to or transiting."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Rwanda","https://x.com/RwandaHealth/status/2057790371657101712?s=20"]," and ",["Uganda","https://x.com/MinofHealthUG/status/2057471796497035293"]," have announced restrictions which impact travellers to DRC."]},{"k":"p","s":["The UK’s Returning Workers Scheme has been activated, due to the outbreak of Ebola disease. Returning health and humanitarian workers should check the latest at ",["UK’s Returning Workers Scheme","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/ebola-returning-workers-scheme"]," before returning to the UK."]},{"k":"h","s":["Departure tax"]},{"k":"p","s":["You need to pay a departure tax of 55 US dollars on international flights and 10 US dollars on domestic flights. You pay these fees when you check in for your departure. Get an official receipt and a copy for each fee. Hand the originals on request to immigration and at boarding and keep the copies."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter DRC, you must have certificates to prove you’ve had:"]},{"k":"li","s":["a yellow fever vaccination"]},{"k":"li","s":["a polio vaccine, in some circumstances"]},{"k":"p","s":["For full details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s DRC guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/63/democratic-republic-of-the-congo#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You may need a yellow fever certificate for onward travel to some other countries, due to the risk of yellow fever in DRC."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about goods you can take into or out of DRC. You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"p","s":["You may have difficulties when entering DRC if you are travelling with:"]},{"k":"li","s":["satellite phones"]},{"k":"li","s":["GPS receivers"]},{"k":"li","s":["military clothing"]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"p","s":["This guide also has safety advice for ",["regions of the Democratic Republic of the Congo (DRC)","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/democratic-republic-of-the-congo/regional-risks"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in DRC"]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorists are very likely to try to carry out attacks in DRC."]},{"k":"p","s":["ADF, a militant group with links to Daesh, carry out regular attacks in North Kivu and Ituri provinces, eastern DRC. The majority of its attacks target villages in rural areas, but it has attacked military targets – primarily Ugandan and Congolese armed forces personnel. Attacks have also targeted bars, places of worship, markets and vehicle convoys."]},{"k":"p","s":["Attacks could be indiscriminate including in places visited by foreign nationals. Stay aware of your surroundings, keep up to date with local media reports and follow the advice of local authorities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Political situation"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protests and demonstrations"]},{"k":"p","s":["A range of military and peacekeeping forces are deployed in eastern DRC. Tensions about the presence of these forces and the role of international actors can cause protests in Goma and Kinshasa. There have been large protests against the UN peacekeeping mission known as the United Nations Organization Stabilization Mission (MONUSCO). In February 2024 there were protests outside the British Embassy and other western embassies. Similar protests cannot be ruled out in future. These could be directed at foreign nationals or target UN vehicles and premises."]},{"k":"p","s":["On 28 January 2025, there were large and violent protests outside multiple embassies in Kinshasa, in response to the fighting in eastern DRC. This resulted in an increased security presence and there is an ongoing risk of sporadic protests, which can involve gun fire."]},{"k":"p","s":["Public gatherings and demonstrations can occur with little or no notice and can quickly turn violent."]},{"k":"p","s":["Protests may result in:"]},{"k":"li","s":["the closure of shops and public services"]},{"k":"li","s":["restrictions on movement"]},{"k":"p","s":["In the event of serious unrest:"]},{"k":"li","s":["commercial flights may be suspended"]},{"k":"li","s":["roads may be blocked"]},{"k":"li","s":["international borders may be closed at short notice, particularly those with Rwanda, at Gisenyi/Goma and Cyangugu/Bukavu"]},{"k":"li","s":["internet connections and mobile phone networks may have reduced services or be cut off"]},{"k":"li","s":["military and police presence in Kinshasa and other major cities may increase - this may include stop-and-search checkpoints, especially after dark"]},{"k":"p","s":["To minimise your personal risk:"]},{"k":"li","s":["follow local media for news of any planned protests"]},{"k":"li","s":["leave quickly and do not attempt to watch or photograph any demonstration or disturbance"]},{"k":"li","s":["consider making contingency plans"]},{"k":"li","s":["keep a stock of essential supplies"]},{"k":"li","s":["keep your travel documents up-to-date, including appropriate visas"]},{"k":"li","s":["be prepared to move or go into curfew at short notice if told to by the authorities"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["how to prepare for a crisis overseas","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"]]},{"k":"p","s":["Stay away from areas where protests are planned, particularly in Kinshasa, Goma and other large cities. This may include:"]},{"k":"li","s":["N’Djili airport, Kinshasa"]},{"k":"li","s":["Churches and other religious buildings and institutions"]},{"k":"li","s":["large sporting stadiums or music venues"]},{"k":"li","s":["universities"]},{"k":"li","s":["political party headquarters"]},{"k":"li","s":["foreign embassies"]},{"k":"li","s":["government and parliament buildings"]},{"k":"li","s":["offices of the Electoral Commission"]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not assume FCDO will be able to help you leave the country in the event of serious unrest."]},{"k":"h","s":["Traveling around DRC"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is widespread poverty, social exclusion and health risks in many parts of the DRC. You may be at greater risk of being robbed or attacked in rural areas. Transport and accommodation are extremely limited outside Kinshasa and the major towns, so make travel arrangements in advance. Travel in the company of experienced people or organisations."]},{"k":"p","s":["Be respectful of local customs and land rights, including the necessary permissions for activities. Recent incidents have occurred with local communities when foreign nationals have wild camped without permission."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Street crime and scamming"]},{"k":"p","s":["Foreign nationals are at particular risk of street robbery in Kinshasa, Lubumbashi and other urban centres, especially near hotels and supermarkets in the centre of town. Organised gangs lure people into traps through techniques including the use of children, promising cut-price gold and diamonds, or posing as police or security personnel. Robberies by gangs of street children are common and can be aggressive."]},{"k":"p","s":["In Kinshasa, robberies can be carried out by people posing as taxi drivers or taxi passengers, and are often accompanied by a threat of violence."]},{"k":"p","s":["In North and South Kivu, reports of criminal activity have increased, particularly those targeting the international community. There have been many reports of robberies and banditry in Goma, especially after dark."]},{"k":"p","s":["To reduce your personal risk:"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid walking in the streets alone at any time, especially at night"]},{"k":"li","s":["do not display valuables and cash"]},{"k":"li","s":["use a hotel safe if possible and keep copies of documents, including your passport, separately"]},{"k":"li","s":["use transport organised by a hotel or tour operator"]},{"k":"li","s":["if you must take a taxi, use a privately booked one and do not hail taxis in the street"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Criminal kidnap"]},{"k":"p","s":["Kidnapping is a risk in parts of Kinshasa, including the Limete area."]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been several recent incidents where criminals pretending to be policemen or security personnel have captured foreign nationals and then demanded payment for their release."]},{"k":"p","s":["Criminals may also carry out ‘express kidnaps’, where they capture victims, take them to ATMs to withdraw money, and then release them."]},{"k":"p","s":["Foreign nationals can be perceived as being wealthier than locals and may be at particular risk."]},{"k":"p","s":["To reduce risk:"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid walking in the streets alone at any time, especially at night"]},{"k":"li","s":["Do not display valuables and cash"]},{"k":"li","s":["If you must use a taxi, use a privately booked one"]},{"k":"li","s":["do not hail taxis in the street."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Vehicle crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["Carjackings are rare, but lock vehicle doors and keep windows closed when driving. Watch out for armed gangs who may target your car or try to enter it to rob you. Do not drive off the main roads or park in unsupervised areas."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Justice process"]},{"k":"p","s":["The DRC authorities rarely meet their international obligations to notify embassies when foreign nationals have been detained. Even if requested, adequate consular access is not always granted. Keep in close touch with family or friends and ask them to notify the ",["British Embassy in Kinshasa","https://www.gov.uk/world/organisations/british-embassy-kinshasa"]," immediately if you are arrested in DRC."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Using cameras in secure areas"]},{"k":"p","s":["Taking photographs of some government and military buildings is illegal, particularly borders or military installations. You risk being arrested and detained. Journalists should not conduct interviews or film without the necessary local permits."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Same-sex sexual activity is not illegal in DRC but is frowned upon by many. There is no legal recognition of same-sex couples or same-sex marriage, and there are no specific anti-discrimination laws protecting LBGT+ people. Members of the LGBT+ community are known to be harassed. Individuals may be charged under DRC’s Penal Code for ‘crimes against family life’."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Adopting children from DRC"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against adopting from DRC. The UK does not recognise adoptions made in DRC as DRC is not a signatory to the Hague Convention on Protection of Children and Co-operation in Respect of Intercountry Adoption."]},{"k":"p","s":["The DRC government has not issued exit permits for children adopted by foreign nationals in DRC since 2013 and many are still unable to leave the country. It is illegal for same-sex or trans-sexual couples to adopt Congolese children."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Camouflage clothing"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you wear any military-style clothing you could be misidentified as military personnel and be vulnerable to attack or detention."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Money"]},{"k":"p","s":["Credit cards are only accepted in a limited number of places in Kinshasa and other cities. US dollars are widely used alongside the local currency and a number of ATMs dispense US dollars in Kinshasa. Notes should be in good condition and issued after 2001. Elsewhere in DRC, cash is needed for transactions."]},{"k":"p","s":["Make sure you have access to money, or have arrangements in place for it to be sent to you in an emergency, before leaving the UK."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Democratic Republic of Congo, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],". You’ll need a ",["1968 International Driving Permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," to drive in DRC. You will not be able to buy an IDP outside the UK, so get one before you travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["Car hire is possible in Kinshasa although self-drive options are limited. Most car hire companies will only let you hire a car with a driver."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road conditions"]},{"k":"p","s":["Driving standards are well below those in the UK and accidents are very common. Roads in the DRC are poorly maintained, largely unpaved and often not drivable with a standard vehicle, especially during the rainy season from September to May. Inside the cities, including Kinshasa, main roads are often paved but they can be narrow with cars parked on either side. Consider the technical capability of your vehicle and be confident in your ability to operate it. Travel after dark brings increased risk."]},{"k":"p","s":["Public buses and taxis are often not well-maintained, and there is a risk of assault."]},{"k":"p","s":["Security forces operate roadblocks, particularly after dark. If you are asked to produce documents for inspection at a checkpoint, stay inside your vehicle and show them through closed windows."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Air travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["The ",["UK Air Safety List (ASL)","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/uk-air-safety-list#democratic-republic-of-congo-drc"]," lists all known airlines in DRC that do not meet international safety standards and are banned from operating commercial air services to, from, and within the UK. Check the UK Air Safety List when considering which airlines to fly with. The list is maintained by the Department for Transport, based on advice from the ",["UK Civil Aviation Authority","https://www.caa.co.uk/Commercial-Industry/Airlines/Licensing/Requirements-and-guidance/Third-Country-Operator-Certificates"],". FCDO advises against all travel by air into and out of Goma airport. ",["See why FCDO advises against travel","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/democratic-republic-of-the-congo/regional-risks"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Rail travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["The railways are in a poor state and you should be aware of the increased risk of travel by train. A refurbished route opened between Kinshasa and Matadi in 2015, although services are infrequent and unreliable."]},{"k":"hs","s":["River travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["The ferry service between Kinshasa and Brazzaville stops running in the late afternoon and there is no service on Sundays."]},{"k":"p","s":["Boats and ferries on the rivers and lakes are poorly maintained and often overloaded. As a result of the low safety standards, high river traffic levels, strong currents, shifting sandbanks and poor maintenance there have been many accidents."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to ",["prepare for and respond to extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Flooding"]},{"k":"p","s":["During the wet season (approximately September to May), heavy rainfall often causes severe flooding in parts of DRC. Check for news of flooding before travelling."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Earthquakes"]},{"k":"p","s":["Earthquakes are a risk in DRC, but they are infrequent. The US Federal Emergency Management Agency website has advice about ",["what to do before, during and after an earthquake","https://www.ready.gov/earthquakes"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Volcanic eruptions"]},{"k":"p","s":["Mount Nyiragongo volcano, close to the city of Goma and near the border with Rwanda, erupted in 2002 and 2021, resulting in loss of lives and damage to infrastructure in and around Goma. Further volcanic activity is possible at any time."]},{"k":"h","s":["Regional risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["This section has safety advice for regions of the Democratic Republic of Congo. It only covers regions where the Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) has specific advice."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should also read ",["FCDO’s overall travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/democratic-republic-of-the-congo"]," and ",["safety and security advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/democratic-republic-of-the-congo/safety-and-security"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Eastern DRC"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to the provinces of:"]},{"k":"li","s":["North Kivu, including the city of Goma"]},{"k":"li","s":["South Kivu, including the city of Bukavu"]},{"k":"li","s":["Haut-Uélé and Ituri, including the entire DRC-South Sudan border"]},{"k":"li","s":["Maniema"]},{"k":"li","s":["Tanganyika"]},{"k":"li","s":["Haut Lomami"]},{"k":"p","s":["The security situation in eastern DRC remains unstable. Armed groups are active and intercommunal violence can affect the political, security and humanitarian situation. Large numbers of civilians remain displaced as a result of the conflict. Acts of violence, including killing, rape and looting continue against civilians."]},{"k":"p","s":["There are continued reports of towns in eastern DRC being attacked by or falling under temporary control of armed groups. There are continued reports of attacks and kidnappings, including against staff from NGOs and international organisations. Be prepared to leave at short notice via available routes. If you are in an area against FCDO advice, you should be vigilant at all times and keep your security situation under constant review."]},{"k":"p","s":["Foreign nationals travelling in eastern DRC have been left vulnerable, without escorted transport. The risk of kidnap or injury remains high."]},{"k":"p","s":["While British government staff do visit areas of eastern DRC, the British Embassy’s ability to offer support is severely limited."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Peacekeeping forces"]},{"k":"p","s":["A United Nations peacekeeping presence is deployed in eastern DRC. The Congolese army is carrying out operations against foreign and domestic armed groups operating in North and South Kivu and Ituri provinces. Foreign, regional forces are also present in eastern DRC."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Goma and Bukavu"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to Goma in North Kivu and Bukavu in South Kivu in eastern DRC. The situation in eastern DRC is unpredictable, and there is a high risk of ongoing instability, particularly in Goma and Bukavu."]},{"k":"p","s":["The armed group M23 and Rwanda Defence Forces (RDF) have captured and taken control of Goma. Fighting in Goma and the surrounding areas has intensified. Goma airport is currently not operational and is under the control of RDF and M23."]},{"k":"p","s":["On 16 February, RDF and M23 forces captured and took control of Bukavu, the main city in South Kivu. This follows advances south from Goma. On Friday 14 February, M23 and RDF forces captured Kavuma airport, approximately 30km north of the city. Commercial flights are not operating from the airport."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Ruzizi border crossing in Bukavu is under RDF and M23 control and appears open, but the situation remain highly unpredictable and may change at short notice."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is an ongoing risk of protests in the east, particularly in Goma, North Kivu province. These could be directed at foreign nationals."]},{"k":"p","s":["A ‘state of siege’ is in place in the provinces of Ituri and North Kivu. Military administrations with extended security powers have replaced the civilian administrations. On 20 February 2024, the Governor of North Kivu banned vehicles from driving in the province with tinted windows (this includes the city of Goma)."]},{"k":"p","s":["The situation in Goma, Bukavu, and the surrounding areas remains uncertain, unstable and can change quickly. British nationals should be prepared to leave at short notice and have adequate supplies of food, water, medicine etc in case of the need to lock down."]},{"k":"h","s":["Tshopo Province"]},{"k":"p","s":["The security situation in and around Bangoka International Airport, Kisangani, remains unpredictable following recent drone attacks against DRC military assets at the airport. These attacks have been claimed by the M23. Commercial flights are operating as usual, but availability can change at short notice. These border crossings are controlled by RDF and M23."]},{"k":"h","s":["Border crossings with Rwanda"]},{"k":"p","s":["The border crossings between Rwanda and the DRC at Gisenyi/Goma and Cyangugu/Bukavu may close at short notice. These border crossings are controlled by RDF and M23."]},{"k":"p","s":["Following the Ebola outbreak, transit from the Democratic Republic of the Congo through Rwanda is only permitted in exceptional circumstances related to humanitarian missions and essential travel, and is subject to health risk assessment, destination-country, transport operator, and public health requirements, and approval by the Rwandan authorities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Territory in Mai-Ndombe Province"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to the Kwamouth territory of Mai-Ndombe Province. This is between, and including, the towns of Kwamouth, Bandundu and the southern border of Mai-Ndombe Province."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is ongoing intercommunal violence between ethnic groups over land. The government has deployed a military force to the area. We are not aware of any direct threat against the international community or British nationals. Be aware of the increased violence and potential threat."]},{"k":"h","s":["Areas in Kinshasa Province"]},{"k":"p","s":["Due to the risk of violent crime, FCDO advises against all but essential travel in the districts of:"]},{"k":"li","s":["N’djili and Kimbanseke in Kinshasa city, south of the main access road to N’djili airport, in Nsele commune"]},{"k":"li","s":["Kasa Vubu in Kinshasa City, bordered by the N1 Triumphal Road (Stadium), Barumbu District, Lingwala District and the south of the botanical garden"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the N1 road in Kinshasa Province, between and including Menkao to the west, Kenge to the east, the border of Mai-Ndombe province to the north, and 10km to the south. There has been fighting between local militia and Congolese Armed Forces on this section of the N1 road. There are checkpoints on the road and reports of access being blocked. The authorities advise to travel during daylight hours."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is no general emergency medical number in the Democratic Republic of the Congo (DRC). If you have a medical emergency which requires an ambulance, contact a hospital to make this request."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for DRC","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/63/democratic-republic-of-the-congo#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in DRC","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/63/democratic-republic-of-the-congo"]," including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["ebola"]},{"k":"li","s":["malaria"]},{"k":"li","s":["cholera"]},{"k":"li","s":["yellow fever"]},{"k":"li","s":["mpox"]},{"k":"p","s":["Altitude sickness is a risk in parts of DRC. Read more about ",["altitude sickness on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/26/altitude-illness"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Ebola"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are frequent outbreaks of serious infectious diseases in DRC. On 17 May, the World Health Organization (WHO) declared the Ebola (Bundibugyo virus disease) outbreak in DRC a ",["Public Health Emergency of International Concern","https://www.who.int/news/item/17-05-2026-epidemic-of-ebola-disease-in-the-democratic-republic-of-the-congo-and-uganda-determined-a-public-health-emergency-of-international-concern"],". The outbreak is active, evolving and geographically widespread."]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel to DRC read ",["Ebola Disease in DRC","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/news/909/ebola-disease-in-drc-and-uganda"]," and ",["general information on Ebola and similar diseases","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/68/viral-haemorrhagic-fever"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Some countries have additional health screening requirements or entry restrictions for travellers arriving from, or who have recently visited the DRC. ",["Check entry requirements","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/"]," for any destination or transit country before travelling."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Health Security Agency has ",["Ebola information for humanitarian or healthcare workers","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/ebola-virus-disease-information-for-workers-in-at-risk-countries"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ebola spreads through direct contact with the blood, body fluids or tissues of an infected person, or through contact with contaminated materials. To reduce your risk:"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid contact with anyone who is unwell or showing symptoms of Ebola"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid contact with blood, body fluids and human remains"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid handling bushmeat or contact with bats and other wild animals"]},{"k":"li","s":["wash your hands regularly and follow local public health advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you develop symptoms such as fever, severe headache, muscle pain, diarrhoea, vomiting or unexplained bleeding while in DRC, seek medical advice immediately and avoid contact with others. Symptoms can develop up to 21 days after exposure."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in DRC"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a ",["list of medical providers in DRC","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/medical-practitioners"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"p","s":["Medical care is extremely limited. The Centre Prive d’Urgence (CPU) clinic in Kinshasa is able to cope with basic health problems and to stabilise a patient after most serious accidents. Outside Kinshasa, Western-standard medical facilities are almost non-existent. Medical evacuation to South Africa (or elsewhere) could be necessary. Make sure you have adequate travel health insurance and accessible funds to cover the cost of any medical treatment abroad and repatriation."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you take medication regularly, make sure you bring enough for your time in the DRC, and that it is in properly marked packaging."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in DRC"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is no general emergency medical number in Kinshasa or elsewhere in the Democratic Republic of the Congo (DRC)."]},{"k":"p","s":["Some major cities have emergency services, but their level of assistance is limited."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you have a medical emergency which requires an ambulance, contact a hospital to make this request. If you are in Kinshasa, you can contact the fire service on 118, and the police on 112."]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Congo%2C%20Democratic%20Republic"],", ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Congo%2C%20Democratic%20Republic"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=Congo%2C%20Democratic%20Republic"]]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in DRC","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/bereavement-information-pack-democratic-republic-of-congo"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested or imprisoned in DRC","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/democratic-republic-of-congo-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/democratic-republic-of-the-congo/british-embassy-kinshasa"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/democratic-republic-of-the-congo/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]}],"chars":30829,"change":"New information and guidance about the ongoing Ebola outbreak in DRC (see 'Warnings and insurance' and 'Health' pages)."},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/ecuador":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-20T16:50Z","sha":"6c957604d97b7fa20e974d53a71d464c4ae0c08f13f1a4a42586e757d326d337","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/ecuador","bytes":124810,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Ecuador travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-03-15T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-11-20T13:14:04+00:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["Your travel insurance could be invalidated if you travel against advice from the Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO)."]},{"k":"h","s":["Areas where FCDO advises against all but essential travel"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Coastal Region"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the Coastal Region provinces of:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Esmeraldas"]},{"k":"li","s":["Manabí"]},{"k":"li","s":["Santa Elena"]},{"k":"li","s":["Guayas"]},{"k":"li","s":["El Oro"]},{"k":"li","s":["Los Ríos"]},{"k":"li","s":["Santo Domingo de los Tsáchilas"]},{"k":"p","s":["This does not apply to airside transit within Guayaquil Airport in Guayas province."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Within 20km of the Ecuador-Colombia border"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to areas within 20km of the Ecuador-Colombia border, except for these areas in Carchi province:"]},{"k":"li","s":["El Ángel Ecological Reserve"]},{"k":"li","s":["Rumichaca border crossing"]},{"k":"li","s":["the town of Tulcán"]},{"k":"li","s":["the Pan-American Highway"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["why FCDO advises against travel","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/ecuador/regional-risks"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Flooding on Santa Cruz Island, Galapagos"]},{"k":"p","s":["Heavy rains have caused flooding on Santa Cruz Island, prompting ",["Gobierno Galapagos","https://x.com/CGGalapagos"]," to declare an emergency on 31 October. Road closures, power outages, and disruptions to travel to Baltra Airport have been reported."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should follow the instructions of the local authorities, avoid flooded areas, and confirm travel arrangements with airlines or tour operators."]},{"k":"p","s":["Local authorities encourage tourists on Santa Cruz Island to complete the ",["form","https://form.jotform.com/230545460190652"]," (available only in Spanish) indicating whether they need urgent assistance and what their travel plans are."]},{"k":"h","s":["State of Emergency"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Ecuadorean government has extended the state of emergency for a further 30 days, effective from 11 November, for security reasons in the following 8 provinces:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Guayas"]},{"k":"li","s":["Manabí"]},{"k":"li","s":["Santa Elena"]},{"k":"li","s":["Los Ríos"]},{"k":"li","s":["El Oro"]},{"k":"li","s":["Pichincha"]},{"k":"li","s":["Esmeraldas"]},{"k":"li","s":["Santo Domingo de los Tsáchilas"]},{"k":"p","s":["The state of emergency includes the following cantons:"]},{"k":"li","s":["La Maná (Cotopaxi province)"]},{"k":"li","s":["Las Naves (Bolívar province)"]},{"k":"li","s":["Camilo Ponce Enriquez (Azuay province)"]},{"k":"p","s":["The State of Emergency will mean greater police and military presence on the streets. Follow the advice of local authorities and monitor local media."]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/ecuador/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of Ecuador’s current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Ecuador set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Ecuadorean Embassy in the UK","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/foreign-embassies-in-the-uk"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Documents required to enter via land or river border"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you wish to enter Ecuador via a land or river border from Peru or Colombia, you must present a criminal record certificate from the country where you lived for the last 5 years. The certificate must be legalised with the Hague Apostille and translated into Spanish if issued in another language. This mandatory requirement was announced on 11 January 2024 for implementation with immediate effect."]},{"k":"p","s":["Alternatively, if you do not have a legalised criminal record certificate, you can ask the Ecuadorean immigration authorities at the border to carry out a check on their ’SIMIEC’ Ecuadorean Immigration System (which flags any travel prohibitions or INTERPOL alerts). The following people are exempt from the presentation of the criminal record certificate:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Holders of a valid Ecuadorean visa"]},{"k":"li","s":["Holders of diplomatic passports"]},{"k":"li","s":["Children and adolescents under 18"]},{"k":"li","s":["Victims of human trafficking or those seeking international protection under the Ecuadorean Human Mobility Law."]},{"k":"p","s":["There are no restrictions in place for anyone flying into Ecuador."]},{"k":"p","s":["To obtain a UK Police Criminal Record Certificate, ",["check the ACRO website","https://www.acro.police.uk/s/acro-services/police-certificates"],". For information about legalising the document with the Hague apostille check the ",["Foreign, Commonwealth and Development Office’s Legalisation Office website","https://www.gov.uk/get-document-legalised"]," site."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Ecuador, your passport must have an ‘expiry date’ at least 6 months after the date you arrive."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can visit Ecuador without a visa for up to 90 days in any 12-month period."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re already in Ecuador and want to stay longer than 90 days, you can pay to ",["extend your stay","https://servicio.migracion.gob.ec/tramite/3"]," (in Spanish) by an extra 90 days. You must apply for an extension before the first 90-day period ends or you could be fined."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you overstay your visa, you will get a fine when you leave. You will not be allowed to return to Ecuador unless you pay the fine before you leave the country."]},{"k":"p","s":["For immigration information, see ",["Ecuador Migration","https://www.migracion.gob.ec/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["To stay longer, to work or study, for business travel or for other reasons, you must meet the Ecuadorean government’s entry ",["requirements","https://www.cancilleria.gob.ec/2020/06/15/visas-en-el-ecuador/"]," (in Spanish)."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Applying for a visa"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ecuador’s Ministry of Foreign Affairs and Human Mobility (MFAHM) has an ",["e-visa application process","https://serviciosdigitales.cancilleria.gob.ec/authentication"]," (in Spanish). Find the ",["relevant MFAHM district zone offices","https://www.cancilleria.gob.ec/2020/07/30/direccioneszonales/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["For general guidance contact ssmc@cancilleria.gob.ec or call (02) 299 3200 extension 23064."]},{"k":"h","s":["Checks at border control"]},{"k":"p","s":["All travellers entering Ecuador must register their entry and exit in the national immigration database. This is a mandatory requirement under Ecuadorean immigration regulations. At border control, you may be asked to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["provide your reason for travel"]},{"k":"li","s":["show proof of a return or onward journey"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Peru and Colombia land border crossings"]},{"k":"p","s":["On the northern border with Colombia, the Rumichaca checkpoint is open. On the southern border with Peru, the Huaquillas, Macará, Zapotillo, and Lalamor checkpoints are open to international travellers."]},{"k":"p","s":["Other checkpoints remain closed until further notice."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are entering Ecuador by land from Peru or Colombia, it is essential to use an official immigration checkpoint to receive the required passport entry stamp indicating your arrival date. Some buses may bypass immigration checkpoints, which can result in travellers not receiving the necessary stamp. This can lead to serious immigration issues."]},{"k":"p","s":["Evading immigration control filters, regardless of the reason, is considered a serious offence. According to official sources:"]},{"k":"li","s":["it will result in denied entry (‘inadmisión’) on future entry attempts"]},{"k":"li","s":["immigration fines are generally not applicable for this type of violation (but they apply for overstaying cases)"]},{"k":"li","s":["for official enquiries or direct assistance, contact an ",["immigration office","https://servicio.migracion.gob.ec/"]," (in Spanish) as soon as possible"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Galapagos Islands"]},{"k":"p","s":["Tourists can stay in the Galapagos Islands for up to 60 days. To enter Galapagos, you must have:"]},{"k":"li","s":["evidence of a hotel booking or an invitation letter from your host"]},{"k":"li","s":["evidence of a return flight to the Ecuadorean mainland"]},{"k":"li","s":[["purchase a transit control card","https://siiws.gobiernogalapagos.gob.ec/siicgg_web/"]," at your departure airport before checking in for your flight – you must also keep a copy"]},{"k":"li","s":["travel health insurance, which is mandatory for foreign tourists"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are travelling to or from Galapagos Islands via Guayaquil airport you should check with the airline before booking to ensure you will remain airside at Guayaquil airport. FCDO advises against all but essential travel to Guayaquil, except for airside transit through the airport."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check the ",["Ministry of Tourism’s accredited tourism service providers","https://www.observatoriogalapagos.gob.ec/directorio-servicios-regularizados-galapagos"]," (in Spanish), which includes information on accommodation, transport, tour operators and restaurants."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travelling with children"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Leaving Ecuador"]},{"k":"p","s":["British children, including British - Ecuadorean dual nationals, aged 17 and under must have a notarised consent letter (in Spanish) to leave Ecuador if they are:"]},{"k":"li","s":["travelling alone or with one parent or legal guardian"]},{"k":"li","s":["resident in Ecuador or have been in Ecuador for over 90 days, even if they are travelling on a British passport"]},{"k":"p","s":["If they are tourists (not resident in Ecuador) British children (or British-Ecuadorean dual nationals) do not need a notarised consent letter (Art.137 Human Mobility Organic Law’ 2017)."]},{"k":"p","s":["If one parent is deceased, the other parent must submit the death certificate to an Ecuadorean public notary to get an indefinite notarial permit to travel with the child."]},{"k":"p","s":["In more complex situations, such as legal disputes, a child will need judicial written permission (‘Autorización de Viaje Judicial’) issued by an Ecuadorian judge (‘Juzgado de la Niñez y Adolescencia’)."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Entering Ecuador"]},{"k":"p","s":["Children entering Ecuador with someone other than a parent or legal guardian do not need a consent letter."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["For full details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Ecuador guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/70/ecuador#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["From 29 July, every adult passenger or family group travelling to or from Ecuador carrying taxable goods or cash equal to or higher than 10,000 US dollars must:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["register online","https://www.aduana.gob.ec/servicio-al-ciudadano/formulario-de-registro-aduanero/login/"]]},{"k":"li","s":["complete the form, and present the digital version (QR code) to customs on arrival/departure (airports, land borders, ports)"]},{"k":"p","s":["This form must be completed at least three days before travelling. Failure to declare goods can lead to fines, confiscation of goods or criminal charges."]},{"k":"h","s":["Taking money out of Ecuador"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must declare cash you’re carrying when you leave Ecuador. You will have to pay tax on amounts over 1,350 US dollars."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"p","s":["You should also read ",["FCDO’s overall travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/ecuador/warnings-and-insurance"]," and ",["regional risks advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/ecuador/regional-risks"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Ecuador"]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorist attacks in Ecuador cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"h","s":["Political situation"]},{"k":"p","s":["Due to the current State of Emergency, expect heightened police and military presence nationwide without previous notice, and potential travel disruptions due to extra security checks."]},{"k":"p","s":["Exercise caution around large gatherings. Street demonstrations, protests and strikes are common and can occur without warning. While most are peaceful, they can turn violent. You should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["stay alert and monitor local media"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid large gatherings"]},{"k":"li","s":["follow updates from the ",["ECU 911 emergency services","https://twitter.com/ecu911_"]]},{"k":"li","s":["be wary of unverified information"]},{"k":"li","s":["allow extra time to reach your destination"]},{"k":"li","s":[["check road conditions","https://www.ecu911.gob.ec/consulta-de-vias/"]," (in Spanish) on the Ecuadorean government website"]},{"k":"p","s":["Even peaceful protests can lead to travel disruption."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting yourself and your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["Mugging and pickpocketing are common, take care in Quito’s old town and at transport hubs. The methods criminals use include:"]},{"k":"li","s":["distraction techniques (for example, requests for assistance, squirting liquids on to you, staged fights and pushing or shoving)"]},{"k":"li","s":["bag snatching at knife or gunpoint by a passenger on a motorbike"]},{"k":"p","s":["To reduce your risk:"]},{"k":"li","s":["stay alert in public places"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid walking alone in quiet areas or at night"]},{"k":"li","s":["do not wear expensive jewellery in public"]},{"k":"li","s":["carry only the money you need for the day"]},{"k":"li","s":["take care of your credit cards"]},{"k":"li","s":["watch your bags on public transport and wear your rucksack on the front of your body"]},{"k":"li","s":["carry a colour copy of your passport, including the visa entry stamp page – keep the original safe"]},{"k":"li","s":["use a money belt or secure inside pocket to keep your passport, credit cards and money safe"]},{"k":"p","s":["For more information on general travel safety in Ecuador, ",["check the Ministry of Tourism website","https://ecuador.travel/en/travel-safe/"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Violent crime and armed robbery"]},{"k":"p","s":["On 14 October 2025, a car bomb exploded near the Mall del Sol shopping centre and the Sheraton Hotel in northern Guayaquil, resulting in multiple injuries and at least one fatality. Secondary explosions were reported on 15 October 2025 on a road connecting the provinces of Guayas and El Oro."]},{"k":"p","s":["Armed robbery is a risk throughout Ecuador. Crimes with the threat of violence, such as gunpoint robbery and home invasion, can happen throughout Ecuador."]},{"k":"p","s":["Take particular care in Esmeraldas, Guayas and Manabi provinces (currently the FCDO advises against all but essential travel to those provinces) and get local advice on where to visit. Armed thieves have stopped vehicles and threatened passengers."]},{"k":"p","s":["Most violent crime is gang-related, but tourists can be affected. The murder rate in Guayaquil is very high, but is mainly gang-related. Be particularly cautious in Guayaquil city centre, southern parts of the city and port areas."]},{"k":"p","s":["Since March 2023, organised crime gangs have caused small explosions and made false bomb threats in Quito and Guayaquil. If you’re near an incident, follow the instructions of police and local authorities."]},{"k":"p","s":["Get local advice about the area you’re visiting and travel in a group when possible."]},{"k":"hs","s":["ATM and bank customer robbery"]},{"k":"p","s":["Take care when withdrawing money from a bank or ATM. Where possible use ATMs inside banks or shopping centres, and avoid withdrawing money after dark. There have been violent robberies outside banks. The Ecuadorean national police offers a free escort service if you are withdrawing or depositing large quantities of cash. To request this service, call 911. Only take out as much money as you need."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Transport robbery"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a risk of robbery and pickpocketing on interstate transport and at bus stations, including on routes commonly used by tourists. To reduce your risk:"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid road travel after dark"]},{"k":"li","s":["keep valuables safe in a money belt or inside pocket"]},{"k":"li","s":["do not store bags in overhead luggage spaces or under your seat"]},{"k":"p","s":["Criminals can pose as uniformed bus inspectors in some Quito bus stations. They might insist you place your luggage overhead so an accomplice can steal it later. You do not have to place belongings overhead."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are robbed, do not resist attackers or do anything that puts you at greater risk. Report the incident to the police as soon as possible."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Sexual assault"]},{"k":"p","s":["Serious sexual assaults and attacks against foreign women have happened in Ecuador, particularly in the tourist beach town of Montañita in Santa Elena Province. Check reviews of your accommodation to make sure it is reputable and secure, even if you’re travelling in a group. Avoid travel after dark and be alert to the use of date rape and other drugs in drinks. If you feel unwell, seek urgent help from the police or nearest health centre. Call 911 for the emergency services."]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["information for victims of rape and sexual assault in Ecuador","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/ecuador-information-for-victims-of-rape-and-sexual-assault"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can ",["report gender-based violence","https://www.fiscalia.gob.ec/denuncia-en-linea-violencia-contra-la-mujer/"]," to the Prosecutor Office (‘Fiscalía’) online."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Criminal kidnap"]},{"k":"p","s":["Kidnapping rates have risen in Ecuador. Express kidnappings – short term opportunistic abductions, aimed at extracting cash from the victim – are common throughout Ecuador. Victims can be targeted or selected at random. They are held while criminals withdraw money from their bank accounts using their cash cards. Many cases involve victims who have hailed taxis (registered or illegal) from the street. In some cases, victims are subdued with scopolamine (causing amnesia). Be aware of your surroundings and always let someone you trust know your whereabouts, especially after dark."]},{"k":"p","s":["Business people and visitors perceived to be wealthy may be targeted by kidnappers in search of pay-outs. Be discreet about discussing your financial or business affairs in places where you may be overheard by others, and when arranging meetings use a secure location."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are a victim of kidnapping, follow the kidnapper’s instructions."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Drug-assisted robbery"]},{"k":"p","s":["Criminals may use drugs to incapacitate victims, leaving them vulnerable to robbery, assault and other crimes. Substances such as scopolamine can cause confusion, compliance, memory loss and an inability to resist or seek help, even while victims remain conscious and appear functional."]},{"k":"p","s":["These substances may be administered in food or drinks and, in some reported cases, through direct physical contact without a victim’s knowledge. Even brief interactions can impair awareness and judgement. Be cautious of strangers offering food, drinks, cigarettes, chewing gum, leaflets, perfume samples or other items. Avoid accepting anything from people you do not know well."]},{"k":"p","s":["British nationals have reported suspected drug-assisted robberies in private rented accommodation. Take particular care when meeting with people you only know through online interactions, inviting unfamiliar individuals into your accommodation, or visiting theirs. Where possible, meet in public, share your plans with someone you trust, and avoid being alone with people you do not know well."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Methanol poisoning"]},{"k":"p","s":["There has been an increase in cases of serious illness caused by alcoholic drinks containing methanol in popular travel destinations around the world."]},{"k":"p","s":["Even small amounts of methanol can kill. It is not possible to identify methanol in alcoholic drinks by taste or smell. See ",["Travel Aware Spiking and methanol poisoning","https://travelaware.campaign.gov.uk/spiking-and-methanol-poisoning/"]," for information about how to reduce the risks."]},{"k":"p","s":["Seek urgent medical attention if you or someone you are travelling with show the ",["signs of methanol poisoning","https://travelaware.campaign.gov.uk/spiking-and-methanol-poisoning/"]," after drinking."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["By law you must carry ID. Always carry a printed copy of your passport, including the pages with your photograph and Ecuadorean entry stamp."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs and prison sentences"]},{"k":"p","s":["The penalties for drug trafficking or drug use are harsh, and prison conditions are very basic."]},{"k":"hs","s":["‘Spiritual cleansing’ hallucinogens"]},{"k":"p","s":["In Ecuador people use traditional hallucinogens such as Ayahuasca or San Pedro. These substances are marketed to tourists for ‘spiritual cleansing’ rituals. They often contain dimethyltryptamine (DMT), a strong hallucinogen that is illegal in the UK."]},{"k":"p","s":["There are many risks when taking these substances including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["serious illness and death"]},{"k":"li","s":["assault and robbery while intoxicated"]},{"k":"li","s":["lack of nearby medical help as these ceremonies often take place in remote locations"]},{"k":"p","s":["Consumption of traditional hallucinogens is unregulated."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Same-sex relations are legal in Ecuador. However, local attitudes towards the LGBT+ community can be conservative and there is still societal discrimination. People may be less tolerant of same-sex couples showing affection in public than they are in the UK. Showing affection may attract negative attention, especially in small towns. Transgender people in particular could face unwanted attention."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Money"]},{"k":"p","s":["US dollars and 5, 10, 25 and 50 centavos coins minted in Ecuador are the only legal currencies. Credit cards and travellers cheques are generally accepted in cities but not elsewhere in the country."]},{"k":"h","s":["Outdoor activities and adventure tourism"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Volunteer and adventure activities"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you join a volunteer or adventure expedition programme, make sure the UK organisation responsible for travel has an official agent in Ecuador able to handle an emergency. Be wary of unauthorised intermediaries (‘enganchadores’) trying to offer you cheap hotels or tour deals."]},{"k":"p","s":["British nationals have died while rafting, kayaking and on canopy walks and zip-lines. Make sure you’re fit enough for these activities and others such as bungee jumping and quad biking. For water adventure sports, make sure the weather conditions and river currents are safe."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["only use reputable tour operators with a specific licence to provide these services"]},{"k":"li","s":["be aware equipment may not meet UK safety and insurance standards"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the company uses the most up-to-date equipment and safety features"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the company is properly insured"]},{"k":"li","s":["make sure your insurance covers all your activities"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Swimming safety"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a risk of drowning caused by strong, rapidly changing ocean currents. Beaches do not always have swimming safety warning flags. Seek local advice on tidal activity."]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["water safety on holiday","https://www.rlss.org.uk/safety-on-holiday"]," from the Royal Life Saving Society."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Hiking and mountaineering"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re hiking or mountaineering in Ecuador, prepare for high altitude and unpredictable climates. Hire an accredited guide or tour operator for these activities."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["climb at a moderate rate so your body can adjust"]},{"k":"li","s":["stay well hydrated"]},{"k":"li","s":["keep to established paths or use an experienced guide"]},{"k":"li","s":["make sure someone knows where you’re going and when you plan to return"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid walking alone"]},{"k":"p","s":["Lightning has killed tourists climbing mountains. Watch the weather and reconsider your plans if conditions look bad. Turn off any electronic devices if you encounter a thunderstorm; this prevents electrical surges, stops devices from acting as lightning rods, and protects you from close-range strikes."]},{"k":"p","s":["For more information on climbing or mountaineering, see the ",["Ministry of Environment","https://www.ambiente.gob.ec/"],", [Ecuador Tourism] (https://www.turismo.gob.ec/), and ",["Chimborazo Local Government","https://twitter.com/goberchimborazo"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["For accredited guides, check ",["the Ecuadorean Mountaineering Accredited Guides Association","https://aseguim.org/"]," (in Spanish)."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Climbing mountains with glaciers"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to do high mountaineering or climb a glaciated mountain without an official accredited guide."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Pichincha volcano"]},{"k":"p","s":["Tourists take day trips to Pichincha volcano on the cable car (‘teleférico’) from Quito. Cruz Loma arrival station is at 4.050 metres above sea level. There have been accidents on the route to one of the peaks, Rucu Pichincha, including deaths from hypothermia. You should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["be aware of the risk of altitude sickness"]},{"k":"li","s":["take warm, waterproof clothing and high-factor sunblock"]},{"k":"li","s":["go with an accredited specialised guide who knows the route"]},{"k":"li","s":["start early to reduce risks from unexpected heavy mist or storms"]},{"k":"li","s":["wear a helmet if climbing up the peak Rucu Pichincha"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Cayambe Volcano"]},{"k":"p","s":["There may be access restrictions for Cayambe volcano depending on the weather and glacier conditions. Comply with safety regulations."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Chimborazo Reserve"]},{"k":"p","s":["To visit Chimborazo National Reserve, you must email chimborazo@ambiente.gob.ec at least 5 days in advance to register on the Biodiversity Information System (‘Sistema de Información de Biodiversidad’). The Chimborazo National Reserve is only open for tour operators and accredited mountaineering clubs after an avalanche killed 3 climbers in 2021."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Cotopaxi National Park"]},{"k":"p","s":["High mountaineering in Cotopaxi National Park is restricted. Since November 2023, tour operators, mountaineering clubs and individual visitors can go high mountaineering in Cotopaxi National Park. However, they must comply with mandatory national park rules and safety regulations."]},{"k":"p","s":["For information, see the ",["Ecuadorean Ministry of Environment","https://twitter.com/ambiente_ec"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re visiting Cotopaxi National Park, carry:"]},{"k":"li","s":["sunglasses and a hat"]},{"k":"li","s":["clothing that covers your skin"]},{"k":"li","s":["enough water and food"]},{"k":"li","s":["an emergency kit"]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Ecuador, see information on ",["driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can use a UK photocard driving licence to drive in Ecuador for the first 6 months after you arrive. If you still have a paper UK driving licence, you may need to ",["update it to a photocard licence","https://www.gov.uk/exchange-paper-driving-licence"]," or get the ",["correct version of the international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," as well. After 6 months, you need to take an Ecuadorean driving test to get an Ecuadorean driving licence or carry out the driving licence exchange process."]},{"k":"p","s":["Always carry your passport, driving licence and vehicle registration with you in the vehicle."]},{"k":"p","s":["Hire car companies often have stricter requirements for their customers, such as 6 months of driving experience, a minimum age of 18 years old and holding an IDP."]},{"k":"p","s":["Some cities do not allow vehicles with Ecuadorean plates to drive on certain days or at peak times based on the last digits of their car’s registration plate. Check for restrictions before you drive. You could be fined if you do not follow the rules."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Driving conditions"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ecuador has one of the highest rates of road accidents in Latin America due to careless driving, speeding and badly maintained vehicles. There have been many deaths, including British nationals."]},{"k":"p","s":["In Ecuador:"]},{"k":"li","s":["road conditions vary"]},{"k":"li","s":["heavy rains and mudslides often cause roads to be closed or wash away"]},{"k":"li","s":["driving can be erratic – be prepared to stop unexpectedly"]},{"k":"li","s":["vehicles may move slowly, change lanes without indicating or jump red lights"]},{"k":"li","s":["many drivers are uninsured"]},{"k":"li","s":["drivers usually ignore zebra crossings"]},{"k":"p","s":["Always wear a seat belt. If you’re a passenger in a speeding vehicle, ask the driver to slow down."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taxis"]},{"k":"p","s":["Book taxis through your hotel or by calling a known radio-dispatched taxi service. Travel in a group if possible. Using unregistered taxis significantly increases your risk of becoming a victim of crime."]},{"k":"p","s":["While taxi service apps do exist and provide the driver’s details, the services themselves are unregulated in Ecuador."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re using a yellow registered taxi in Quito or Guayaquil, make sure it has:"]},{"k":"li","s":["a municipality registration number sticker on the windscreen and doors"]},{"k":"li","s":["orange licence plates or the new white plates with an orange strip on the top"]},{"k":"li","s":["video cameras inside"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are authorised taxi booths at Quito and Guayaquil international airports, and potentially at other domestic airports."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re using a yellow registered taxi in Quito, make sure the driver resets the meter. In Guayaquil and other cities, taxis use fixed prices rather than meters. In these places, or if you or your hotel calls a taxi in Quito, agree a price before you get in."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Sea travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["There has been piracy and armed robbery against ships in and around Ecuador’s waters. Sailors should stay alert and take appropriate precautions."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re travelling by sea, ",["read about the regional risks at sea","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/sea-river-and-piracy-safety"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been several serious accidents in the Galapagos Islands involving tour company boats and smaller vessels transporting people between islands. Some of the smaller boats do not follow safety measures, such as holding the right licence, respecting maximum capacity for passengers, checking their motor or fuel and providing enough life vests. Use reputable boat operators and ask about safety features before you book, even for short trips. Check they provide life vests and lifeboats (if appropriate) before boarding."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to prepare for and respond to ",["extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["2026–2027 El Niño"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Ecuadorean authorities have issued a red alert ahead of the forecast 2026-2027 El Niño weather event."]},{"k":"p","s":["El Niño is expected to generate unusually heavy rainfall, possible flooding and landslides, and higher temperatures, which may disrupt travel and other services."]},{"k":"p","s":["Extreme weather may affect your travel plans. Monitor local news and weather reports and follow the advice of local authorities. For official updates and forecasts, see the Ecuadorean government’s ",["El Niño information website","https://script.google.com/macros/s/AKfycbz6HA9kKLeksqm49YYPD7i3A40mMK6JwmoDc50vaiv4myVTk0lFYswqnE4IbJXmr9Lm/exec"]," (in Spanish)."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Landslides"]},{"k":"p","s":["Landslides are common in Ecuador and can have a serious impact on travel. Heavy rains can lead to landslides, which frequently lead to road closures. Check the weather forecast if you are travelling by road."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Earthquakes"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high risk of earthquakes across Ecuador. Earthquakes and aftershocks can cause landslides, which block roads."]},{"k":"p","s":["Familiarise yourself with safety procedures and any instructions in your hotel. If there is an earthquake, follow instructions from the authorities and keep essential belongings, such as your passport and money, with you."]},{"k":"p","s":["Get information (in Spanish) following an earthquake from the:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Ecuadorean National Geophysical Institute"]},{"k":"li","s":["Secretariat for Risk Management (Secretaría Nacional de Gestión de Riesgos) – check current alerts"]},{"k":"li","s":[["ECU 911 emergency services","https://www.ecu911.gob.ec/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["The US Federal Emergency Management Agency website has advice about ",["what to do before, during and after an earthquake","https://www.ready.gov/earthquakes"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can also ",["get earthquake alerts with an Android phone","https://support.google.com/android/answer/9319337?hl=en-GB"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Tsunamis"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high risk of tsunamis along the coast and in the Galapagos Islands. If there is a tsunami alert, sirens will sound in Esmeraldas, El Oro, Guayas, Santa Elena, Manabí and Galapagos. See ",["evacuation route maps","https://www.gestionderiesgos.gob.ec/biblioteca/"]," and follow the advice of the authorities."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Rainy season"]},{"k":"p","s":["The rainy season usually runs from October to May but can last until June."]},{"k":"p","s":["During heavy rainy seasons:"]},{"k":"li","s":["monitor local media"]},{"k":"li","s":["check your itinerary with your tour operator to avoid disruption"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid river crossings due to potential strong currents"]},{"k":"li","s":["take care in affected areas"]},{"k":"p","s":["The weather can change quickly. Check ",["weather forecasts","https://twitter.com/inamhi_ec"],". Get local advice on tides if you’re near the coast."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re climbing or mountaineering, get official advice from the authorities and tour operators."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Forest fires"]},{"k":"p","s":["Forest fires happen in many areas, especially in Pichincha, Loja, Azuay and Cotopaxi provinces , due to high temperatures, strong winds, dry conditions and arson. Call 911 if you see a fire."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Volcanic eruptions"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are many volcanoes in the highlands of Ecuador and the Galapagos Islands. Some are currently erupting, active or potentially active. Check the ",["current volcano alerts","https://www.igepn.edu.ec/red-de-observatorios-vulcanologicos-rovig"]," (in Spanish). Follow instructions issued by the local authorities."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ashfall from volcanoes can disrupt flights and close airports at short notice. Before going to the airport, check with your airline and on the airport website. Ash is also a health hazard, especially for travellers with respiratory problems."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high risk from mixed flows of water, mud, lava and debris (‘lahars’) around glaciated volcanoes, including Cotopaxi. These flows can be very destructive. The towns of Latacunga and Salcedo and low-lying areas in the valley to the east of Quito (Los Chillos and Rumiñahui) are particularly vulnerable."]},{"k":"p","s":["Access to the Reventador volcano (Napo province) is currently restricted."]},{"k":"h","s":["Regional risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["This section has safety advice for regions of Ecuador. It only covers regions where FCDO has specific advice."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should also read ",["FCDO’s overall travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/ecuador"]," and ",["safety and security advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/ecuador/safety-and-security"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Coastal regions"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the Coastal Region provinces of:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Esmeraldas"]},{"k":"li","s":["Manabi"]},{"k":"li","s":["Santa Elena"]},{"k":"li","s":["El Oro"]},{"k":"li","s":["Los Ríos"]},{"k":"li","s":["Santo Domingo de los Tsáchilas"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is due to a high level of gang-related violence linked to the presence of organised crime relating to the production and trafficking of illegal drugs."]},{"k":"p","s":["Tourists are not usually targeted. However, you could be a victim of violence due to mistaken identity or be caught up in a security incident involving others."]},{"k":"h","s":["Guayas"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the Coastal Region province of Guayas, except:"]},{"k":"li","s":["airside transit within Guayaquil Airport in Guayas province."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are travelling to or from the Galápagos Islands via Guayaquil airport you should check with the airline before booking to ensure you will remain airside at Guayaquil Airport."]},{"k":"p","s":["This is due to a high level of gang-related violence linked to the presence of organised crime relating to the production and trafficking of illegal drugs."]},{"k":"p","s":["There are instances of express kidnapping, where individuals have been kidnapped for a short period of time, and are often driven to an ATM to withdraw money and then abandoned."]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been several security incidents in and around the city of Guayaquil in Guayas province since 2023 including an increase in murders and small explosions. There have also been fatal armed attacks against the police and prosecutors."]},{"k":"p","s":["Tourists are not usually targeted. However, you could be a victim of violence due to mistaken identity or caught up in a security incident involving others."]},{"k":"h","s":["Within 20km of the Ecuador-Colombia border"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to areas within 20km of the Ecuador-Colombia border, except for these areas in Carchi province:"]},{"k":"li","s":["El Ángel Ecological Reserve"]},{"k":"li","s":["Rumichaca border crossing"]},{"k":"li","s":["the town of Tulcán"]},{"k":"li","s":["the Pan-American Highway"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is due to the presence of organised crime linked to the production and trafficking of drugs."]},{"k":"p","s":["The security situation can change quickly in areas outside the 20km border zone, including Esmeraldas, Carchi and Sucumbíos provinces. There are illegal armed groups and criminal gangs in these areas. If you are travelling to these areas, including Cuyabeno, the Napo River, and the El Ángel Ecological Reserve, where there are ecolodges, you should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["stay alert and take local advice"]},{"k":"li","s":["pay close attention to warnings issued by the Ecuadorean authorities"]},{"k":"li","s":["travel during daylight hours with a reputable, official guide"]},{"k":"li","s":["have an emergency plan and good communication systems in place"]},{"k":"li","s":["be aware some lodges are far from a major hospital"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you cross the northern border at Tulcán (Rumichaca official land border point), enter and exit the town on the Pan-American Highway."]},{"k":"p","s":["Lago Agrio (also known as Nueva Loja) the main town in Sucumbíos province, and San Lorenzo, in Esmeraldas province, are both within the 20km border zone where FCDO advises against all but essential travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Call 911 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can get emergency assistance and register medical issues using the ",["ECU 911 smartphone application","https://www.ecu911.gob.ec/app-ecu-911/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Ecuador","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/70/ecuador#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Ecuador","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/70/ecuador"],", including Oropouche virus."]},{"k":"p","s":["Altitude sickness is a risk in parts of Ecuador. Read more about ",["altitude sickness on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/26/altitude-illness"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ultraviolet radiation is a risk in Ecuador. Read more about ",["sun protection on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/23/sun-protection"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Drinking water"]},{"k":"p","s":["To avoid getting sick, drink boiled, filtered or bottled water and avoid ice in drinks."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pharmacies in Ecuador may accept some UK prescriptions. They will accept antimicrobial prescriptions up to 3 days old and narcotic or psychotropic prescriptions up to 5 days old."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Ecuador"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Ecuadorean public healthcare system provides the same level of care to locals and foreigners free of charge. However, it is currently facing challenges, including delays in obtaining appointments and limited access to medicines, due to funding constraints, increased demand and potential staff shortages. Private treatment can be very expensive, and private hospitals require a credit card guarantee for admission. Healthcare standards and access to specialised treatment can vary, and may be limited outside major cities."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a list of ",["medical providers in Ecuador","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/ecuador-list-of-hospitals--2"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["hospitalisation information pack","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/ecuador-hospitalisation-information-pack"]," for further details on healthcare in Ecuador, including a ",["list of hospitals","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/ecuador-list-of-hospitals"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Healthcare in the Galapagos Islands"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are limited medical facilities in the Galapagos Islands. You should ensure that your travel insurance includes air ambulance evacuation."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you travel to the Galapagos Islands by boat, you may be asked to supply information such as your blood group and emergency contacts when you board."]},{"k":"p","s":["Healthcare provision varies across the islands. San Cristóbal has a relatively well-equipped public hospital, although it may face the same constraints as mainland facilities. Santa Cruz has a basic hospital that is currently undergoing refurbishment. Isabela Island only has a very small and extremely basic health centre."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],". You can find information about ",["mental health support for British nationals in Ecuador.","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/ecuador-mental-health-support-for-british-nationals/ecuador-mental-health-support-for-british-nationals"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Ecuador"]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 911 (ambulance, fire, police)"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Tourism police"]},{"k":"p","s":["Quito has a tourism police unit with branches in the north, old town, airport and at bus terminals. There are also tourism police units in the cities of Guayaquil, Cuenca, Santa Elena and Galapagos provinces. Read more ",["information on the tourism police from their website","https://www.policia.gob.ec/policia-turismo/"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Reporting robbery and theft online"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can ",["report robbery and theft online in English","https://www.fiscalia.gob.ec/denuncias-en-linea-para-turistas/"]," to the Ecuador Attorney General’s Office (‘Fiscalía General’). This report is valid for insurance claims, however, once you leave Ecuador, following up a case report through this link may be complicated."]},{"k":"h","s":["Complaining about tourism services"]},{"k":"p","s":["To complain about tourism services, email the Ministry of Tourism: denuncias@produccion.gob.ec."]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=ecuador"],", ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=ecuador"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=ecuador"]," in Ecuador"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Ecuador","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/ecuador-bereavement-information-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested or imprisoned in Ecuador","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/ecuador-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/ecuador/british-embassy-quito"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/ecuador/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in Ecuador","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-ecuador"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":38780,"change":"Updated information following the Ecuadorean government extending the state of emergency for a further 30 days, and updated information about drug-assisted robbery ('Warnings and insurance' and 'Safety and security' pages)."},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/estonia":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T16:38Z","sha":"4212bc3b67cb12272422e8f7e6b8b047ad84916d19fddf32c6a1e00db72e7a84","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/estonia","bytes":57141,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Estonia travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-01-07T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-08-11T10:18:21+01:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/estonia/email-signup"]," when this advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/travelaware/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of the current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Estonia set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Estonian Embassy in London","https://london.mfa.ee/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["Estonia follows ",["Schengen area rules","https://europa.eu/youreurope/citizens/travel/entry-exit/non-eu-nationals/index_en.htm"],". Your passport must:"]},{"k":"li","s":["have a ‘date of issue’ less than 10 years before the date you arrive – if you renewed your passport before 1 October 2018, it might have a date of issue that is more than 10 years ago, making it invalid for entry to the Schengen area"]},{"k":"li","s":["have an ‘expiry date’ at least 3 months after the day you plan to leave the Schengen area (the expiry date does not need to be within 10 years of the date of issue)"]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can ",["travel without a visa to the Schengen area","https://www.gov.uk/travel-to-eu-schengen-area"],", which includes Estonia, for up to 90 days in any 180-day period without a visa. This applies if you travel:"]},{"k":"li","s":["as a tourist"]},{"k":"li","s":["to visit family or friends"]},{"k":"li","s":["to attend business meetings, cultural or sports events"]},{"k":"li","s":["for short-term studies or training"]},{"k":"p","s":["The ",["requirements for working in Estonia","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/travel-to-estonia-for-work"]," are different."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re travelling to other Schengen countries as well, make sure your whole visit is within the 90-day visa-free limit. Visits to Schengen countries within the previous 180 days before you travel count towards your 90 days. If you overstay the 90-day visa-free limit, you may be banned from entering Schengen countries for up to 3 years."]},{"k":"p","s":["At Estonian border control, you may also need to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["show a return or onward ticket"]},{"k":"li","s":["prove that you have enough money for your stay – the amount varies depending on your accommodation"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Staying longer than 90 days in a 180-day period"]},{"k":"p","s":["To stay longer than 90 days, check the ",["Estonian government’s entry requirements","https://www2.politsei.ee/en/teenused/eestis-viibimise-seaduslikud-alused/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re in Estonia with a residence permit or long-stay visa, this does not count towards your 90-day visa-free limit."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read about ",["entry processes if you live in Estonia","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/living-in-estonia#passports"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["New Schengen entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["The European Union’s (EU) new Entry/Exit System (EES) is now being implemented across the Schengen area."]},{"k":"p","s":["This means that when you travel into the Schengen area for short stays, you may need to register your biometric details, such as fingerprints and a photo. There is no cost for EES registration."]},{"k":"p","s":["On your first visit into a Schengen country, you may be asked to register your details at a special booth before proceeding to the immigration desk. Follow directions from your travel operator or the staff at your port of entry. You may also need to provide either your fingerprint or photo when you leave the Schengen area. Children aged 11 or younger will not have their fingerprints scanned but can be required to have their photo taken."]},{"k":"p","s":["You do not need to take any action before you arrive at the border on entry to the Schengen area, but EES may take each passenger extra time to complete so be prepared to wait longer than usual at the border and to allow more time for immigration controls when you depart the Schengen area. If you are departing the Schengen area by plane, allow extra time to reach your departure gate as EES checks may take place before boarding."]},{"k":"p","s":["EES is replacing the previous system of manually stamping passports when visitors arrive in the Schengen area for short stays. You may be asked to input biometric details every time you enter or exit."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you enter the Schengen area through the Port of Dover, Eurotunnel at Folkestone or Eurostar at St Pancras International, any information will be taken at the border before you leave the UK."]},{"k":"p","s":["Your digital EES record is valid for 3 years."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["information on the EU Entry/Exit System and to understand which countries are in the Schengen area","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/eu-entryexit-system"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are long-term resident in a Schengen country, you are exempt from EES in all Schengen countries. The full list of EES exemptions is on ",["the EU’s official Travel Europe website.","https://travel-europe.europa.eu/en/ees/to-whom-does-ees-not-apply"]]},{"k":"p","s":["If you believe you have been incorrectly entered into EES or your record of time spent in the Schengen area is incorrect, approach border officials when you next cross the Schengen border and request a correction. If you are exempt, carry documentation confirming your status. If you believe your time spent in the Schengen area has been recorded incorrectly, raise this with border officials and be prepared to provide supporting evidence if requested."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel from Ukraine, Russia and Belarus"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are arriving in Estonia from Ukraine, Russia or Belarus, check the ",["Estonian government crisis website","https://kriis.ee/en"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel from Russia"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can reserve crossings and check the real-time ",["level of traffic at border crossing points from Russia","https://www.estonianborder.eu/yphis/borderQueueInfo.action"]," on Estonia’s ‘Go Swift’ website."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["For details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Estonia guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/75/estonia#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about ",["goods you can take into or out of Estonia","https://www.emta.ee/en/private-client/consignments-travel-settlement/travel/declaration-goods"],". You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking food and drink into Estonia"]},{"k":"p","s":["You cannot take ",["meat, milk or products containing them into EU countries","https://ec.europa.eu/food/animals/animalproducts/personal_imports_en"],". There are some exceptions such as powdered baby milk, baby food and special foods or pet feed required for medical reasons."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Restrictions on Russian vehicles"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are restrictions on vehicles with Russian licence plates in Estonia. See the ",["Estonian Ministry of the Interior’s website for more information","https://www.siseministeerium.ee/en/news/estonia-prohibits-entry-russian-motor-vehicles"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Estonia"]},{"k":"p","s":["Although there’s no recent history of terrorism in Estonia, attacks cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"p","s":["Attacks could be indiscriminate including in places visited by foreign nationals. Stay aware of your surroundings, keep up to date with local media reports and follow the advice of local authorities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["Pickpockets can be a problem in bars and nightclubs in Tallinn’s Old Town."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Drink spiking, alcohol and sexual assault"]},{"k":"p","s":["Attacks or assault, including sexual assaults, are rare but do occur. The risk is highest late at night around popular nightlife locations. To reduce your personal risk:"]},{"k":"li","s":["save the location of your accommodation on your maps app, so it’s easier to find at the end of the night"]},{"k":"li","s":["set up a WhatsApp group to keep in touch with others in your group"]},{"k":"li","s":["keep an eye on each other’s drinks to make sure they do not get spiked"]},{"k":"li","s":["do not let a friend walk back to their hotel alone"]},{"k":"li","s":["do not give a drunk person more alcohol"]},{"k":"p","s":["Alcohol and drugs can reduce your vigilance, making you less in control. If you drink, know your limit. Drinks served in bars in Estonia are often stronger than those in the UK."]},{"k":"p","s":["Report anything that does not feel right to local authorities or hotel or club management."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taxi safety"]},{"k":"p","s":["Always use pre-arranged taxis or official taxis with ‘TAKSO’ signage. Do not accept lifts from unmarked vehicles or with strangers."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you use an app, check that the car details match the car assigned to you. See ‘ ",["transport risks","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/estonia/safety-and-security"],"’ for more details."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Bank card skimming"]},{"k":"p","s":["Keep cards in sight when paying in shops and restaurants. Read more about ",["how to avoid card skimming","https://www.actionfraud.police.uk/a-z-of-fraud/bank-card-and-cheque-fraud"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs"]},{"k":"p","s":["Illegal drugs, including cannabis, are strictly prohibited, even in very small quantities. Severe penalties apply for possessing, using, buying, or smuggling illegal drugs, including when transiting through airports. You should expect long jail sentences of up to 10 years and heavy fines."]},{"k":"p","s":["Airports in Estonia have excellent technology and security for detecting illegal items. This is also used to scan the baggage of transiting passengers."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Same-sex sexual activity is legal in Estonia, and same-sex marriages have been recognised since 1 January 2024."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Estonia, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"]," and check the ",["rules of the road in the RAC’s Estonia guide","https://www.rac.co.uk/drive/travel/country/estonia/"],". The guide lists driving regulations and other legal requirements you need to be aware of."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can drive in Estonia with a UK driving licence. You must have the original V5C vehicle registration document with you. Check for more details on the ",["Estonian state portal","https://www.eesti.ee/en/traffic/vehicles-and-right-to-drive/travel-documents-for-a-driver-of-a-motor-vehicle"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check if you need a ",["UK sticker to drive your car outside the UK","https://www.gov.uk/displaying-number-plates/flags-identifiers-and-stickers"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are visiting Estonia, you may be able to use your ",["Blue Badge","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/blue-badge-using-it-in-the-eu/using-a-blue-badge-in-the-european-union"]," in some circumstances. Check local parking rules."]},{"k":"p","s":["Hire car companies often have stricter requirements for their customers, such as a year of driving experience or a higher minimum age."]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not drink and drive. If you are tested and found to have more than a quarter of England’s legal limit of alcohol in your body, you may get a fine and possible imprisonment."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taxis"]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not hail unmarked taxis – they’re illegal. Make sure the taxi has:"]},{"k":"li","s":["a price list on the back window"]},{"k":"li","s":["the driver’s licence in a visible place"]},{"k":"li","s":["a working meter"]},{"k":"li","s":["‘TAKSO’ signage (for taxis at taxi ranks)"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can also use taxi apps like Bolt, Forus and Uber."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Drone incidents"]},{"k":"p","s":["Some Ukrainian drones aimed at Russia have crossed into Estonian airspace. Follow official guidance as necessary."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Dial 112 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance or medical assistance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Estonia","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/75/estonia#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See what ",["health risks you’ll face in Estonia","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/75/estonia"],", including biting insects and ticks."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries. If you need advice about what you can take into Estonia, contact the ",["Estonian Medicine Agency","https://www.ravimiamet.ee/en/human-medicines/manufacture-distribution-pharmacy/travelling-medicinal-products"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Estonia"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a list of ",["medical providers in Estonia","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/estonia-list-of-medical-facilitiespractitioners"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Health insurance cards"]},{"k":"p","s":["To get medically necessary state healthcare in Estonia, you need a Global Health Insurance Card (GHIC) or a European Health Insurance Card (EHIC)."]},{"k":"p","s":["The NHS’s ",["getting healthcare abroad webpage","https://www.nhs.uk/using-the-nhs/healthcare-abroad/apply-for-a-free-uk-global-health-insurance-card-ghic/"]," has details about:"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to apply for a GHIC"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to get temporary cover if you lose your card or it does not arrive in time"]},{"k":"li","s":["who qualifies for a new EHIC instead of a GHIC"]},{"k":"li","s":["what treatment counts as medically necessary"]},{"k":"p","s":["A GHIC or EHIC is not an alternative to travel insurance. You may have costs your GHIC or EHIC does not cover, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["changes to travel and accommodation bookings"]},{"k":"li","s":["additional standard costs for treatment"]},{"k":"li","s":["medical repatriation to the UK"]},{"k":"li","s":["treatment that is ruled non-urgent"]},{"k":"li","s":["private healthcare"]},{"k":"li","s":["private clinics"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is also ",["guidance on healthcare if you’re living in Estonia","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/healthcare-in-estonia"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Estonia"]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 112 (ambulance, fire, police)"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Estonia"],", ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Estonia"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=Estonia"]," in Estonia"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Estonia","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/deathbereavement-information-sheet-in-tallinn"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested in Estonia","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/estonia-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/estonia/british-embassy-tallinn"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/estonia/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in Estonia","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-estonia"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":14690,"change":"Updated information on European Entry-Exit System (EES) (‘Entry requirements’ page)."},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/egypt":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-20T16:50Z","sha":"486d555a42e4f28c13b292c97908c584da0a64916c400e16f2fc11862e99e13e","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/egypt","bytes":88231,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Egypt travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-03-18T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-10-27T16:03:56+00:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["Your travel insurance could be invalidated if you travel against advice from the Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO)."]},{"k":"h","s":["Areas where FCDO advises against travel"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Egypt-Libya border"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to within 20km of the Egypt-Libya border, except for the town of El Salloum, where we advise against all but essential travel."]},{"k":"hs","s":["North Sinai"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to the North Sinai Governorate."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Northern part of South Sinai"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the northern part of the South Sinai Governorate, beyond the St Catherine-Nuweibaa road, except for the coastal areas along the west and east of the peninsula."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Eastern part of Ismailiyah Governorate"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the Ismailiyah Governorate east of the Suez Canal."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Western Desert"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the area west of the Nile Valley and Nile Delta regions, except for:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Luxor, Qina, Aswan, Abu Simbel and the Valley of the Kings"]},{"k":"li","s":["the Faiyum Governorate"]},{"k":"li","s":["the coastal areas between the Nile Delta and Marsa Matruh"]},{"k":"li","s":["the Marsa Matruh-Siwa road"]},{"k":"li","s":["the oasis town of Siwa"]},{"k":"li","s":["the Giza Governorate north-east of the Bahariya Oasis"]},{"k":"li","s":["the White Desert and Black Desert"]},{"k":"li","s":["the oasis towns of Bahariya, Farafra, Dakhla (Mut) and Kharga"]},{"k":"li","s":["the following roads and the desert area between them and the Nile valley: the road between Giza and Farafra and within 50km either side of this road (but FCDO advises against all but essential travel on the road between Bahariya and Siwa)"]},{"k":"li","s":["the road between Farafra, Dakhla (Mut) and Kharga"]},{"k":"li","s":["the road between Kharga and Baris"]},{"k":"li","s":["the road between Baris and Luxor"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Hala’ib Triangle and Bir Tawil Trapezoid"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the Hala’ib Triangle and the Bir Tawil Trapezoid."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["why FCDO advises against travel","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/egypt/regional-risks"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Regional tensions"]},{"k":"p","s":["The context in the Middle East remains deeply unpredictable and the risk of sudden escalation is high. Since conflict began in early 2026, Iran has stated its intention to target locations associated with the US and Israel, including, but not limited to, organisations, businesses, facilities, and institutions. There have been strikes and retaliatory attacks by Iran and others across the region against civilian and military infrastructure."]},{"k":"h","s":["Conflict in Israel and Palestine"]},{"k":"p","s":["International borders in Israel and Palestine could close at short notice, including the Taba border crossing between Israel and Egypt. Check with local authorities and read ",["Israel travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/israel"]," and ",["Palestine travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/palestine"]," before trying to cross."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Entering Egypt from Gaza"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Rafah border crossing is currently closed. When re-opened, Israel, Egypt and the authorities in Gaza may determine procedures for who is permitted to cross and when."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are a British national in Gaza who wants to leave Gaza, see ",["Israel travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/israel#travelling-to-egypt-from-gaza"]," and ",["Palestine travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/palestine#travelling-to-egypt-from-gaza"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Concern for friends and family"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are concerned about friends or family, or need support from the UK government, call the British Embassy in Cairo."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: + 20 (0)2 2791 6000"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you have technical difficulties using this number, call +44 1767 667 600 (UK number)."]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/egypt/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of Egypt’s current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Egypt set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Egyptian Consulate General in the UK","https://egyptconsulate.co.uk/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Egypt, your passport must have an ‘expiry date’ at least 6 months after the date you arrive and have at least one blank page."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["British passport holders travelling to Egypt normally need a visa."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are arriving by air to Sharm El-Sheikh and staying for less than 15 days at resorts in Sharm El Sheikh, Dahab, Nuweiba or Taba, you do not need a visa. You will get a free entry permission stamp on arrival at Sharm El-Sheikh Airport. If you plan to travel outside the resorts or stay more than 15 days, you must get a visa. You can get a visa at Sharm El-Sheikh Airport or online."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you arrive in South Sinai by land through the Taba Border Crossing, see ‘Entering Egypt from Israel’."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Applying for a visa"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can apply for a visa:"]},{"k":"li","s":["online – ",["getting an e-visa in advance","https://visa2egypt.gov.eg/eVisa/Home?VISTK=AMEV-QAST-XKKB-4X4J-LYML-KSS1-J4VF-B3V5-GO2U-AYIZ-4F82-1WR5-RW7O-0L87-4CZ8-9CFV"]," can help to prevent delays, tourist e-visas are valid for up to 3 months"]},{"k":"li","s":["in person or by post – apply through the ",["Egyptian Consulate General in the UK","https://egyptconsulate.co.uk/visas/"]]},{"k":"li","s":["on arrival in Egypt – approved airports have kiosks before you reach the immigration counters where you can buy a physical visa for 30 US dollars (cash only). Visas on arrival are valid for up to 30 days."]},{"k":"p","s":["Starting from 1 August 2026, travellers arriving at Cairo International Airport can also purchase digital visas on arrival (card payment only) via self-service machines or the ",["Visa on Arrival portal","https://visaonarrival.gov.eg/home/landing"]," for 36 US dollars, including a 6 US dollar digital service fee."]},{"k":"p","s":["British passport holders from British Overseas Territories and Crown Dependencies cannot apply online."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Visa extensions"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can apply for a visa extension at the Egyptian Passport and Immigration Offices. If you try to leave Egypt on an expired visa, you may face difficulties, including a fine if your visa has expired by more than 14 days. Contact the ",["Egyptian Consulate General in the UK","https://egyptconsulate.co.uk/visas/"]," for more information."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Visa agents in airports"]},{"k":"p","s":["You do not need to buy a visa from an agent. Agents often charge more than the required 30 US dollars. If an agent harasses you, report the incident to the tourist police in the airport terminal."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Gender expression"]},{"k":"p","s":["You may be denied entry if your gender expression or physical appearance does not match the sex marker in your passport or your passport photograph. See ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Entering Egypt from Israel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you plan to cross the border from Israel into Egypt at Taba, we recommend you bring at least 170 US dollars (cash) per person, with some extra US dollars in cash to cover any further expenses. Since early March 2026, border crossing charges at Taba have been subject to increases at short notice."]},{"k":"li","s":["If staying in Taba, travellers will need to pay a border tax of 20 US dollars. The border tax allows you to obtain an entry permission stamp for a stay of up to 15 days"]},{"k":"li","s":["If travelling further than Taba, including to Sharm El-Sheikh, but remaining within the Sinai Peninsula, travellers will need to pay a border tax of 120 US dollars. The border tax allows you to obtain an entry permission stamp for a stay of up to 15 days"]},{"k":"li","s":["If travelling beyond the Sinai Peninsula, including to fly from airports such as Cairo and Hurghada, travellers will need to pay a border tax of 120 US dollars and purchase a standard entry visa for 30 US dollars. At Taba, this entry visa also requires a “letter of guarantee”, provided by travel agents and costing around 20 US dollars. Both the visa and the “letter of guarantee” can be purchased at the Border Crossing"]},{"k":"p","s":["If travelling by car through the Taba Border Crossing, you may also be required to pay 100 US dollars, with additional charges for parking."]},{"k":"p","s":["Please note that ATMs at the Taba Border Crossing are unreliable and frequently run out of cash. Travellers should obtain US dollars before travelling or in Eilat before arriving at the Crossing as all payments are required in cash."]},{"k":"p","s":["Border officials may ask travellers to remove hats, coats or other items of clothing, including religious clothing, as they pass through the Taba Border Crossing terminal."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Entering Egypt from Jordan"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ferry services operate between Aqaba, Jordan and Taba Heights and Nuweiba in Egypt. Contact ferry operators directly for schedules and availability. Please check Travel Advice for Jordan for latest on exit requirements."]},{"k":"p","s":["If your stay in Sinai will exceed 15 days, or you are planning to travel in Egypt beyond the Sinai Peninsula, including to fly from mainland airports, for example Cairo or Hurghada, you will need an entry visa. If entering at Taba Heights, this costs 35 US dollars. If entering at Nuweiba, this costs 30 US dollars. Visas can be purchased at the port terminals. Travellers should obtain USD in cash before travelling given payments are often required in cash."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Entering Egypt from Sudan"]},{"k":"p","s":["The situation at the Egypt-Sudan border remains unclear. There are 2 main land border crossings, Qustul and Argeen. There is almost no infrastructure at these crossings, and it is no longer possible to obtain a visa on arrival at these locations. The Egyptian consulate is based in Wadi Halfa, 30km from the border, applications for Egyptian visas can be made here, but visa approvals can take upwards of 6 months."]},{"k":"p","s":["The British Embassy in Cairo does not have staff at the border and our ability to provide assistance is very limited. Travel in and from Sudan is at your own risk. See ",["Sudan travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/sudan"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are a British national and have crossed into Egypt from Sudan without valid documents, contact the ",["British Embassy in Cairo","https://www.gov.uk/world/organisations/british-embassy-cairo"]," for support."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Egypt, you must have a certificate to prove you’ve had a yellow fever vaccination if you’re coming from a ",["country listed as a transmission risk","https://nathnacyfzone.org.uk/factsheet/65/countries-with-risk-of-yellow-fever-transmission"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["For full details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Egypt guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/71/egypt#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["HIV test for work permits"]},{"k":"p","s":["You will need to show HIV test results to apply for a work permit."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about ",["goods you can take into or out of Egypt","https://www.cairo-airport.com/en-us/Services/Passenger-Guide/Customs-Regulations"],". You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty. Contact the ",["Egyptian Consulate General in the UK","https://egyptconsulate.co.uk/"]," for more information about customs rules."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking money into or out of Egypt"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can bring up to 5,000 Egyptian pounds into or out of Egypt."]},{"k":"p","s":["You must declare foreign currency worth more than 10,000 US dollars on arrival – there is no limit to the amount of foreign currency you can bring."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Electronic and communication devices"]},{"k":"p","s":["You should declare high value electronic devices and recording equipment when you arrive. Officials are likely to confiscate satellite phones or radio communications equipment unless you have prior clearance from the Ministry of Telecommunications."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"p","s":["Approximately one million British people travel to Egypt each year. Most visits are trouble-free. This guide also has safety advice for ",["regions of Egypt","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/egypt/regional-risks"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Egypt"]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorists are likely to try to carry out attacks in Egypt."]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorist attacks could be indiscriminate including in places visited by foreign nationals. Stay aware of your surroundings, keep up to date with local media reports and follow the advice of local authorities. Be vigilant in crowds and large gatherings."]},{"k":"p","s":["Targets might include:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Egyptian security forces"]},{"k":"li","s":["religious sites"]},{"k":"li","s":["large public gatherings"]},{"k":"li","s":["places visited by foreign nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Egypt have a significant security presence across the country. Extra measures are in place at tourist sites."]},{"k":"p","s":["Examples of recent attacks include:"]},{"k":"li","s":["In 2024, one Israeli-Canadian national was killed in a shooting attack in Alexandria"]},{"k":"li","s":["In 2023, 2 Israeli tourists and an Egyptian tour guide were killed in a shooting attack in Alexandria"]},{"k":"li","s":["In 2022, 4 police officers and one insurgent killed in an attack on a police checkpoint in Ismailiya City"]},{"k":"h","s":["Political situation"]},{"k":"p","s":["The political environment in Egypt is restrictive. Avoid large gatherings, demonstrations and protests as the situation could change quickly and without warning. Security forces have responded forcefully to protests and disturbances."]},{"k":"p","s":["Foreign nationals involved in any political activity or activities critical of the government may be at risk of detention. This includes posting negative comments on social media."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["The crime rate is generally low, but visitors should take sensible precautions as they would in the UK."]},{"k":"p","s":["To report a crime, phone the tourist police on 126. If you do not report a crime before you leave Egypt, it will be difficult to prosecute later."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Sexual assault and harassment"]},{"k":"p","s":["A number of sexual assaults have been reported to the British Embassy, including cases involving minors."]},{"k":"p","s":["The majority of cases that have been reported took place in tourist resorts in the Red Sea region, often committed by someone the victim had already met, including hotel workers and excursion staff. There have also been reports of hotel staff discouraging incidents being reported to local police."]},{"k":"p","s":["Female travellers should exercise caution when travelling alone, particularly at night, in taxis."]},{"k":"p","s":["Take extra precautions:"]},{"k":"li","s":["do not leave children unaccompanied"]},{"k":"li","s":["do not allow hotel staff to enter your room when you are alone – try to ensure a friend or relative is present"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid travelling in a taxi alone – if this is not possible, apply extra security by sharing the details of your driver, trip and live location with a friend"]},{"k":"li","s":["use reputable providers for any services and excursions, and carry out research beforehand"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid sharing personal contact or social media details"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["Pickpocketing is rare in Egypt. Take the same precautions as you would in the UK."]},{"k":"p","s":["It might be helpful to make photocopies of your passport, visa and flight ticket to keep separately from originals when travelling. If your passport is lost or stolen, tell the police immediately and get a police report. You will need a police report to get visa stamps transferred to your replacement passport."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Scammers and touts at tourist sites"]},{"k":"p","s":["Be cautious in tourist areas, where scammers and touts sometimes target foreign nationals."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"p","s":["Egypt is predominantly an Islamic country. Take care to respect local traditions, customs, laws and religions. Seek to avoid offence, especially during Ramadan or when you visit religious areas."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Religion"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to encourage people to convert to Christianity or any other religion."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Ramadan"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ramadan is a holy month for Muslims. The dates vary by year and country and you should check this before you travel. During this time, it is culturally insensitive to eat, drink or smoke in public during daylight hours. It is advisable not to play loud music, dance or swear in public."]},{"k":"p","s":["Get more advice when you arrive from your tour guide, hotel or business contacts."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should also:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check opening hours of shops and restaurants"]},{"k":"li","s":["be aware that if hotels and restaurants are providing food or drink in fasting hours, they may separate non-fasting guests, for example with screens"]},{"k":"li","s":["follow local dress codes – clothing that does not meet local dress codes may cause more offence at this time"]},{"k":"li","s":["be aware that driving may be erratic, particularly when people are trying to get home at dusk"]},{"k":"li","s":["be patient and show tolerance"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police check ID regularly and will ask to see your passport. They may detain you if you cannot show your ID and your visa (or a digital/paper copy)."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Dress code"]},{"k":"p","s":["Dress modestly, especially in rural areas, mosques and souqs (markets)."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Behaviour in public"]},{"k":"p","s":["Couples showing physical affection in public is frowned upon. Holding hands is generally fine. Behaviour accepted in tourist resort areas may not be accepted elsewhere."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Alcohol laws"]},{"k":"p","s":["Drinking alcohol anywhere other than licensed restaurants, bars, or private homes or certain tourist resorts is illegal and can lead to arrest."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs penalties"]},{"k":"p","s":["Possession, use or trafficking of illegal drugs is a serious offence and can, even for small amounts, lead to life imprisonment or the death penalty. People who get a life sentence on drugs charges normally spend the rest of their lives in prison with no chance of parole or a pardon."]},{"k":"p","s":["Khat is illegal in Egypt."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Photography and filming restrictions"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must get a permit to enter Egypt with professional photography or film equipment. This includes photography umbrellas, artificial outdoor lighting gear and any equipment that occupies or blocks public roads."]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to take or share photos that could be considered damaging to the country’s image."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Ministry of Tourism regulations","https://egymonuments.gov.eg/en/news/egyptian-government-decided-to-allow-egyptians-and-tourists-to-take-photographs-for-free/"]," on photography say that you must get an Egyptian citizen’s written permission before you take their photo. Taking pictures of children is prohibited. Do not photograph officials without their consent."]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to take photos of, or near, military property. This includes the Suez Canal."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are in any doubt, get permission before taking photos. There are sensitivities about taking photographs of:"]},{"k":"li","s":["embassies"]},{"k":"li","s":["government buildings and infrastructure"]},{"k":"li","s":["religious buildings"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Drones"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to use radio-controlled helicopters or drones to take photos near sensitive sites."]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not import, use or produce drones in Egypt unless the ",["Egyptian Ministry of Defence","https://www.mod.gov.eg/ModWebSite/Default.aspx"]," gives you permission beforehand. Anyone who uses or imports drones without permission could get a prison sentence of up to 7 years or a fine of 5,000 to 50,000 Egyptian pounds."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Same-sex sexual activity is not explicitly criminalised in Egypt. However, the Egyptian authorities have prosecuted LGBT+ people under ‘debauchery’ laws, including people flying rainbow flags at public events."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is little public acceptance of same-sex relationships in Egypt. Same-sex couples showing affection in public are likely to receive negative attention."]},{"k":"p","s":["Be cautious about sharing content or having discussions of a sexual nature on social media, especially about sexual acts that are considered illegal. Some travellers have been arrested and imprisoned for this."]},{"k":"p","s":["You may be denied entry if your gender expression or physical appearance does not match the sex marker in your passport or your passport photograph."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Child custody law"]},{"k":"p","s":["Egyptian family law is very different from UK law, particularly around child custody. See ",["International parental child abduction","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/international-parental-child-abduction"]," for information and how to get assistance."]},{"k":"h","s":["Outdoor activities and adventure tourism"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Insurance for adventure activities"]},{"k":"p","s":["Make sure your travel insurance, or the tour or dive company, will cover the costs for any air or sea rescue, which can cost more than 4,000 US dollars per hour. The Egyptian authorities will only start rescue operations when they are guaranteed payment. Book excursions for activities at your resort or through approved agents or tour operators."]},{"k":"p","s":["See Foreign travel insurance for more information."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Hot air balloons"]},{"k":"p","s":["Speak to your tour company before booking a hot air balloon flight. Some UK tour operators have stopped selling balloon flights because they have not been able to verify safety standards."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Watersports and cruises"]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been recent incidents involving British nationals on diving boats/tours in the Red Sea. Some of these have included fatalities. Safety standards of Red Sea resort diving operators and boats vary considerably. Some operators may not provide adequate safety and insurance standards."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Marine Accident Investigation Branch (an independent investigative unit within the Department for Transport) published ",["guidance","https://www.gov.uk/government/news/safety-bulletin-12025-published"]," about liveaboard vessels on their website in February 2025. They recommend that prospective customers book liveaboard dive holidays only through reputable vendors who can provide assurance about the safety standards applicable to the dive boat. On arrival on board, customers should request that the crew provide a thorough safety briefing before departure."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["observe safety standards on board and exercise caution"]},{"k":"li","s":["make bookings through your tour representative or reputable operator if possible"]},{"k":"li","s":["not dive below your insurance policy’s depth limit – doing so will invalidate your cover"]},{"k":"p","s":["Shark attacks are rare, but there have been attacks on tourists in the Red Sea region. Monitor any updates from local authorities or your tour operator."]},{"k":"p","s":["See ⁠ ",["watersports safety advice","https://www.rospa.com/leisure-water-safety/water/advice/watersports-abroad"]," from the Royal Society for the Prevention of Accidents (ROSPA)."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Quad bikes and desert visits"]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been several serious quad bike accidents involving British nationals in resort areas. Take the same precautions as you would in the UK. Safety standards vary considerably. Always wear a crash helmet."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Egypt, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You’ll need to have both the ",["1949 version of the international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," and your UK driving licence with you in the car. You cannot buy an IDP outside the UK, so get one before you travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can drive in Egypt using your UK licence and an IDP for up to 6 months. If you plan to stay longer, you must apply for an Egyptian driving licence."]},{"k":"p","s":["Drivers and front seat passengers must wear seatbelts."]},{"k":"p","s":["Driving under the influence of alcohol or drugs is a serious offence in Egypt. If you are caught, you may get a fine and possible imprisonment."]},{"k":"p","s":["You may not be allowed to import a vehicle into Egypt. If you want to bring in a vehicle temporarily, you must get a ‘carnet de passage’ from the Automobile Association."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Driving conditions"]},{"k":"p","s":["Accidents are common because of variable road conditions, dangerous driving and poor traffic law enforcement. Do not drive outside main cities and resorts at night. Make sure you have appropriate insurance."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Off-road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re travelling off road, use a qualified guide and get a permit from the ",["Ministry of Interior","https://emoves.moi.gov.eg/en/"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Rail and bus travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["Serious bus crashes in recent years have caused many deaths, including tourists."]},{"k":"p","s":["There have also been fatal train collisions and derailments."]},{"k":"hs","s":["River and sea travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["Overcrowding and poor safety standards have caused accidents on Red Sea ferries and Nile cruises."]},{"k":"h","s":["Regional risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["This section has safety advice for regions of Egypt. It only covers regions where FCDO has specific advice."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should also read ",["FCDO’s overall travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/egypt/warnings-and-insurance"]," and ",["safety and security advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/egypt/safety-and-security"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Egypt-Libya border"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to within 20km of the Egypt-Libya border, except for the town of El Salloum, where we advise against all but essential travel. There are active military operations targeting criminal activity in this area."]},{"k":"h","s":["North Sinai"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to North Sinai Governate due to continuing criminal activity and terrorist attacks on police and security forces that have resulted in deaths. See ",["Terrorism in Egypt","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/egypt/safety-and-security#terrorism-in-egypt"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Northern part of South Sinai"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the northern part of South Sinai Governate, beyond the St Catherine-Nuweibaa road, except for the coastal areas along the west and east of the peninsula."]},{"k":"p","s":["We advise against all but essential travel due to criminal activity and terrorist attacks on police and security forces that have resulted in deaths. See ",["Terrorism","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/egypt/safety-and-security#terrorism"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you plan to travel in a 4-wheel-drive vehicle from mainland Egypt through the Suez crossing, you must get a permit from Travel Permits Department of the Egyptian Ministry of the Interior. You should book any activities outside of resort areas through approved agents or tour operators."]},{"k":"p","s":["Travel to Red Sea tourist areas in the southern part of the Sinai Peninsula is generally low risk. Security forces carry out routine checks on vehicles and at airports to protect resorts such as Sharm El Sheikh, Hurghada and Marsa Alam."]},{"k":"h","s":["Eastern part of Ismailiyah Governorate"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the parts of the Ismailiyah Governorate which are east of the Suez Canal, due to ongoing military operations against terrorists and criminals. Egyptian authorities at checkpoints may prevent onward travel to this region. See ",["Terrorism","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/egypt/safety-and-security#terrorism"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Western Desert"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the area west of the Nile Valley and Nile Delta regions due to risks from criminal activity and military operations, except for:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Luxor, Qina, Valley of the Kings, Aswan and Abu Simbel"]},{"k":"li","s":["the Faiyum Governorate"]},{"k":"li","s":["the coastal areas between the Nile Delta and Marsa Matruh"]},{"k":"li","s":["the Marsa Matruh-Siwa road"]},{"k":"li","s":["the oasis town of Siwa"]},{"k":"li","s":["the Giza Governorate north-east of the Bahariya Oasis"]},{"k":"li","s":["the White Desert and Black Desert"]},{"k":"li","s":["the oasis towns of Bahariya, Farafra, Dakhla (Mut) and Kharga"]},{"k":"li","s":["the following roads and the desert area between them and the Nile valley: the road between Giza and Farafra and within 50km either side of this road (but FCDO advises against all but essential travel on the road between Bahariya and Siwa)"]},{"k":"li","s":["the road between Farafra, Dakhla (Mut) and Kharga"]},{"k":"li","s":["the road between Kharga and Baris"]},{"k":"li","s":["the road between Baris and Luxor"]},{"k":"p","s":["Tourists who enter the Western Desert areas of Bahariya Oasis, Farafra, the White Desert and Black Desert must apply for permits in advance and use an official guide. There is limited phone reception and poor medical facilities. Monitor travel advice and follow guidance from official guides and local authorities."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel on the road between Al Bawiti and Siwa, including the desert areas near the start of the road in Bahariya. The road is closed and there are military checkpoints."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you travel to the south-west corner of Egypt near the border with Sudan or Libya, you will need a permit from the ",["Ministry of Interior","https://emoves.moi.gov.eg/en"],". Bandits and armed groups operate in these areas."]},{"k":"p","s":["Be extremely cautious in all border areas."]},{"k":"h","s":["Hala’ib Triangle and Bir Tawil Trapezoid"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the Hala’ib Triangle and Bir Tawil Trapezoid."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Hala’ib Triangle remains disputed territory between Egypt and Sudan. If you’re in the Hala’ib Triangle and need urgent UK government support, contact the ",["British Embassy in Cairo","https://www.gov.uk/world/organisations/british-embassy-cairo"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Bir Tawil Trapezoid is unclaimed by either Egypt or Sudan. If you’re in this area and need urgent UK government support, ",["contact FCDO","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/home"]," in the last country you travelled through."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Call 123 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance or medical assistance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Egypt","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/71/egypt#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Egypt","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/71/egypt#General_Information"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["dengue"]},{"k":"li","s":["tick-borne diseases such as Crimean-Congo haemorrhagic fever"]},{"k":"p","s":["Altitude sickness is a risk in parts of Egypt. Read more about ",["altitude sickness on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/26/altitude-illness"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Some prescribed and over-the-counter medicines may be controlled substances in Egypt. You may need permission from Egypt’s Ministry of Health before you arrive. If you do not have prior permission or the required documentation, you will not be allowed to take the medication into Egypt and you may be prosecuted."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you travel with prescription medication, carry a letter from your GP stating the:"]},{"k":"li","s":["condition you’re being treated for"]},{"k":"li","s":["amount of medication you will be carrying"]},{"k":"li","s":["medication is for your personal use only"]},{"k":"p","s":["For further information, contact the ",["Egyptian Consulate General in the UK","https://egyptconsulate.co.uk/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Egypt"]},{"k":"p","s":["Some hotel doctors have overcharged for treatment and medicines. Pharmacies outside hotels will often supply medication at lower prices. FCDO has a ",["list of medical providers in Egypt","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/egypt-list-of-medical-facilities-practitioners"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"p","s":["Access to specialised treatment for psychiatric illness is limited and may not be available outside major cities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Egypt"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ambulance: 123"]},{"k":"p","s":["Fire: 180"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police: 122"]},{"k":"p","s":["Tourist police: 126"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Egypt"],", ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find?country=Egypt&serviceType=funeralDirectors"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=Egypt"]," in Egypt"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Egypt","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/egypt-bereavement-information-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested in Egypt","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/egypt-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you are ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/egypt/british-embassy-cairo"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/egypt/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in Egypt","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-egypt"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":30990,"change":"Updated information about Regional tensions (see ‘Warnings and insurance’ page)"},"https://theconversation.com/andy-burnham-and-climate-change-where-does-the-prime-minister-really-stand-296200":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:38Z","sha":"d8393585a419bf51818e3d2e17d816c11806262509b1bcb5cd4f00313d1cb0f6","read":"https://theconversation.com/andy-burnham-and-climate-change-where-does-the-prime-minister-really-stand-296200","bytes":181459,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Andy Burnham and climate change: where does the prime minister really stand?","by":[{"n":"James Jackson","r":"Lecturer and Research Fellow, School of Social Sciences, University of Manchester"}],"pub":"2026-11-10T14:24:03Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Since becoming prime minister, Andy Burnham has set out a relatively ambitious political agenda. He has outlined plans for a national care service, a “Great British Grid” and suggested a rethink of the UK’s relationship with the European Union."]},{"k":"p","s":["But one big omission of Burnham’s agenda is ",["climate","https://theconversation.com/topics/climate-change-27"]," policy. Amid the proposals that put clear water between him and his predecessor Keir Starmer, Burnham’s climate agenda remains unknown."]},{"k":"p","s":["The prime minister has reiterated his intention to reach ",["net zero by 2050","https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/sep/17/andy-burnham-uk-must-fully-commit-to-reaching-net-zero-by-2050"]," (though this target is contentious due to whether it actually reflects climate science as well as the extent to which it depends upon as yet unavailable technology). He has also pledged to attend Cop31, the UN climate summit currently underway in Turkey, in person. However, ",["the budget","https://theconversation.com/the-government-has-delayed-the-toughest-spending-decisions-but-heres-what-we-do-know-after-the-budget-295491"]," – Burnham’s first real opportunity to set out his vision – raised concerns about whether his political rhetoric could translate into a coherent climate policy."]},{"k":"p","s":["The budget revealed that increased defence spending would come at the cost of ",["£3 billion of cuts","https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/nov/08/andy-burnham-uk-climate-crisis-rosebank-jackdaw"]," at the Department for Energy Security and Net Zero. Subsidies for heat pumps, boilers, the warm homes plan, hydrogen and carbon capture and storage were the most prominent policies to be culled. This not only limits the UK’s green industrial policy, but suggests that energy security is still not considered to be part of national security."]},{"k":"h","s":["Energy security and rising bills"]},{"k":"p","s":["For years, the UK has been misaligned with its own carbon budgets set under the ",["Climate Change Act 2008","https://www.legislation.gov.uk/ukpga/2008/27/contents"],". After the Conservatives began to question the ",["objective of net zero","https://www.gov.uk/government/speeches/pm-speech-on-net-zero-20-september-2023"]," towards the ",["end of their term in office","https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/13876988.2023.2242799"],", the election of the first Labour government in 14 years was expected to ",["mark a turning point","https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1111/1467-923x.70151"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Burnham’s climate position has become entwined (and somewhat undermined) by energy security concerns following the so-called ",["fossilflationary","https://theconversation.com/as-the-climate-breaks-down-costs-go-up-welcome-to-climateflation-289352"]," pressures caused by the the US and Israel’s conflict with Iran. This has fed into the licensing of the ",["Jackdaw gasfield","https://theconversation.com/jackdaw-approval-what-a-new-north-sea-gasfield-means-for-uk-energy-security-bills-and-tax-291418"]," 150 miles east of Aberdeen. This is part of Burnham’s self-described ",["“pragmatic”","https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/jul/30/burnham-promises-pragmatic-approach-to-north-sea-oil-and-gas"]," approach to new drilling in the North Sea."]},{"k":"p","s":["The initial justification was that the move would improve energy security by increasing the domestic supply of oil and gas. But critics say that increasing supply has ",["little to no effect","https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cq4g13pplyzzo"]," on domestic bills, as prices are set by international markets. Revenues made from the project will be used to finance an ",["Energy Wealth Fund","https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cm4g1zrl2nrqo"]," to invest in green technologies elsewhere."]},{"k":"p","s":["Then there’s the cost of living. As winter approaches, an increasing number of households will have to choose between ",["heating and eating","https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cglj9685nj0o"],". In response, Chancellor John Healey’s budget ",["removed green levies","https://www.cityam.com/energy-bills-green-levies-scrapped/"]," from consumer bills. These levies fund environmental programmes such as renewable schemes, but the money will now be sourced from general taxation."]},{"k":"p","s":["This does reduce bills in the short term. But the shift, combined with other cuts, raises doubts over the long term."]},{"k":"p","s":["It’s argued that removing green levies from bills will reduce the relative cost of energy. This is a salient argument as the UK approaches a period of higher energy demand to heat the country’s homes. But critics say that reducing support for green energy infrastructure will delay the advent of abundant cheap energy."]},{"k":"h","s":["Political and economic tests"]},{"k":"p","s":["Labour now has two challenges. The first is the political bind the party finds itself in. ",["Its manifesto","https://labour.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/Labour-Party-manifesto-2024.pdf"]," does not contain anything resembling an ambitious climate policy. Although Burnham represents a change at the top, he has not won the right to depart from the platform upon which Starmer was elected."]},{"k":"p","s":["Whether this represents a constraint on Burnham’s political vision or just more of the same on a limited climate policy is up for debate."]},{"k":"p","s":["The second is an economic bind due to the UK’s tight fiscal position. This is despite taxation being at a ",["historically high level","https://www.resolutionfoundation.org/publications/thin-end-of-the-wedge/"]," – much of which has come from ",["“fiscal drag”","https://commonslibrary.parliament.uk/research-briefings/cbp-9687/"]," as taxpayers are pulled into higher tax bands."]},{"k":"p","s":["The broader issues are that ten-year UK gilt yields – the rate the government pays on its debt – have risen to ",["5.13%","https://markets.ft.com/data/bonds/tearsheet/summary?s=UK10YG"],". The irony of the rise in gilt yields is that they have increased primarily because of “fossilflation” as supply-side shocks have fed into energy prices."]},{"k":"p","s":["As a result, the Bank of England has ",["raised interest rates","https://theconversation.com/interest-rates-are-making-uk-homes-less-affordable-even-as-wage-rises-increase-faster-than-house-prices-296075"]," for the first time in three years, to 4%. This will further increase borrowing costs and make life less affordable for UK households."]},{"k":"p","s":["And yet Labour’s propositions only put its climate policy into further doubt. It remains to be seen whether it will grant a licence for the Rosebank oil field, west of Shetland, which is larger than Jackdaw. Unless the government bends to political pressure, Burnham and energy secretary Miatta Fahnbulleh could make the same arguments about energy security again."]},{"k":"p","s":["In the meantime, Burnham has signalled his desire to raise tariffs on ",["Chinese green technology","https://www.telegraph.co.uk/news/2026/10/07/burnham-preparing-to-raise-chinese-ev-tariffs/"]," to align the UK more closely to the EU. This would be a bid to answer security worries, but tariffs on the cheapest and largest source of green technology places climate second to geopolitical concerns."]},{"k":"p","s":["Under Burnham, climate policy has, at best, been lost amid the prime minister’s broader political platform. At worst, he has concluded it is a price worth paying to achieve his other objectives."]}],"chars":5270},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/ghana":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T16:38Z","sha":"5e81061c12e683dcd672ac71e3d93e76a2e9810614ee0a9a118b2f1405eba95e","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/ghana","bytes":66018,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Ghana travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-03-20T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-11-04T17:07:08+00:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["Your travel insurance could be invalidated if you travel against advice from the Foreign, Commonwealth and Development Office (FCDO)."]},{"k":"h","s":["Areas where FCDO advises against all but essential travel"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Bawku Municipality"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the Bawku Municipal area in the Upper East region of Ghana."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out ",["why FCDO advises against travel to Bawku Municipality","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/ghana/regional-risks"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/ghana/email-signup"]," when this advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/travelaware/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of Ghana’s current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Ghana set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Ghana High Commission in the UK","https://www.ghanahighcommissionuk.com/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Ghana, your passport must have an expiry date at least 6 months after the date you arrive."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must have a visa to visit Ghana."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Applying for a visa"]},{"k":"p","s":["Complete the ",["online visa application form on the Ghana High Commission website","https://www.ghanahighcommissionuk.com/"]," and make the online payment."]},{"k":"p","s":["You need to upload your supporting documents (including a yellow fever certificate) and provide hard copies. Print out the form, add supporting documents and send them by post as directed on the website. The visa processing time is 10 to 15 days."]},{"k":"p","s":["To get a visa in around 3 days, check if you can use the express service available in person from the ",["Ghana Premium Application Centre in London","https://ghanahighcommissionuk.com/london-access-premium-centre"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Extending your visa"]},{"k":"p","s":["To extend your stay, take the ",["visa extension form","https://home.gis.gov.gh/gis-forms/"]," and photos in person to the Ghana Immigration Service (GIS) office on Independence Avenue in Accra."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Ghana, you must have a certificate to prove you’ve had a yellow fever vaccination."]},{"k":"p","s":["For full details about health entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Ghana guide","https://www.travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/89/ghana#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Ebola Screening"]},{"k":"p","s":["Additional screening for Ebola (Bundibugyo Virus) Disease is in place at border entry points into Ghana. International travellers must complete an online ",["Ghana Health Declaration","https://ehds.ghs.gov.gh/"]," before travel. You may also be required to undergo thermal screening and a travel history check on arrival."]},{"k":"p","s":["The World Health Organisation (WHO) has ",["declared this a Public Health Emergency of International Concern","https://www.who.int/news/item/17-05-2026-epidemic-of-ebola-disease-in-the-democratic-republic-of-the-congo-and-uganda-determined-a-public-health-emergency-of-international-concern"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Registering with the authorities"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you live in Ghana, you must register with the National Identification Authority (NIA) of Ghana and get a ",["non-citizen Ghana card","https://fims.org.gh/"],". You must register all foreign nationals aged 6 years and above in your family who are either:"]},{"k":"li","s":["permanently resident in Ghana"]},{"k":"li","s":["resident in Ghana for at least 90 days in any calendar year"]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about ",["goods you can take into or out of Ghana","https://gra.gov.gh/customs/"],". You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking money into Ghana"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must declare all hard currency, using the declaration form provided on arrival. You can bring in up to a maximum Ghanaian cedi equivalent of 10,000 US dollars."]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not carry more than 10,000 dollars in value in any foreign currency. The Ghanaian authorities can ",["confiscate the entire amount","https://www.accra-airport.com/en/customs_accra_airport.php"]," if you are carrying cash of this value or more."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationality"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ghana recognises dual nationality. Ghanaian-British dual nationals can register with the Interior Ministry in Ghana and get a dual nationality card. You can produce this card when entering Ghana to show that you do not need a visa."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"p","s":["This guide also has safety advice for ",["regions of Ghana","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/ghana/regional-risks"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Ghana"]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorist attacks in Ghana cannot be ruled out. Attacks could be indiscriminate, including in places visited by foreign nationals, such as:"]},{"k":"li","s":["northern border areas"]},{"k":"li","s":["busy public locations across the country, such as: beach resorts"]},{"k":"li","s":["hotels, cafes and restaurants"]},{"k":"li","s":["places of worship"]},{"k":"p","s":["Several terrorist groups operate in neighbouring Burkina Faso near to Ghana’s northern border, including Jama’a Nusrat ul-Islam wa al-Muslimin (JNIM) and Islamic State. JNIM regularly conducts attacks in southern Burkina Faso near to the Ghanaian border. There have also been JNIM attacks in the northern region of Togo, which borders Ghana to the east."]},{"k":"p","s":["Stay aware of your surroundings, keep up to date with local media reports, and follow the advice of local authorities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Political situation"]},{"k":"p","s":["Demonstrations in the capital Accra are normally well policed and peaceful, but sometimes they occur at short notice and can cause disruption. Protests may result in restriction of movement. Follow local media for updates on planned routes."]},{"k":"p","s":["Disputes can occur between local tribes. This can lead to inter-ethnic violence and civil unrest. Seek local advice and take precautions in areas where political tensions are heightened. If you encounter any type of demonstration or disturbance leave the area quickly and do not attempt to watch or photograph any demonstration or disturbance. See ",["Regional risks","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/ghana/regional-risks"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting yourself and your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["Cases of robbery, burglary and serious assault have become more common since 2021, and in some cases involve the use of weapons. Foreign nationals have been attacked and robbed at gunpoint. Street crime like pickpocketing and bag-snatching is on the increase in Accra. To reduce your personal risk:"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid carrying large sums of money or valuables"]},{"k":"li","s":["use a hotel safe to store passport and valuables whenever possible"]},{"k":"li","s":["be alert when withdrawing cash from ATMs, and where possible go by pre-arranged transport"]},{"k":"li","s":["be particularly careful after nightfall and avoid walking alone"]},{"k":"li","s":["take care of your belongings when arriving at and leaving hotels"]},{"k":"li","s":["keep a copy of your passport’s photo page and your visa or entry stamp in a separate place"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Safety at beaches"]},{"k":"p","s":["Theft is the main problem at beaches, but there have been isolated incidents of violent crime and sexual assault in areas popular with tourists. Do not visit beaches alone and take care on public beaches."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Safety at airports"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are reports of a small number of thefts of luggage and travel documents at Kotoka International Airport. Make sure your passport is always secure and do not leave your bags unattended. Be wary of offers of help except from uniformed porters or officials. All permanent staff at the airport wear an ID card showing their name and a photo. ID cards without a photo are not valid."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re being collected at the airport, confirm the identity of your driver by asking for ID. British nationals have been robbed by impostors who have approached them around the main arrivals area pretending to be their driver."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Accommodation security"]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been cases of burglaries in areas used by the international community, including Airport Residential, Cantonments, Ridge and Kokrobite, with greater frequency over the Christmas period. Make sure doors and windows are locked and keep all valuables in a secure lockbox. Set the burglar alarm if your accommodation has one."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Vehicle crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["Attacks on vehicles are increasing, sometimes involving the use of weapons. A British national died in one such attack in August 2021. Take particular care when your car or taxi is stationary in a busy area. Keep windows up and doors locked."]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been isolated incidents of crime taking place in all types of taxis, including licensed taxis, minibuses (‘tro tros’) and app-based taxi services. Use licensed taxis and check driver ID and the vehicle’s condition before you travel. Some hotels will book transport to pick you up on arrival. Avoid travelling alone in taxis after dark."]},{"k":"p","s":["Local police have highlighted the risk to vehicles on specific roads in Accra:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Graphic Road"]},{"k":"li","s":["George Walker Bush Highway"]},{"k":"li","s":["Accra Mall Roundabout"]},{"k":"li","s":["Awudome Cemetery Road"]},{"k":"li","s":["Pokuase-Amasaman Road"]},{"k":"li","s":["Teshie-Nungua Road"]},{"k":"li","s":["Labadi beach area"]},{"k":"li","s":["GIMPA road and surrounding areas"]},{"k":"li","s":["Kokrobite beach area"]},{"k":"p","s":["For longer trips outside major cities:"]},{"k":"li","s":["travel during daylight hours"]},{"k":"li","s":["travel in a convoy of at least 2 vehicles"]},{"k":"li","s":["get advice from local police"]},{"k":"li","s":["do not stop your vehicle if people at the roadside try to flag you down"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Criminal kidnap"]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been reports in the media of criminally motivated kidnapping in Accra, Takoradi and Kumasi, including the targeting of foreign nationals. Kidnaps can be for financial or political gain. If you’re kidnapped, the reason for your presence in Ghana is unlikely to serve as a protection or secure your safe release."]},{"k":"p","s":["The long-standing policy of the British government is not to make substantive concessions to hostage takers. The British government considers that paying ransoms and releasing prisoners increases the risk of further hostage-taking."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Scams"]},{"k":"p","s":["Scam artists target foreign visitors and residents. The scams come in many forms – romance and friendship, business ventures, work and employment opportunities – and can cause great financial loss. Warn your friends and family to be sceptical if they’re asked to transfer funds to you in Ghana. Tell them to contact you to check that you’ve made this request."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Bank card fraud"]},{"k":"p","s":["Keep your card in sight when paying bills and look closely when you use an ATM in case a skimming device has been attached to it."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ghana is a conservative and deeply religious country. Although attitudes are largely modern and progressive, you should show respect for traditional values and morals."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Dress code"]},{"k":"p","s":["Dress modestly in public. Shorts and t-shirts are acceptable for both males and females, but it is best not to wear anything too revealing."]},{"k":"p","s":["Wearing military clothing including camouflage is illegal."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is advisable to carry ID. A copy of your passport’s photo page is acceptable. Keep the original in a safe place such as a hotel safe."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs"]},{"k":"p","s":["The possession of Illegal drugs, including cannabis, carry severe penalties."]},{"k":"p","s":["Bail is not normally granted."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should expect a long jail sentence and heavy fines for possessing, using or smuggling illegal drugs, including when transiting through the airport."]},{"k":"p","s":["Even possession of small amounts of cannabis can lead to a prison sentence of more than 5 years, usually after a long and expensive legal process."]},{"k":"p","s":["Airports in Ghana have excellent technology and security for detecting illegal items. This is also used to scan the baggage of transiting passengers."]},{"k":"p","s":["Class A drugs like cocaine are likely to be laced with other substances. Foreign visitors, including British nationals, have died after taking these drugs."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Using cameras in secure areas"]},{"k":"p","s":["Photography near sensitive sites like military installations or the airport is illegal. Ask permission if you want to take a photograph of a building where there are guards on duty. Beware of self-appointed officials trying to charge fees to let you take pictures of well-known sites of interest."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Some same-sex sexual acts could lead to a prison sentence of between 3 and 25 years. Although there are no records of this being enforced, there were arrests at a gathering of the LGBT+ community in 2021. Ghanaian society is intolerant of people of the same sex showing affection in public. Many Ghanaians do not accept that such relationships exist."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Human Sexual Rights and Family Values Bill is not law, but its passage through Ghana’s Parliament could increase the risk of violence and other threats (such as blackmail and intimidation) to the LGBT+ community and their allies. Rhetoric by some politicians, religious leaders, and local media can incite violence and psychological abuse of the LGBT+ community. FCDO are aware of reported attacks against LGBT+ individuals."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Family law in Ghana"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ghanaian family law is very different from UK law, particularly when child custody becomes an issue. Ghana is not a signatory to the Hague Convention. This means:"]},{"k":"li","s":["the custody process might not be as straightforward as in cases where both countries are signatories"]},{"k":"li","s":["you might need to initiate legal proceedings in Ghana for custody or to have your child returned to the UK"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Money"]},{"k":"p","s":["While ATMs are common in large towns, they may not be available in rural areas. Many hotels, guesthouses and shops accept credit cards except for Mastercard, which is not widely accepted. Check ahead that you can make payment, and have back-up funds."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your card issuer before you travel in case they put a block on your account."]},{"k":"h","s":["Outdoor activities and adventure tourism"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Swimming safety"]},{"k":"p","s":["Swimming is dangerous on the beaches along the southern coast of Ghana due to rip tides and undertows. There are occasional reports of deaths of both adults and children."]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["water safety on holiday","https://www.rlss.org.uk/safety-on-holiday"]," from the Royal Life Saving Society."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can drive in Ghana using the ",["1949 version of the international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," or a Ghanaian driving licence. Carry your driving documents with you."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Driving standards"]},{"k":"p","s":["Roads can be in a poor condition, particularly in rural areas. Grass or leaves strewn in the road often mean there is an accident or other hazard ahead."]},{"k":"p","s":["Street lighting is poor or non-existent. Avoid travelling by road outside the main towns after dark, when the risk of serious road accidents is much greater, and there is a heightened risk of attacks on vehicles (see the crime section). If you choose to drive at night be aware of impromptu police checkpoints. Do not give cash to the police as this can be perceived as a bribe."]},{"k":"p","s":["Safety standards of taxi services in Ghana are low. Driver training and vehicle standards will vary from providers in the UK. Drivers of ‘tro-tros’ and popular app-based taxi services are not centrally licensed. There is no responsible body that is accountable for your safety."]},{"k":"p","s":["Outside major towns and cities it’s safer to use pre-booked vehicles from reputable taxi companies."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to prepare for and respond to ",["extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Flooding"]},{"k":"p","s":["Flooding is common in the Upper West, North East, Northern and Savannah regions during the rainy season, from March to November."]},{"k":"p","s":["Heavy rainfall can also cause flooding in other parts of Ghana, including urban areas such as Accra and its surroundings. Flooding can disrupt road travel, public transport, electricity and other services, and conditions can change quickly following periods of intense rainfall."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow the advice of local authorities, monitor local weather reports and expect difficulties when travelling to affected areas."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Earthquakes"]},{"k":"p","s":["Earthquakes and tremors are a risk in Ghana. The US Federal Emergency Management Agency website has advice about ",["what to do before, during and after an earthquake","https://www.ready.gov/earthquakes"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Regional risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["This section has safety advice for regions of Ghana. It only covers regions where FCDO has specific advice."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should also read ",["FCDO’s overall travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/ghana"]," and ",["safety and security advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/ghana/safety-and-security"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Civil unrest in specific local regions of Ghana can build up at short notice and may become violent, sometimes involving weapons. Avoid large crowds and political protests. Take local advice if you’re in an area with heightened political tension. Local police may impose curfews to contain the situation. Curfews usually run from 7pm to 5am but times can vary. The authorities may put out a press release which is usually posted on the ",["Ministry of the Interior’s website","https://www.mint.gov.gh/category/press-release/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Bawku Municipality"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the Bawku Municipal area in the Upper East region of Ghana. This is due to the number of violent incidents. The Ghanaian military have deployed additional military to the region to strengthen security."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you must travel to Bawku, you are strongly advised to contact the regional police headquarters in Bolgatanga town before travelling. Frequent curfews have been put in place in Bawku, with requirements and times changing. Security checks, including roadblocks, are often in effect and you should be prepared to show identification if asked. Be prepared for the security response to change without notice."]},{"k":"p","s":["Since October there have been a number of attacks related to the conflict in Bawku on the Nasia -Walewale-Bolgatanga road (Northeast) and the Bolgatanga- Zebilla – Bawku – Pulmankom road (Upper East). Many people are arranging police escorts when travelling along these roads. British citizens should take this into consideration including any precautionary measures before deciding to travel along these roads."]},{"k":"h","s":["Savannah Region"]},{"k":"p","s":["In August, tribal conflict broke out in the western part of Savannah Region, near the Cote d’Ivoire and Burkina Faso borders. This has resulted in a number of deaths and displacement of communities. Visitors travelling in that region should keep informed about the situation, seek local advice and take precautions."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Call 999 or 112 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Ghana","https://www.travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/89/ghana#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Ghana","https://www.travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/89/ghana"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["yellow fever"]},{"k":"li","s":["malaria"]},{"k":"li","s":["dengue"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Marburg virus"]},{"k":"p","s":["In September 2022, Ghana declared an end to the Marburg virus disease outbreak that was first reported in July 2022. See ",["more details about the outbreak","https://www.who.int/emergencies/disease-outbreak-news/item/2022-DON409"]," and ",["more information on Marburg virus and similar diseases","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/68/viral-haemorrhagic-fever"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Ghana"]},{"k":"p","s":["Medical facilities are poor outside towns. For serious medical treatment, medical evacuation will be necessary. Make sure you have adequate travel health insurance and accessible funds to cover the cost of any medical treatment abroad and repatriation."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a ",["list of medical providers in Ghana","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/ghana-list-of-medical-facilities"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Ghana"]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone:"]},{"k":"li","s":["999 or 112 (ambulance, fire, police, coast guard and mountain rescue)"]},{"k":"li","s":["192 (police)"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Ghana"]," and ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Ghana"]," in Ghana"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Ghana","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/ghana-bereavement-information"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested or imprisoned in Ghana","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/ghana-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/ghana/british-high-commission-accra"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/ghana/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in Ghana","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-ghana"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":21657,"change":"Updated information about Ebola screening in Ghana (‘Entry requirements’ page)."},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/laos":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T17:03Z","sha":"ad98b4b3e727ad7c52455482cda5347648bde44cb89c391bfd0342191a165613","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/laos","bytes":78924,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Laos travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-01-25T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-08-13T12:10:25+01:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["Your travel insurance could be invalidated if you travel against advice from the Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO)."]},{"k":"h","s":["Areas where FCDO advises against all but essential travel"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Xaisomboun Province"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to Xaisomboun Province. There are intermittent attacks on infrastructure and armed clashes with anti-government groups."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["why FCDO advises against travel","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/laos/regional-risks"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Global travel impacts due to escalation in the Middle East"]},{"k":"p","s":["Escalation in the Middle East has caused widespread travel disruption, including airspace closures, delayed and cancelled flights."]},{"k":"p","s":["Your travel plans may be affected, even if your destination is not in the Middle East. Before you travel:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check travel advice for any countries or territories you are transiting through"]},{"k":"li","s":["check for the latest updates from your airline or tour operator"]},{"k":"li","s":["review your travel insurance policy for coverage"]},{"k":"li","s":["monitor local and international media for the latest information and sign up for travel advice email alerts"]},{"k":"li","s":["be mindful of your permitted length of stay in Laos, extend visa if necessary, and see ",["visa extensions on Entry requirements page","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/laos/entry-requirements"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Land borders and crossing with Thailand and Cambodia"]},{"k":"p","s":["In July 2025, Thailand and Cambodia fought along parts of the border. The fighting included the use of rocket and artillery fire. Tensions remain and fighting erupted again at various points along the border in December. Land borders and crossings between Thailand and Cambodia continue to be suspended. Some tourist destinations in border areas such as the Khao Phra Wihan/Preah Vihear temple, the Ta Kwai/Ta Krabey temple and the Ta Muen Thom/Tamone Thom temple are closed."]},{"k":"p","s":["There are also unexploded landmines in the border area."]},{"k":"p","s":["British nationals in Southern Laos travelling to Cambodia or Thailand, should carefully consider which land border crossings to use. British nationals should also carefully consider any travel they have planned close to the Lao border adjoining the affected areas."]},{"k":"p","s":["See our travel advice for ",["Thailand","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/thailand"]," and ",["Cambodia","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/cambodia"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/laos/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of Laos’s current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Laos set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, send a message to the ",["Lao Embassy London Facebook page","https://www.facebook.com/LaoEmbassyLondon/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Laos, your passport must have an ‘expiry date’ at least 6 months after the date you arrive and at least 2 blank pages."]},{"k":"p","s":["Airlines will only let you board your flight if your passport has enough blank pages."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider to make sure your passport and other travel documents meet their requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Digital Arrival/Departure Cards - Lao Digital Immigration Form (LDIF)"]},{"k":"p","s":["All foreign nationals entering Laos are required to complete the ",["LDIF","https://www.immigration.gov.la/en/home"]," digitally within 3 days before arrival and 3 days before departure."]},{"k":"p","s":["The LDIF applies at Wattay International Airport (Vientiane), Luang Prabang International Airport, Pakse International Airport and Lao-Thai Friendship Bridge I. At these checkpoints, the LDIF replaces paper arrival and departure cards."]},{"k":"p","s":["The LDIF does not replace visa requirements."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must have a visa to visit Laos."]},{"k":"p","s":["To work, study and travel for business or other reasons, you must meet the ",["Lao immigration department’s entry requirements","https://immigration.gov.la/en/home"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Applying for a visa"]},{"k":"p","s":["From 1 January 2025, tourist visas reverted to the previous 30 days from the date you arrive in Laos."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can ",["apply online for a Laos e-visa","https://laoevisa.gov.la/index"]," – apply at least 5 days in advance. The e-visa is single entry only and is accepted at major entry points."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can also get a visa on arrival (single entry) at many entry points, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Vientiane Wattay airport"]},{"k":"li","s":["Luang Prabang airport"]},{"k":"li","s":["Pakske airport"]},{"k":"p","s":["See a full ",["list of the entry points that accept e-visas and visas on arrival","https://immigration.gov.la/en/checkpoints/category/category/?limit=12&offset=0&category=international-border-checkpoint"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Visa extensions"]},{"k":"p","s":["From 1 January 2025, you’re allowed to ",["extend your tourist visa","https://immigration.gov.la/en/services/1"]," twice while in Laos, for a total of 60 additional days."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you do not extend your visa within 90 days, you will face a fine in Lao kip worth 2,000 US dollars, deportation to your home country and a ban on returning to Laos."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["For details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Laos guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/124/laos#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about goods you can take into or out of Laos. You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Laos"]},{"k":"p","s":["Although there’s no recent history of terrorism in Laos, attacks cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"h","s":["Political situation"]},{"k":"p","s":["Specific events or political disputes may trigger violent protests. You should avoid any demonstrations or large gatherings of people. Keep yourself informed of local developments."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting yourself and your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["Petty crime can occur in tourist areas and around ATMs. Try to have someone with you and do not carry your bank cards and cash in the same bag. Keep a copy of your passport somewhere safe."]},{"k":"p","s":["Travellers regularly report random bag snatches, often by people on motorcycles. Hold your bags on the side away from the road, and do not have valuables on display."]},{"k":"p","s":["People have reported incidents where they are approached and followed when alone. Be alert to your surroundings, trust your instincts and if you think you’re being followed move to an area where there are other people. Consider sharing your planned route in advance and avoid quiet or less-travelled areas."]},{"k":"p","s":["Safes in hotels and guesthouses are not necessarily secure. Use your own lock where possible. Take care of your possessions if you’re travelling overnight on public transport."]},{"k":"p","s":["Be particularly careful travelling at night by bicycle or motorcycle. Stick to well-used, well-lit roads and carry a personal alarm if possible, especially if you’re alone."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Sexual assault"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a risk of harassment when travelling alone. We recommend you use a known taxi service; one booked by your accommodation or one of the local taxi apps. You should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["confirm the driver’s identity and license plate matches when the vehicle arrives"]},{"k":"li","s":["share your journey details with a friend or use the apps sharing feature if available"]},{"k":"li","s":["be wary of drivers claiming to be registered with app companies and trying to pick up passengers on the street"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Motorcycle scams"]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not leave your passport as a deposit or guarantee when hiring motorcycles. There have been reports of rental companies arranging for their motorcycles to be deliberately stolen or damaged, then keeping passports and demanding high fees. Make sure your travel insurance covers medical and other costs that arise from motorcycle accidents."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Reporting a crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["Call the Tourist Police in Vientiane on 021 251 128."]},{"k":"p","s":["Local law enforcement responses to crimes, even violent crimes, are often limited. Foreigners attempting to report crimes have reported finding police stations closed, emergency telephone numbers unanswered, or police with no transport or authorisation to investigate crimes at night. If the police do attend, they may ask you to pay fuel and telephone costs. Ask the staff at your accommodation for help with reporting a crime."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Drink and food spiking"]},{"k":"p","s":["Both male and female tourists have reported having their drink or food spiked with drugs and in some cases been assaulted. Never leave food or drink unattended. Be cautious about accepting drinks from strangers at bars, clubs, restaurants and parties."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Methanol poisoning"]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been deaths and cases of serious illness caused by alcoholic drinks containing methanol in Laos."]},{"k":"p","s":["Methanol poisoning cases have resulted from drinks purchased in licensed bars, shops and hotels in tourist areas. Laos authorities have issued an order prohibiting the sale and consumption of Tiger Vodka and Tiger Whisky due to concerns about them being a risk to health."]},{"k":"p","s":["Even small amounts of methanol can kill. It is not possible to identify methanol in alcoholic drinks by taste or smell. See ",["Travel Aware Spiking and methanol poisoning","https://travelaware.campaign.gov.uk/spiking-and-methanol-poisoning/"]," for information about how to reduce the risks."]},{"k":"p","s":["Seek urgent medical attention if you or someone you are travelling with show the ",["signs of methanol poisoning","https://travelaware.campaign.gov.uk/spiking-and-methanol-poisoning/"]," after drinking."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Legal system"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Lao legal system operates differently from the UK, and the standard of prisons is very poor."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are under criminal investigation, you can be detained for long periods without evidence or official charges. There can be long delays before you can contact lawyers, British Embassy officials or family. Legal representation is far below UK standards."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs and the death penalty"]},{"k":"p","s":["Possession, trafficking and manufacture of any illegal drugs are serious offences in Laos. This includes cannabis. British nationals have been caught carrying cannabis while transiting through Laos."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Laos authorities have a zero-tolerance policy to drug offences. Possessing drugs, even in very small quantities, carries severe penalties, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["arrest and detention"]},{"k":"li","s":["a long jail sentence if charged and convicted"]},{"k":"li","s":["a possible death penalty for drug trafficking"]},{"k":"p","s":["Legal processes before court hearings can be long and expensive. It can take many months for a case to go to trial."]},{"k":"p","s":["Criminal gangs in the UK and elsewhere are known to coerce people into carrying drugs across borders. Do not allow yourself to be persuaded."]},{"k":"p","s":["Airports in Laos have security equipment and procedures in place for scanning and detecting illegal substances, including cannabis. This is also used to scan the carry-on and checked-in baggage of transiting passengers."]},{"k":"p","s":["It is important to be aware of your rights if you are detained by the police. See our ",["guidance for those detained or imprisoned in Laos","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/laos-prisoner-pack"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Police often raid venues known to be frequented by foreigners. You may have to take a urine or blood test if there is a suspicion you have used drugs. You will be arrested if the test is positive."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Using cameras and binoculars in secure areas"]},{"k":"p","s":["Photographing or entering any military site without an official invitation is prohibited and you may be arrested or detained. Avoid photographing bridges or airfields."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Getting permission for special travel projects"]},{"k":"p","s":["You should get permission from the local district authorities for any travel seen as out of the ordinary, such as extensive photography, or scientific research of any kind."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Relationships with Lao nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Lao government prohibits sexual relationships between foreign and Lao nationals, except when the parties have been married in accordance with Lao family law. You must ask permission for marriage or engagement to a Lao national in a formal application to the Lao authorities."]},{"k":"p","s":["Penalties for failing to register such a relationship can be up to 5,000 US dollars fine and possible imprisonment. It is not unknown for Lao authorities to demand entry into hotel rooms or guesthouses where they suspect this regulation is being broken."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Smoking and e-cigarette bans"]},{"k":"p","s":["While cigarettes are common, the use of e-cigarettes (vapes), heated tobacco and shisha (water-pipe tobacco) are illegal. You could be fined or imprisoned for possessing, using them, importing, selling, purchasing or exporting them."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Dress codes"]},{"k":"p","s":["When you visit any temples and religious sites, your shoulders and knees should be covered, whether you are male or female."]},{"k":"p","s":["It is not culturally appropriate to walk around in public wearing swimming costumes after leaving waterfalls, rivers or swimming pools."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are no legal restrictions on same-sex sexual relations in Laos. Proud To Be Us Laos raises awareness about LGBT+ rights and HIV/AIDS among the LGBT+ community. More information can be found on the ",["Proud To Be Us Laos Facebook page","https://www.facebook.com/proudtobeuslaos/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Outdoor activities and adventure tourism"]},{"k":"p","s":["Safety and maintenance may not meet the standards you find in the UK. Risks include:"]},{"k":"li","s":["remote areas that are difficult for rescue services to reach"]},{"k":"li","s":["flooding, swollen rivers and landslides, especially during the rainy season"]},{"k":"li","s":["lower standards than in the UK"]},{"k":"hs","s":["River rafting and other water activities"]},{"k":"p","s":["Activities such as white-water rafting, kayaking, tubing and swimming, particularly in the Mekong River, can carry significant risks, including strong currents and hidden obstacles. There have been incidents of drowning and serious injuries involving tourists."]},{"k":"p","s":["Safety standards vary widely. Operators may not provide adequate safety advice, and there may not be warning signs for dangerous currents or other hazards. Stay alert and check that lifejackets are provided."]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["water safety on holiday","https://www.rlss.org.uk/safety-on-holiday"]," from the Royal Life Saving Society."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Extreme or adventure sports, including paragliding/motoring, climbing, off-road driving and hot air ballooning"]},{"k":"p","s":["Be aware equipment may not meet UK safety and insurance standards."]},{"k":"p","s":["Make sure:"]},{"k":"li","s":["you use reputable properly insured operators and insist on training"]},{"k":"li","s":["adequate safety precautions are in place"]},{"k":"li","s":["your travel insurance covers all the activities you want to undertake"]},{"k":"li","s":["you read the contract you are offered and be clear about who is responsible for all parts of the venture."]},{"k":"li","s":["if you choose an organisation that prepares properly, you are more likely to stay safe"]},{"k":"h","s":["Travelling within Laos"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Laos, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You’ll need to have both the ",["1949 version of the international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," and your UK driving licence with you in the car. You cannot buy an IDP outside the UK, so get one before you travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["Police may stop your car at any time, particularly in the evening, and ask for ID. You should stop at checkpoints and roadblocks unless you are waved on."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Driving conditions"]},{"k":"p","s":["Roads in Laos are often in poor condition and vehicles may not be maintained to UK standards. Travel after dark significantly increases the risk of an accident, as vehicles often do not have lights. Livestock, including water buffalo, also stray onto roads, creating hazards for motorists."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road accidents and safety"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re involved in a road accident, you will have to pay compensation for third-party property damage and injury, even if you’re not at fault. Generally, the Lao authorities will find in favour of Lao citizens, regardless of the situation. Lao insurers typically only cover a small proportion of accident costs and do not provide broader compensation."]},{"k":"p","s":["Motorbike rentals may not supply helmets, so you may need to bring your own or purchase one locally. Take extra care when using public transport or shared vehicles, as they can be overcrowded and unsafe. You can report road accidents to a dedicated police number +856 20 5666 9090."]},{"k":"hs","s":["China-Laos Expressway"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Vientiane to Vang Vieng section of the China-Laos Expressway is the first contained high-speed road in Laos, with posted speed limits between 80 and 120km/h. Take care when using this road, as some local users will be unfamiliar with this type of carriageway."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel by Boat or Ferry"]},{"k":"p","s":["Travel on the Mekong River can be dangerous due to changing water levels, strong currents, and hidden obstacles. There have been incidents of boating and ferry accidents. Vessel safety standards vary widely and operators may not provide adequate safety advice. Stay alert, ensure boats are equipped with life jackets and avoid boarding overcrowded vessels."]},{"k":"h","s":["Landmines and unexploded weapons"]},{"k":"p","s":["Landmines and other unexploded weapons are a hazard throughout Laos and kill a number of people each year. Keep to main routes in rural areas, and do not pick up metal objects. This risk is higher after flash floods or landslides during the monsoon season."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to ",["prepare for and respond to extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Monsoon"]},{"k":"p","s":["The rainy season in Laos normally runs from May to October, at the same time as the typhoon season in south-east Asia. During this period river levels can can increase dramatically within hours and heavy rainstorms may cause unexpected and serious flooding. Be aware of local advice, social media coverage and follow the advice of the local authorities."]},{"k":"p","s":["Travel to some provinces can be seriously disrupted during this time. Mountain areas are vulnerable to landslides in the rainy season and the Mekong’s river basins and surrounding areas are likely to be flooded. Meteorologists predict that tropical storms could be more forceful and more frequent in the future, this can amplify monsoon storms and rainfall. Away from river basins there is a high risk of flash flooding causing falling trees, damage to buildings and transport infrastructure; be aware landslides may expose undiscovered UXO."]},{"k":"p","s":["During the monsoon season local road transport is often disrupted due to conditions. Cross country journeys can often take substantially longer than posted schedules and have limited mobile phone coverage. Travel with extra water and food supplies."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Mekong River Commission posts ",["official updates on the Mekong River","https://webarchive.nationalarchives.gov.uk/ukgwa/20250801154111mp_/http://ffw.mrcmekong.org/"],". Travel to some provinces can be seriously disrupted during this time. Monitor local news and check ",["World Meteorological Organization weather reports","https://webarchive.nationalarchives.gov.uk/ukgwa/20250801154111mp_/https://worldweather.wmo.int/en/country.html?countryCode=121"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Regional risks"]},{"k":"h","s":["Regional risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["This section has safety advice for regions of Laos. It only covers regions where FCDO has specific advice."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should also read ",["FCDO’s overall travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/laos"]," and ",["safety and security advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/laos/safety-and-security"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Xaisomboun Province"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to Xaisomboun Province. There were reports in 2021 of attacks on infrastructure and armed clashes with anti-government groups in the province. There could be more skirmishes."]},{"k":"h","s":["Borders with Thailand and Myanmar (Golden Triangle)"]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been small-scale clashes between anti-government groups and government troops in isolated areas along the Laos-Thailand border. The local law enforcement agencies have limited capability to counter these threats."]},{"k":"p","s":["Be extremely cautious in Bokeo Province, particularly near the borders with Myanmar and Thailand, and around the Golden Triangle Special Economic Zone. Armed groups carry out employment scams and drug trafficking in this area."]},{"k":"p","s":["Recent clashes in this area between the Lao army and unidentified armed groups has led to increased security levels with associated military checkpoints. Make yourself aware of local official guidance and be prepared to reconsider travel plans to this area."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical numbers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Dial 1195 or 030 525 7239 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Voluntary ambulance services also operate in Vientiane free of charge."]},{"k":"p","s":["Vientiane Rescue: 1623 or (0)20 5666 8825"]},{"k":"p","s":["Lao Red Cross Rescue: (0)20 5996 6111 or (0)20 2200 5563"]},{"k":"p","s":["Make sure anyone attending an accident is wearing a uniform marked ‘Vientiane Rescue’ or ‘Lao Red Cross’. There have been reports of bogus companies attending accidents and trying to charge fees."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Laos","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/124/laos#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Laos","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/124/laos#General_Information"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Mosquito-borne diseases"]},{"k":"p","s":["The rainy season sees an increase in dengue cases. Dengue and malaria are endemic, so you should increase precautions to ",["avoid being bitten by mosquitoes","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/38/insect-and-tick-bite-avoidance"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Anthrax"]},{"k":"p","s":["Anthrax has been found in cattle and buffalo near the tourist areas of 4,000 Islands, Pakse and the Bolaven Plateau. Anthrax is a serious disease that can be transmitted to humans. Avoid contact with cattle and buffalo and make sure meat is thoroughly cooked. Seek medical attention if you are exposed to infected animals or show symptoms."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Air pollution"]},{"k":"p","s":["Regional air pollution can be a problem in Laos and may aggravate heart, lung or respiratory conditions. Children, the elderly and those with pre-existing medical conditions may be especially affected. You can read guidance on ",["how to cope with air pollution","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/disease/219/outdoor-air-quality"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["International clinics, large hospitals and larger pharmacies in Laos can supply most prescription medication. In remoter areas this may be more difficult."]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Laos"]},{"k":"p","s":["Medical care in Laos can be basic and outside the capital there are no reliable facilities to deal with medical emergencies. Medical evacuation is difficult to organise and very expensive. Make sure you have adequate travel health insurance and accessible funds to cover the cost of any medical treatment abroad and repatriation."]},{"k":"p","s":["You may be asked to pay for an ambulance and any treatment you need in advance. Make sure you get a receipt to use for insurance claims."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a list of ",["medical providers in Laos","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/laos-list-of-medical-facilities"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is also ",["guidance on healthcare if you’re living in Laos","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/living-in-laos#healthcare-in-laos"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Laos"]},{"k":"p","s":["Fire: 1190"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police: 1191"]},{"k":"p","s":["Alternative numbers for police stations: 241162, 241163, 241164, and 212703"]},{"k":"p","s":["Tourist police in Vientiane: 021 251 128"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ambulance: 1195 or 030 525 7239"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Laos"],", ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Laos"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=Laos"]," in Laos"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Laos","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/bereavement-information-for-laos"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested or imprisoned in Laos","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/laos-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/laos/british-embassy-vientiane"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/laos/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]}],"chars":24673,"change":"Updated information on flooding risks during periods of heavy rain (‘Safety and security’ page)."},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/philippines":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T17:18Z","sha":"2fd696bf7028d23c2a4623758e3ba1bd6d5ebd0aa3cc9b0e89c4dbf698116690","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/philippines","bytes":92709,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Philippines travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-03-06T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-07-15T09:55:25+01:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["Your travel insurance could be invalidated if you travel against advice from the Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO)."]},{"k":"h","s":["Areas where FCDO advises against travel"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Mindanao and the Sulu archipelago"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to western and central Mindanao and the Sulu archipelago."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO also advises against all but essential travel to the remainder of Mindanao, except for:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Camiguin Island"]},{"k":"li","s":["Dinagat Island"]},{"k":"li","s":["Siargao Island"]},{"k":"p","s":["This advice is due to terrorist activity and clashes between the military and insurgent groups in south Philippines."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["why FCDO advises against travel","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/philippines/safety-and-security#terrorism"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Typhoons"]},{"k":"p","s":["Around 20 typhoons hit the Philippines each year. Most typhoons happen between June and November. Follow the advice of local authorities, and monitor the progress of storms on the Philippines state weather agency and the Philippines Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Council. You can find updates on typhoon2000.ph, or follow ",["@Typhoon2k","https://twitter.com/Typhoon2k"]," on X."]},{"k":"h","s":["Global travel impacts due to escalation in the Middle East"]},{"k":"p","s":["Escalation in the Middle East has caused widespread travel disruption, including airspace closures, delayed and cancelled flights."]},{"k":"p","s":["Commercial options to depart the Philippines remain available, but your travel plans may be affected, even if your destination is not in the Middle East. Before you travel:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check travel advice for any countries or territories you are transiting through"]},{"k":"li","s":["check for the latest updates from your airline or tour operator"]},{"k":"li","s":["review your travel insurance policy for coverage"]},{"k":"li","s":["monitor local and international media for the latest information and sign up for travel advice email alerts"]},{"k":"h","s":["Demonstrations"]},{"k":"p","s":["Large-scale demonstrations are expected over the coming weeks in Metro Manila and elsewhere in the Philippines."]},{"k":"p","s":["Avoid all demonstrations and large gatherings and follow the advice of local authorities. Demonstrations may lead to travel disruption. You should allow extra time for journeys and monitor local media for updates."]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["Safety and security","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/philippines/safety-and-security"]," for more information on demonstrations and rallies in the Philippines."]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/philippines/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of the Philippines’ rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in the Philippines set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Philippine Embassy in the UK","https://londonpe.dfa.gov.ph/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter the Philippines, your passport must have an ‘expiry date’ at least 6 months after the date you arrive."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can visit the Philippines without a visa for tourism or business for up to 30 days."]},{"k":"p","s":["You must have a QR code to show that you have registered on the ",["e-travel system","https://etravel.gov.ph/"]," within the 72 hours before your arrival in the Philippines. Some airlines will not allow you to board your flight to the Philippines if you cannot show the QR code."]},{"k":"p","s":["The e-travel registration is free of charge."]},{"k":"p","s":["Most UK visitors are also expected to have proof of return or onward travel. Immigration officials and airlines may ask for this."]},{"k":"p","s":["To stay more than 30 days, you can ",["apply for an extension","https://e-services.immigration.gov.ph/Dashboard/Index"]," when you are in the Philippines. If you overstay any visa without authority, it is a serious matter. You could face fees and fines, and detention if you cannot pay them, or you could be deported at your own expense."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you want a visa to live, work, or study in the Philippines, you’ll need to meet the requirements of the Philippine immigration regulations. This includes having certain UK documents (birth certificates, marriage certificates, UK police certificates and school documents) ",["legalised by the Legalisation Office","https://www.gov.uk/get-document-legalised"]," (not by the Philippine Embassy in London)."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Children travelling without their parents"]},{"k":"p","s":["If your non-Filipino children aged 14 or under are travelling without either parent, you must apply for a ",["waiver of exclusion ground","https://londonpe.dfa.gov.ph/consular-matters/forms"]," for entry into the Philippines."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter the Philippines, you must have certificates to prove you’ve had:"]},{"k":"li","s":["a yellow fever vaccination if you’re coming from a ",["country listed as a transmission risk","https://nathnacyfzone.org.uk/factsheet/65/countries-with-risk-of-yellow-fever-transmission"]]},{"k":"li","s":["a polio vaccine if you are coming from certain countries with a transmission risk"]},{"k":"p","s":["For full details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Philippines guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/178/philippines#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about ",["goods you can take into or out of the Philippines","https://customs.gov.ph/home/traveler-homepage/"],". You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking money into the Philippines"]},{"k":"p","s":["You cannot take in more than 50,000 Philippine pesos."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are bringing in foreign currency (cash or cheques) worth more than 10,000 US dollars, you must declare it on your foreign currency declaration form on arrival."]},{"k":"h","s":["Exit requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you have stayed in the Philippines for 6 months or more on a tourist visa, you must get an ",["emigration clearance certificate","https://e-services.immigration.gov.ph/Dashboard/Index?ReturnUrl=%2FEmigrationClearanceCertificateB"]," (ECC) during the 72 hours before you leave the country."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you were in the Philippines on a visa issued by the Department of Justice (DoJ), the Board of Investments (BoI), or the Philippine Economic Zone Authority (PEZA), you will need a travel pass from the department that issued your visa to leave the Philippines. If you have an ECC, you do not need a travel pass."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Airport tax"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re leaving the country from Cebu Mactan airport, you must pay a departure tax of 850 Philippine pesos in local currency or the equivalent in US dollars. There’s no longer a departure tax at Manila airport. This information can change and you should check with your airline before you travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in the Philippines"]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorists are very likely to try to carry out attacks in the Philippines."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to western and central Mindanao and the Sulu archipelago."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO also advises against all but essential travel to the remainder of Mindanao, except for:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Camiguin Island"]},{"k":"li","s":["Dinagat Island"]},{"k":"li","s":["Siargao Island"]},{"k":"p","s":["This advice is due to terrorist activity and clashes between the military and insurgent groups in south Philippines."]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorist attacks occur frequently in Mindanao and the Sulu Archipelago. While attacks primarily target Filipino security forces, certain groups operating in these regions have pledged allegiance to Daesh and have targeted religious groups. Terrorist groups may also consider westerners as legitimate targets for an attack."]},{"k":"p","s":["There are multiple terrorist and militant groups operating in the Philippines, including the Abu Sayyaf Group (ASG), Islamic State Philippines (IS-Philippines), the Bangsamoro Islamic Freedom Fighters (BIFF)."]},{"k":"p","s":["Multiple terrorist groups have the intent to carry out attacks anywhere in the Philippines, including in the capital Manila. Terrorism attacks could be indiscriminate, including in places visited by foreign nationals, such as:"]},{"k":"li","s":["shopping malls"]},{"k":"li","s":["entertainment establishments"]},{"k":"li","s":["public transport, including airports and the metro system"]},{"k":"li","s":["places of worship"]},{"k":"p","s":["Previous significant incidents include:"]},{"k":"li","s":["in December 2023, 4 people were killed and several injured in an explosion during a Catholic mass in Marawi, South Lanao Province"]},{"k":"li","s":["in August 2020, dual explosions in Jolo Island, Sulu Province resulted in a number of deaths and injuries"]},{"k":"li","s":["in 2019, a dual suicide attack on a military base in Indanan, Sulu Province killed 3 civilians and 3 military personnel as well as the 2 attackers, with a further 22 people injured"]},{"k":"li","s":["in 2019, 27 people were killed and many more injured as a result of bomb attacks at a Roman Catholic cathedral on Jolo Island, Sulu Province"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorist kidnapping"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a threat of kidnapping by terrorist groups operating in the Philippines, including the targeting of foreign nationals in rural, urban and coastal areas throughout Mindanao especially in the Sulu Archipelago and the Zamboanga Peninsula."]},{"k":"p","s":["A number of Westerners have been kidnapped in recent years, including British Nationals in 2019."]},{"k":"p","s":["British nationals are seen as legitimate targets, including tourists, humanitarian aid workers, journalists, and business travellers. If you are kidnapped, the reason for your presence is unlikely to protect you or secure your safe release."]},{"k":"p","s":["The long-standing policy of the British government is not to make substantive concessions to hostage takers. The British government considers that paying ransoms and releasing prisoners builds the capability of terrorist groups and finances their activities. This can, in turn, increase the risk of further hostage-taking. The Terrorism Act (2000) makes payments to terrorists illegal."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are high levels of street crime and robbery, sometimes involving weapons and firearms."]},{"k":"p","s":["Be alert when travelling on public transport and avoid displaying cash or jewellery. Armed hold-ups on ‘jeepneys’ and buses can happen, particularly in Manila and other large cities. In some cases these have resulted in fatalities."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re travelling by taxi, including to or from the airport, only use taxis from a reputable company. Some taxi drivers and their accomplices have robbed and harmed passengers. Consider arranging to be met at the airport or using a hotel transfer service."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Methanol poisoning"]},{"k":"p","s":["There has been an increase in cases of serious illness caused by alcoholic drinks containing methanol in popular travel destinations around the world."]},{"k":"p","s":["Even small amounts of methanol can kill. It is not possible to identify methanol in alcoholic drinks by taste or smell. See ",["Travel Aware Drink Spiking and Methanol Poisoning","https://travelaware.campaign.gov.uk/spiking-and-methanol-poisoning/"]," for information about how to reduce the risks."]},{"k":"p","s":["Seek urgent medical attention if you or someone you are travelling with show the ",["signs of methanol poisoning","https://travelaware.campaign.gov.uk/spiking-and-methanol-poisoning/"]," after drinking."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Sexual assault"]},{"k":"p","s":["British nationals have reported rape and sexual assaults in some locations popular with backpackers, including Coron and Siargao."]},{"k":"p","s":["See our ",["advice for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Criminal kidnapping"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a risk of being kidnapped by criminals who will demand a ransom."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must be able to show some identification if requested by the police. If you want to keep your passport in a safe place, such as in a hotel safe, carry a printed copy of the photo page."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Public offences"]},{"k":"p","s":["Violating local laws may result in a prison sentence, served in a local prison. Sentences are severe. The judicial system allows long-term detention until a court hearing takes place. Foreign nationals have been known to spend several years in prison on remand while their cases are processed."]},{"k":"p","s":["The ",["detention facilities and prison conditions","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/philippines-prisoner-pack"]," are far below UK standards."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Demonstrations and rallies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Philippines Bureau of Immigration has warned foreign nationals against participating in public protests and political rallies. If you participate, you may be detained and deported. Avoid demonstrations and large gatherings of people."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs and prison sentences"]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not become involved with drugs of any kind. Penalties for importing and using illegal drugs are particularly severe. A conviction for possession of even a small amount of any illicit drug in the Philippines means a mandatory prison sentence."]},{"k":"p","s":["Police and other authorities have been publicly encouraged to kill suspected drug traffickers who resist arrest."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Laws on child abuse and rape"]},{"k":"p","s":["Child abuse and rape are punished with extremely long prison sentences. Be cautious about strangers offering friendship. There have been cases where women, single or sometimes with children, have befriended single male tourists and then threatened to report rape or abuse in an apparent attempt to extort money. A child is defined in Philippine law as a person aged 17 and under."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Philippines is generally a tolerant and progressive place for LGBT+ travellers, although overt public displays of affection may be considered a ‘grave scandal’ under the Revised Penal Code. If convicted, you could get a fine or a 6-month prison sentence."]},{"k":"p","s":["Current legislation does not recognise same-sex marriage. Same-sex relationships are not illegal in the Philippines, but some stigma exists outside urban centres."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Independent travel and adventure tourism"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re planning to travel away from the main resort areas and tourist spots, contact the authorities in the local area as part of your preparation."]},{"k":"p","s":["Always leave travel plans and your passport and credit card details with friends, colleagues or relatives. Carry identification such as a driving licence or copy of your passport at all times, and make sure the emergency contact details in your passport are up to date."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Water safety"]},{"k":"p","s":["Swimming and surfing beaches are unlikely to have lifeguards or warning signs, so get advice from your hotel or local residents before starting any activities. The seas can be extremely dangerous and British nationals regularly get into trouble in the water, or even drown."]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["water safety on holiday","https://www.rlss.org.uk/safety-on-holiday"]," from the Royal Life Saving Society."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Scuba diving"]},{"k":"p","s":["Diving schools may have limited resources and do not always observe safety and maintenance standards. Always:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check a dive operator’s credentials"]},{"k":"li","s":["make sure you’re covered by insurance"]},{"k":"li","s":["make sure safety equipment is available on the boat, particularly oxygen"]},{"k":"li","s":["ask about safety precautions, including the ability to transfer divers to a hyperbaric (recompression) chamber"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you have not had any previous diving experience:"]},{"k":"li","s":["ask your dive instructor to explain what insurance cover they offer before signing up"]},{"k":"li","s":["check what to do if something goes wrong, including how to call for help while at sea"]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in the Philippines, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can drive in the Philippines on a UK driving licence for up to 90 days. If you’re planning to hire a car, check their requirements before you travel. If you’re staying longer than 90 days, you must apply for a Philippine driving licence."]},{"k":"p","s":["Accidents happen frequently, mainly due to poor road conditions, dangerous driving and non-enforcement of traffic laws. Observe the speed limit and be cautious around motorbikes and scooters. Avoid driving at night or during dangerous weather conditions if possible. Make sure you have adequate insurance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Safety standards on taxis and buses can be low."]},{"k":"p","s":["When travelling by private car, taxi or any shared transport, you can expect a routine security presence with random checkpoints along the roads. Always co-operate with officials and allow extra time to pass through security checks."]},{"k":"h","s":["Sea travel"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Piracy"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high level of ",["piracy and armed robbery against ships","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/sea-river-and-piracy-safety"]," in and around the Sulu and Celebes seas. Boats travelling to and from offshore islands and dive sites are also possible targets."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Sea safety"]},{"k":"p","s":["The ferry and passenger boat network has a poor record of maritime safety. Boats sometimes lack lifesaving equipment, and maritime rescue services may be limited. You should be cautious when using ferries and avoid overcrowded boats. Accidents are more frequent during the rainy season between June and December when storms can develop quickly."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/extreme-weather-and-natural-hazards"]," for information about how to prepare, and how to react if there is a warning."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Typhoons"]},{"k":"p","s":["Around 20 typhoons hit the Philippines each year. Most typhoons happen between June and November. Follow the advice of local authorities, and monitor the progress of storms on the Philippines state weather agency and the Philippines Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Council. You can find updates on typhoon2000.ph, or follow ",["@Typhoon2k","https://twitter.com/Typhoon2k"]," on X."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Earthquakes"]},{"k":"p","s":["Earthquakes are a risk in the Philippines. The US Federal Emergency Management Agency website has advice about ",["what to do before, during and after an earthquake","https://www.ready.gov/earthquakes"],". You can get more information from the Philippine Institute for Volcanology and Seismology (PHIVOLCS)."]},{"k":"p","s":["On 30 September 2025, a magnitude 6.9 earthquake struck northern Cebu, with the epicentre near Bogo City. Local authorities have reported casualties, injuries, and significant damage to infrastructure."]},{"k":"p","s":["Power outages and disruptions to transport and communications have been reported. Aftershocks are expected and may continue over the coming days"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are in the affected area:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Follow the advice of local authorities and emergency services."]},{"k":"li","s":["Be aware of the risk of aftershocks."]},{"k":"li","s":["Avoid damaged buildings and infrastructure."]},{"k":"li","s":["Monitor local media and official sources for updates."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to travel to Cebu or nearby provinces:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Contact your travel provider for updates."]},{"k":"li","s":["Ensure your travel insurance covers natural disasters."]},{"k":"li","s":["Stay informed via the ",["Philippine Institute of Volcanology and Seismology (PHIVOLCS)","https://www.phivolcs.dost.gov.ph/"]," and ",["the National Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Council (NDRRMC)","https://ndrrmc.gov.ph/"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Volcanoes"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are numerous volcanoes in the Philippines, any of which can erupt without warning. Sudden steam and ash explosions may happen at any time."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Mayon Volcano is currently at alert level 3 (increased tendency towards a hazardous eruption)."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check news reports and follow local advice before travelling to any areas around volcanoes. Avoid volcanic areas during and immediately after heavy rainfall when there’s increased risk of lava flows."]},{"k":"p","s":["Get more information about volcanoes from the Philippine Institute for Volcanology and Seismology (PHIVOLCS)."]},{"k":"p","s":["Entry into Taal Volcano Island and Taal’s Permanent Danger Zone is prohibited. See ",["updates from PHIVOLCS","https://www.phivolcs.dost.gov.ph/index.php/taal-volcano-bulletin-menu/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ash plumes can affect air quality and have an impact on health. If you have any pre-existing respiratory conditions, you might be at increased risk of triggering or worsening your symptoms. A properly fitted face mask may provide some protection."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Philippine emergency and rescue services have a limited capacity to deal with large natural disasters."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Call 911 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for the Philippines","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/178/philippines#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See what ",["health risks you’ll face in the Philippines","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/178/philippines"],", including :"]},{"k":"li","s":["dengue"]},{"k":"li","s":["tick-borne encephalitis"]},{"k":"li","s":["Zika virus"]},{"k":"p","s":["Mosquito-borne diseases are a risk all year round. However, there’s a heightened risk of dengue during the rainy season from June to October. Take precautions to avoid being bitten by mosquitoes."]},{"k":"p","s":["Altitude sickness is a risk in parts of the Philippines. Read more about ",["altitude sickness on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/26/altitude-illness"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in the Philippines"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a ",["list of medical providers in the Philippines","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/philippines-list-of-medical-facilities"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"p","s":["The availability of medical care varies across the Philippines and may not meet the standards of care in the UK, particularly in rural and remote areas. Many places, including some tourist destinations, do not have easy access to emergency medical care."]},{"k":"p","s":["Private hospital treatment and medical transport is expensive – the daily cost in intensive care units can be more than £1,000. Make sure you have adequate travel health insurance and accessible funds to cover the cost of any medical treatment, including repatriation."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in the Philippines"]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 911 (ambulance, fire, police)"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Philippines"],", ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Philippines"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=Philippines"]," in the Philippines"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in the Philippines","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/philippines-bereavement-pack/philippines-bereavement-guide"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested or imprisoned in the Philippines","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/philippines-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/philippines/british-embassy-manila"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/philippines/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in the Philippines","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-philippines"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":23285,"change":"Information about typhoon season (‘Warnings and insurance’ page)."},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/saudi-arabia":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T17:18Z","sha":"67b08d2113a2bcb18d25af8f431fbb33d05c04c01282f3c4061f9f4ef109052c","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/saudi-arabia","bytes":104006,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Saudi Arabia travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-02-15T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-10-27T16:54:07+00:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["Your travel insurance could be invalidated if you travel against advice from the Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO)."]},{"k":"h","s":["Areas where FCDO advises against travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against:"]},{"k":"li","s":["all travel to within 10km of the border with Yemen"]},{"k":"li","s":["all but essential travel to the rest of Saudi Arabia"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["why FCDO advises against travel","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/saudi-arabia/regional-risks"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Regional tensions"]},{"k":"p","s":["King Khalid International Airport was struck by a missile on 10 October 2026. The airport continues to be targeted and remains at risk of further attacks."]},{"k":"p","s":["Since 13 July, the Houthis (a military group in Yemen) have launched missiles and drones targeting several locations in Saudi Arabia. There is a heightened threat against airports, Saudi military and defence buildings, military bases, ports and energy infrastructure across Saudi Arabia, including Abha, Jizan, Najran, Riyadh, Jeddah, Dammam and Yanbu, as well as shipping in the Red Sea. Further attacks against airports as well as disruption and cancellations are very likely."]},{"k":"p","s":["As an alternative to airports within Saudi Arabia, British nationals wishing to leave Saudi Arabia should consider travelling by land to a neighbouring country and flying from there. Plan your journey carefully, including checking the travel advice for any entry and exit requirements. See ",["‘Regional risks page’","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/saudi-arabia/regional-risks"]," for more information on land routes."]},{"k":"p","s":["In addition to the threat from Houthi attacks, the wider context in the Middle East remains deeply unpredictable and the risk of sudden escalation is high. Since conflict began in early 2026, Iran has stated its intention to target locations associated with the US and Israel, including, but not limited to, organisations, businesses, facilities, and institutions. There have been strikes and retaliatory attacks by Iran and others across the region against civilian and US military infrastructure."]},{"k":"p","s":["In light of the regional tensions, British nationals in Saudi Arabia should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["read ",["If you’re affected by a crisis abroad - GOV.UK","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],". This includes guidance on “how to prepare for a crisis” including suggestedemergency supplies and “what to do in a crisis”"]},{"k":"li","s":["sign up for FCDO Travel Advice ",["email alerts","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/saudi-arabia/email-signup"]]},{"k":"li","s":["follow advice from the local authorities. Saudi Civil Defence may issue early warning alerts to people in affected areas"]},{"k":"li","s":["monitor local and international media for the latest information"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid capturing or sharing images of conflict-related incidents"]},{"k":"li","s":["stay away from areas around oil infrastructure and military facilities"]},{"k":"li","s":["keep your travel plans under review and ensure your travel documents are up to date"]},{"k":"li","s":["if travelling by air, check that your booking is confirmed and the status of your flight before travelling to the airport; remain alert and follow instructions from local authorities"]},{"k":"li","s":["if you are advised to take shelter, stay indoors or go to the nearest safe building or designated shelter; an interior stairwell or a room with as few external walls or windows as possible may provide additional protection; the greatest risk is from falling debris caused by interceptions, and you are safest inside a secure structure"]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/saudi-arabia/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of Saudi Arabia’s current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Saudi Arabia set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Saudi Embassy in the UK","https://embassies.mofa.gov.sa/sites/uk/EN/Pages/default.aspx"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["For entry into Saudi Arabia, your passport must have an ‘expiry date’ at least 6 months after the date you arrive."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Previous travel to Israel"]},{"k":"p","s":["You may not be allowed to enter Saudi Arabia if your passport shows that you have travelled to, or were born in, Israel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must get a visa to visit Saudi Arabia. The type of visa you choose depends on your reason for travelling and how long you want to stay."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you overstay your visa, you could face large fines, detention and deportation. You could be banned from returning to Saudi Arabia."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Applying for an electronic travel authorisation"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can apply for an electronic travel authorisation (ETA) if you are travelling to Saudi Arabia for:"]},{"k":"li","s":["tourism"]},{"k":"li","s":["business"]},{"k":"li","s":["study"]},{"k":"li","s":["medical treatment"]},{"k":"li","s":["Umrah (outside the Hajj season)"]},{"k":"p","s":["An ETA is is valid for 730 days from the date of issue."]},{"k":"p","s":["Valid for multiple entries, but only 180 days in total across the 730 day period ."]},{"k":"p","s":["Apply for an ETA ",["online","https://ksavisa.sa/visa/electronic-travel-authorization/details?category=OTHER&categoryId=aab79697-b721-4907-b772-62a9bb42c36e"]," before you travel. If you are travelling for Hajj, you must obtain a separate Hajj visa. See ",["Pilgrimage","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/saudi-arabia/pilgrimage"]," for more information."]},{"k":"p","s":["An ETA does not include health insurance for your visit. Visas issued before the ETA was introduced will remain valid, in accordance with the conditions and dates on the visa when issued."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Applying for an e-visa"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can apply for an e-visa if you are a tourist."]},{"k":"p","s":["E-visas are:"]},{"k":"li","s":["valid for 365 days from the date of issue"]},{"k":"li","s":["valid for multiple entries, but only for 90 days in total across the 365 day period"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Apply for an e-visa online","https://visa.visitsaudi.com/"]," or when you arrive at any of Saudi Arabia’s international airports."]},{"k":"p","s":["An e-visa includes health insurance for your visit up to 100,000 Saudi Arabian Riyals (SAR). Medical treatment in Saudi Arabia can be expensive, and you should consider taking out additional travel insurance to cover costs beyond 100,000 SAR."]},{"k":"p","s":["You must get a separate visa for Hajj. See ",["Pilgrimage","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/saudi-arabia/pilgrimage"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Applying for an electronic visa waiver"]},{"k":"p","s":["Electronic visa waivers are for:"]},{"k":"li","s":["tourism"]},{"k":"li","s":["business"]},{"k":"li","s":["medical treatment"]},{"k":"li","s":["study"]},{"k":"li","s":["Umrah (outside of Hajj season)"]},{"k":"p","s":["An electronic visa waiver allows you to enter Saudi Arabia once and stay for up to 180 days."]},{"k":"p","s":["An electronic visa waiver does not include health insurance for your visit."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Apply for an electronic visa waiver online","https://visa.mofa.gov.sa/"]," at least 48 hours before your flight, or up to 90 days in advance. You will need to give your flight details."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travelling overland"]},{"k":"p","s":["Your visa may only allow you to enter Saudi Arabia by air. If you plan to travel to Saudi Arabia by the Bahrain causeway, check your visa before travelling. Ask your travel agent or the Saudi Embassy if you need help."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travelling through Saudi Arabia"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re transferring through Saudi Arabia, you may need a transit visa if:"]},{"k":"li","s":["you will pass through immigration control"]},{"k":"li","s":["you will leave Saudi Arabia on a separate ticket to the one you arrive on"]},{"k":"li","s":["the connecting time between your flights is more than 12 hours"]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your airline or travel agency if you require a transit visa."]},{"k":"h","s":["Exit, re-entry and final exit permits"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you live in Saudi Arabia, you must get an exit or re-entry permit from your sponsor to leave and re-enter the country. If you leave Saudi Arabia on a final exit permit, you must apply for a new visa to return to the country."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Wives and children of Saudi nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re a woman married to a Saudi national, you must get a re-entry or final exit permit from your husband to leave Saudi Arabia. This also applies to children of Saudi nationals."]},{"k":"h","s":["Flight restrictions around Hajj"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you plan to travel around the time of the Hajj pilgrimage, check with your airline for any flight restrictions."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Saudi authorities have stopped visitors who are not performing Hajj from flying to Jeddah, Madinah and Taif. You may need a Hajj visa to board flights to these places during Hajj."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will still be able to enter Saudi Arabia through other airports."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Saudi Arabia, you must have certificates to prove you’ve had a:"]},{"k":"li","s":["yellow fever vaccine if you’re coming from a ",["country listed as a transmission risk","https://nathnacyfzone.org.uk/factsheet/65/countries-with-risk-of-yellow-fever-transmission"]]},{"k":"li","s":["meningococcal quadrivalent vaccine if you’re a Hajj or Umrah pilgrim or a seasonal worker"]},{"k":"p","s":["For full details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Saudi Arabia guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/191/saudi-arabia#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about goods you can take into or out of Saudi Arabia. You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"p","s":["Items it’s illegal to import include:"]},{"k":"li","s":["alcohol"]},{"k":"li","s":["pork and pork products"]},{"k":"li","s":["pornographic material"]},{"k":"li","s":["distillery equipment"]},{"k":"li","s":["weapons"]},{"k":"li","s":["narcotics"]},{"k":"li","s":["re-treaded or used tyres"]},{"k":"li","s":["used clothing except for personal use"]},{"k":"li","s":["certain sculptures such as religious symbols Other items may be examined, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["personal videos"]},{"k":"li","s":["books"]},{"k":"li","s":["electronic devices"]},{"k":"p","s":["You may need special approval to bring some items such as:"]},{"k":"li","s":["agricultural seeds"]},{"k":"li","s":["live animals"]},{"k":"li","s":["religious books (except for personal use)"]},{"k":"li","s":["chemicals and harmful materials"]},{"k":"li","s":["some pharmaceutical products"]},{"k":"li","s":["wireless equipment"]},{"k":"li","s":["radio-controlled model airplanes"]},{"k":"li","s":["archaeological artefacts"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Using technical equipment"]},{"k":"p","s":["You may need a licence for:"]},{"k":"li","s":["satellite phones"]},{"k":"li","s":["listening or recording devices"]},{"k":"li","s":["radio transmitters"]},{"k":"li","s":["powerful cameras or binoculars"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you need information on customs rules, contact the ",["Saudi Embassy","https://embassies.mofa.gov.sa/sites/uk/EN/Pages/default.aspx"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Saudi Arabia"]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorists are likely to try to carry out attacks in Saudi Arabia."]},{"k":"p","s":["In addition to missile and drone strikes conducted by the Houthis, attacks from terrorist groups could be indiscriminate, including in places visited by foreign nationals. Stay aware of your surroundings, keep up to date with local media reports and follow the advice of local authorities."]},{"k":"p","s":["For information about Houthi attacks and the current conflict see ",["Warnings and insurance","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/saudi-arabia/warnings-and-insurance"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorists have threatened to carry out attacks in the Gulf region, including on:"]},{"k":"li","s":["residential compounds"]},{"k":"li","s":["military, oil, transport and aviation interests"]},{"k":"li","s":["public places, including restaurants, hotels, beaches, shopping centres and mosques"]},{"k":"li","s":["tourist sites"]},{"k":"p","s":["Be aware of your surroundings, particularly during high-profile events, and avoid large demonstrations."]},{"k":"h","s":["Political situation"]},{"k":"p","s":["Public demonstrations are illegal. Avoid any protest or demonstration and follow the advice of local authorities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["The crime rate in Saudi Arabia is low, but there is petty crime. There have also been more serious crimes, including crimes against women. Take care when travelling outside towns and cities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"p","s":["Saudi Arabia is a Muslim country and Islamic law is strictly enforced. Respect local traditions, customs, laws and religion so you do not cause offence. There may be serious penalties for doing something that might not be illegal in the UK."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should avoid:"]},{"k":"li","s":["showing affection in public"]},{"k":"li","s":["swearing and rude gestures"]},{"k":"li","s":["playing loud music"]},{"k":"li","s":["making critical political statements or behaving in ways the Saudi authorities assess disrupt the public order"]},{"k":"p","s":["Penalties include fines, imprisonment and deportation. See ",["Visit Saudi","https://www.visitsaudi.com/en/understand"]," for information on behaviour."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must always carry ID. You can get a fine or prison sentence if you do not have any."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re a tourist, carry a copy of your passport and visa."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you live in Saudi Arabia, carry your residency card (‘Iqama’). Police also accept an electronic version of the Iqama on the Tawakkalna app and Absher."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Ramadan"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ramadan is a holy month for Muslims. The dates vary by year and country. Ramadan in Saudi Arabia started on 18 February in 2026 and will last for 30 days. During this time, do not:"]},{"k":"li","s":["eat, drink, smoke or chew gum in public in the daytime, including in your car"]},{"k":"li","s":["play loud music or dance"]},{"k":"li","s":["swear in public"]},{"k":"p","s":["Get more advice when you arrive from your tour guide, hotel or business contacts."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should also:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check opening hours of shops and restaurants"]},{"k":"li","s":["be aware that if hotels and restaurants are providing food or drink in fasting hours, they may separate you from Islamic guests, for example with screens"]},{"k":"li","s":["follow local dress codes – clothing that does not meet local dress codes may cause more offence at this time"]},{"k":"li","s":["be patient and show tolerance"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Dress code"]},{"k":"p","s":["Men and women must wear loose-fitting clothing that covers the elbow and below the knees."]},{"k":"p","s":["Avoid clothing that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["is tight-fitting"]},{"k":"li","s":["has profane slogans or images"]},{"k":"li","s":["has symbols or slogans that could be viewed as political and lead to arrest"]},{"k":"p","s":["Female travellers do not have to wear the traditional robe (‘abaya’) or cover their hair. See ",["Visit Saudi","https://www.visitsaudi.com/en/understand"]," for more information on dress codes."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Religion"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to practise any religion other than Islam. However, the Saudi authorities accept private practice of other religions."]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to try to convert people to another religion. You can bring other religious books for personal use. However, you may be prosecuted if you try to import large numbers of religious books."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Alcohol laws and bans"]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not bring alcohol into Saudi Arabia or arrive under the influence of alcohol."]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to drink alcohol or be drunk in public. Police have arrested British nationals for disorderly or offensive behaviour when drinking. You can face severe penalties, including prison, for brewing, possessing or selling alcohol."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs penalties"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is zero tolerance for drug offences in Saudi Arabia, and the penalties are severe. If you’re arrested for drug offences, you may have a long period of detention before trial. You can get a prison sentence of up to 5 years and a fine of 30,000 Saudi riyals for possessing even small amounts. Drug dealing and smuggling can result in a death sentence."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Sexual relations outside of marriage"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sex outside of marriage and adultery are illegal, including for tourists. In the most serious circumstances (for example, those involving Saudi nationals) the penalties could include custodial sentences or deportation. There are special arrangements for visitors, and unmarried tourists may share hotel rooms."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Pregnancy outside of marriage"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you or your partner becomes pregnant outside marriage in Saudi Arabia, you could both face penalties including imprisonment and deportation. However, in practice, legal action is uncommon."]},{"k":"p","s":["Doctors may ask for proof of marriage during antenatal checks."]},{"k":"p","s":["To get a birth certificate from the Saudi authorities, you must provide a marriage certificate. The authorities may compare the date of the marriage against the estimated date of conception."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re an unmarried woman who gives birth in Saudi Arabia, you may have difficulties registering the birth of a child in Saudi Arabia. You could be arrested, imprisoned or deported."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Filming, photography and other media restrictions"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to film or photograph government buildings, diplomatic premises, military installations and palaces."]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not circulate material related to security risks, including drone or missile attacks or interceptions, on social media. Residents can use the “Tawakkalna” app to report suspicious aerial sightings. The “Kollona Amn” app can be used to report other security risks and serious crimes."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you produce, transmit or distribute printed, digital, audio or video information, you must get permission from the ",["General Authority of Media Regulation (GCAM)","https://www.gcam.gov.sa/"]," in advance. If you do not, you could get a large fine and a prison sentence."]},{"k":"p","s":["Only photograph local people if you have their consent."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Public statements and criticism"]},{"k":"p","s":["Be careful about what you circulate on social media. It is illegal to say publicly anything that the Saudi authorities deem disruptive to public order. Avoid making comments verbally or on social media on the topics below:"]},{"k":"li","s":["The King, Crown Prince or Royal Family"]},{"k":"li","s":["the Saudi government or authorities, including the police"]},{"k":"li","s":["Islam"]},{"k":"li","s":["the country’s culture, beliefs and ways of public life"]},{"k":"li","s":["issues that could be perceived as political, including wearing clothing with political slogans or carrying flags or banners, especially when performing Hajj and Umrah"]},{"k":"li","s":["the situation in Israel and Palestine"]},{"k":"p","s":["Speaking publicly about these issues can be defined by the Saudi authorities as posing a threat to national security. Statements made on social media many years ago, or those published outside Saudi Arabia, may be taken into account. Punishment can include long custodial sentences. The legal processes around national security cases can be complex and slow. If you are detained, it may take some time for the Saudi authorities to grant permission for consular officials to visit you."]},{"k":"p","s":["You’re likely to come under more scrutiny if you’re a British national who also:"]},{"k":"li","s":["carries Saudi citizenship"]},{"k":"li","s":["has close Saudi relatives"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Carrying 2 passports"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to have 2 passports in your name in Saudi Arabia. Immigration authorities will take additional passports. You must leave Saudi Arabia using the passport you entered on."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Legal system and due process"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Saudi legal system differs from the UK, for example:"]},{"k":"li","s":["suspects can be held without charge during an investigation"]},{"k":"li","s":["suspects are not always allowed quick access to legal representation"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re detained and need consular assistance, British Embassy staff will visit once they know about your case. In some cases, British Embassy staff have not been allowed to visit immediately or have had limited access."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is no legal aid in Saudi Arabia. You may want to hire a translator if you need to attend a criminal proceeding. ",["Find a translator or interpreter in Saudi Arabia","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=Saudi%20Arabia"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Unpaid debts and other financial crimes"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can get a fine, prison sentence or travel ban, or face deportation for financial crimes, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["writing a cheque which bounces (including post-dated and ‘security cheques’)"]},{"k":"li","s":["not paying bills (for example hotel bills or car hire)"]},{"k":"li","s":["fraud and bribery"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Saudi authorities can also freeze your bank account or other assets. You may be liable for cheques you signed on behalf of a company."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Saudi authorities could:"]},{"k":"li","s":["prevent you from cancelling your residence permit"]},{"k":"li","s":["stop you leaving the country"]},{"k":"li","s":["block your government services"]},{"k":"li","s":["not allow you to renew your residency card, re-entry visa or exit permits"]},{"k":"li","s":["stop you transferring to a new employer (sponsor)"]},{"k":"li","s":["use your end-of-service benefits to pay outstanding debts"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel bans"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Saudi authorities may stop you from leaving the country for:"]},{"k":"li","s":["unpaid debts"]},{"k":"li","s":["ongoing commercial, financial or labour disputes"]},{"k":"li","s":["legal cases"]},{"k":"li","s":["investigations"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re under a travel ban, you cannot leave the country, even if you’re a British national or dual British-Saudi national. They can take years to resolve. If you’re banned from travel, get legal advice."]},{"k":"p","s":["Government bodies often keep passports for official purposes. Employers (sponsors) may try to hold onto your passport, but this is illegal."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Deportation"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re found guilty of an offence and sentenced to over 3 months in prison, the Saudi authorities can deport you. Sometimes the authorities deport people with shorter sentences, regardless of whether the judgement included deportation. If you’re employed in Saudi Arabia, deportation will impact your employment and may affect your ability to return to Saudi Arabia in the future."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Same-sex relations are illegal, although legal action is uncommon. All couples should be aware of local customs and avoid showing affection in public."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Visit Saudi","https://www.visitsaudi.com/en"]," says all visitors are welcome, are not required to disclose their personal information and will have their right to privacy respected."]},{"k":"p","s":["Being transgender is not recognised in Saudi Arabia. Transgender people could also face difficulties with dress codes and access to medical care."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re planning to drive in Saudi Arabia, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can use a UK photocard driving licence for the first 3 months after you arrive in Saudi Arabia. After that, you must apply for a local licence. Hire care companies may require an ",["international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Standards of driving are poor and there are a high number of serious accidents on the roads. You should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["always wear seatbelts"]},{"k":"li","s":["keep to major roads if possible"]},{"k":"li","s":["travel in convoy and in daylight when travelling through desert areas"]},{"k":"p","s":["Some cities have an automated traffic system. Anyone caught speeding or committing other traffic offences will be notified by text of their fine. Fines are recorded on the Absher system, which is linked to your passport, residency or ID card. You must pay any outstanding fines through the system before leaving the country. You can pay at the airport but only during Saudi office hours."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Sea travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["Vessels operating in the Gulf of Oman, Northern Arabian Sea, Gulf of Aden and Bab El Mandeb areas may be at increased risk of attack by pirates. See ",["piracy and armed robbery at sea","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/sea-river-and-piracy-safety"],". There is also a heightened risk of Houthi attacks against Saudi shipping vessels in the Red Sea and other waters."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Air travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a heightened threat of attacks against airports in Saudi Arabia by the Houthis (a military group in Yemen). Further attacks against airports as well as disruption and cancellations are very likely. See the ‘ ",["Warnings and insurance’ page","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/saudi-arabia"]," for more information."]},{"k":"p","s":["King Khalid International Airport was struck by a missile on 10 October 2026. The airport continues to be targeted and remains at risk of further attacks."]},{"k":"p","s":["As an alternative to airports within Saudi Arabia, British nationals wishing to leave Saudi Arabia should consider travelling by land to a neighbouring country and flying from there. See the ",["‘Regional risks’ page","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/saudi-arabia/regional-risks"]," for more information on land routes."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to prepare for and respond to ",["extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Flooding"]},{"k":"p","s":["Heavy rains from November to February can cause flooding. Use the internet to check weather forecasts. In a flood, follow Civil Defence advice or call them on 998."]},{"k":"h","s":["Regional risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["This section has safety advice for regions of Saudi Arabia. It only covers regions where FCDO has specific advice."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should also read ",["FCDO’s overall travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/saudi-arabia"]," and ",["safety and security advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/saudi-arabia/safety-and-security"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Saudi Arabia-Yemen border and threats from the Houthis"]},{"k":"p","s":["In 2026, direct military conflict between the Houthi rebel military group and the Governments of Yemen and Saudi Arabia has resumed."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against:"]},{"k":"li","s":["all travel to within 10km of the border with Yemen"]},{"k":"li","s":["all but essential travel to the rest of Saudi Arabia"]},{"k":"p","s":["As an alternative to airports within Saudi Arabia, British nationals wishing to leave Saudi Arabia should consider travelling by land to a neighbouring country and flying from there. If you judge it is safe to do so, plan your journey carefully, including checking travel advice for the country you are considering to travel through, and any entry and exit requirements to make sure you have the correct documentation and not be denied entry."]},{"k":"p","s":["If travelling by car, the vehicle must be wholly owned and registered in your name. If using commercial transport, check the latest updates from your airline or tour operator and ensure they can transport you across the border, follow instructions from the local authorities and check the status of border crossings before you travel. Make sure you have access to emergency supplies, water and essential medication. Travel within or out of Saudi Arabia is at your own risk."]},{"k":"p","s":["Vehicle authorisations can be issued through the Absher portal, allowing another person, including dependants aged 18 and over, to drive your vehicle in Saudi Arabia or abroad. Drivers with a valid Exit/Re-Entry Visa must cancel it before the authorisation can be issued."]},{"k":"p","s":["Some bus services, private hire taxis and other vehicles may offer cross-border travel. Check schedules, confirm bookings and make sure the operator has the necessary permissions to cross the border. Before you travel, check where your transport will leave you. Some border crossings do not have onward transportation, and facilities can be extremely limited."]},{"k":"li","s":["Bus service: ",["SAT Transportation","https://satrans.com.sa/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Military zones and border posts"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Saudi Tourism Authority has banned tourist trips to military zones and border posts."]},{"k":"p","s":["In light of the regional tensions, British nationals in Saudi Arabia should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["read ",["If you’re affected by a crisis abroad - GOV.UK","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],". This includes guidance on “how to prepare for a crisis” with suggested emergency supplies, and “what to do in a crisis”"]},{"k":"li","s":["sign up for FCDO Travel Advice ",["email alerts","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/saudi-arabia/email-signup"]]},{"k":"li","s":["follow advice from the local authorities; Saudi Civil Defence may issue early warning alerts to people in affected areas"]},{"k":"li","s":["monitor local and international media for the latest information"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid capturing or sharing images of conflict-related incidents"]},{"k":"li","s":["stay away from areas around oil infrastructure and military facilities"]},{"k":"li","s":["keep your travel plans under review and ensure your travel documents are up to date"]},{"k":"li","s":["if travelling by air, check that your booking is confirmed and the status of your flight before travelling to the airport; remain alert at airports and follow instructions from local authorities"]},{"k":"li","s":["if you are advised to take shelter, stay indoors or go to the nearest safe building or designated shelter; an interior stairwell or a room with as few external walls or windows as possible may offer additional protection; the greatest risk is from falling debris caused by interceptions, and you are safest inside a secure structure"]},{"k":"h","s":["Pilgrimage"]},{"k":"p","s":["Many British nationals travel to Saudi Arabia each year for Umrah or Hajj pilgrimage."]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements for pilgrimage"]},{"k":"p","s":["You should also read the main section on ",["Entry requirements","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/saudi-arabia/entry-requirements"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can apply for an e-visa or electronic visa waiver to perform Umrah outside of the Hajj season."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can only book a Hajj place through the official ",["Nusuk Hajj platform","https://hajj.nusuk.sa/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visas"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Hajj visa is for a set length of time. It is not extendable. Check your visa expiry date to make sure you know when you must leave Saudi Arabia by. If you overstay, you may incur large fines and/or be detained and deported or banned from returning to Saudi Arabia in the future. Stay with your tour guide and group throughout the Hajj to make sure you receive your Hajj package entitlement."]},{"k":"h","s":["Personal documents"]},{"k":"p","s":["Keep your passport and travel documentation safe during Hajj and Umrah. Take photocopies and keep one copy with you. Leave a copy with friends or family. If you lose your passport during the Hajj, you will need to apply for an Emergency Travel Document (ETD) to return to the UK which costs £125. You will need to allow time for the ETD to be processed. See ",["Apply for an Emergency Travel Document","https://www.gov.uk/travel-urgently-from-abroad-without-uk-passport"]," for more information."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Health risks and vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must have a valid certificate of vaccination against the ACWY strains of meningitis 10 days before arriving for Hajj and Umrah. For more information on health risks and vaccination requirements, read the TravelHealthPro Hajj and Umrah guide."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check ",["Health","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/saudi-arabia/health"]," for advice on bringing medicines into Saudi Arabia. Make sure you have enough medication for your entire trip, including if your return is delayed."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contagious diseases spread quickly, particularly during Hajj and Ramadan. Flu, colds and respiratory problems are common."]},{"k":"p","s":["Prepare for extreme heat. During the summer months, the temperature may exceed 50°C. Consume enough liquids and avoid prolonged exposure to direct sunlight."]},{"k":"h","s":["Scams"]},{"k":"p","s":["UK-based organised crime groups target people planning Hajj or Umrah trips. Criminals pick people of any age, gender or location for their scams. Many victims are over the age of 65."]},{"k":"p","s":["To avoid scams:"]},{"k":"li","s":["be aware you can only book a Hajj place on the ",["Nusuk Hajj platform","https://hajj.nusuk.sa/"]]},{"k":"li","s":["check Saudi Ministry of Hajj information for the procedures you must follow"]},{"k":"li","s":["make sure your travel agent or operator is ATOL protected when booking Umrah"]},{"k":"li","s":["research the travel company before you book, even if family or friends recommended it"]},{"k":"li","s":["be wary of offers too good to be true – criminals advertise fraudulent deals through licensed travel companies"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Paying for trips"]},{"k":"p","s":["When paying for your Hajj or Umrah visit:"]},{"k":"li","s":["use a credit card where possible"]},{"k":"li","s":["have an audit trail and keep a record of any transactions"]},{"k":"li","s":["get everything confirmed in writing"]},{"k":"li","s":["always ask for written terms and conditions"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Reporting fraud"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you have been a victim of Hajj fraud in the UK, contact:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your local police"]},{"k":"li","s":[["City of London Police Fraud Desk","https://www.cityoflondon.police.uk/ro/report/fo/v1/fraud/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Action Fraud","https://www.actionfraud.police.uk/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Further information and help"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you have booked a Hajj package and have any queries, you should visit ",["Nusuk Hajj","https://hajj.nusuk.sa/"]," or check:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Tel: +966 9200 31201"]},{"k":"li","s":["Email: Support@hajj.nusuk.sa"]},{"k":"li","s":["Social media: ‘Nusuk Hajj’ on ",["Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Fnusukhajj%2F&is_from_rle"],", ",["Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/NusukHajj/"]," or ",["X","https://x.com/hajj_nusuk"]]},{"k":"p","s":["If you require consular assistance that is not related to your Nusuk travel package, contact:"]},{"k":"li","s":["the British Consulate General in Jeddah on +9661 1481 9100"]},{"k":"li","s":["the FCDO in the UK on +44 207 008 5000"]},{"k":"p","s":["To plan your visit and keep updated when travelling, see the:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["Ministry of Hajj and Umrah on X","https://x.com/MoHU_EN"]," and ",["Nusuk Hajj on X","https://x.com/hajj_nusuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":["British Embassy in Saudi Arabia on ",["X","https://x.com/ukinsaudiarabia"]," and ",["Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/ukinsaudiarabia"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Saudi Embassy in the UK","https://embassies.mofa.gov.sa/sites/uk/EN/Pages/default.aspx"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Call 911 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Saudi Arabia","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/191/saudi-arabia#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Saudi Arabia","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/191/saudi-arabia"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Altitude sickness is a risk in parts of Saudi Arabia. Read more about ",["altitude sickness on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/26/altitude-illness"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contagious diseases spread quickly, particularly during Hajj and Ramadan. There is an increased risk of heat stroke and dehydration during the summer months. Bring basic medicines with you and consume adequate liquids and salts."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries. In Saudi Arabia some prescribed or over-the-counter medicines are controlled substances. You may need approval from the Saudi authorities to bring some prescription drugs. See ",["rules on bringing prescription drugs to Saudi Arabia","https://saudiembassy.net/bringing-prescription-drugs-kingdom-saudi-arabia"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you need to bring controlled or prescription medication, make sure you have an official prescription, hospital note or a letter from your GP, which includes:"]},{"k":"li","s":["the amount prescribed"]},{"k":"li","s":["details of the drug and dosage"]},{"k":"li","s":["your doctor’s signature"]},{"k":"li","s":["a stamp from the clinic or hospital"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["narcotics and psychotropic substances information from the Saudi government","https://www.sfda.gov.sa/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK prescriptions are not accepted in Saudi Arabia. Only doctors registered and licensed by the Saudi Commission for Health Specialities may issue prescriptions."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pharmacies are common and easy to find, particularly in the big cities. All hospitals have a dispensing pharmacy. Shopping malls and plazas sell international brands."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Saudi Arabia"]},{"k":"p","s":["Healthcare facilities in major Saudi cities are of a high standard. Most towns have a health centre or basic hospital. Serious cases may be transferred by ambulance or air to a hospital in a major city, which might be some distance away."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a ",["list of medical providers in Saudi Arabia","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/saudi-arabia-list-of-medical-facilities-and-practitioners"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Saudi Arabia"]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 911 (ambulance, fire, police)"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you do not have a Saudi SIM card, call 112 in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Reporting an incident in Saudi Arabia from the UK or another country"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact the Saudi Embassy in London or the Saudi Embassy in the country you are located."]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you’re involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you’re in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Saudi%20Arabia"],", ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Saudi%20Arabia"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=Saudi%20Arabia"]," in Saudi Arabia"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Saudi Arabia","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/saudi-arabia-bereavement-information-guide"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested or imprisoned in Saudi Arabia","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/saudi-arabia-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/saudi-arabia/british-embassy-riyadh"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/saudi-arabia/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in Saudi Arabia","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-saudi-arabia"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":34364,"change":"Updated information about Regional tensions (‘Warnings and insurance’ page)"},"https://theconversation.com/massive-sinkholes-open-up-across-turkey-as-it-struggles-with-drought-and-climate-change-295123":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T17:18Z","sha":"8c3e8c0b96c3831758033ed340c4e2bbc20a090475f1b5613b44963f9b81f346","read":"https://theconversation.com/massive-sinkholes-open-up-across-turkey-as-it-struggles-with-drought-and-climate-change-295123","bytes":182342,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Massive sinkholes open up across Turkey as it struggles with drought and climate change","by":[{"n":"Nima Shokri","r":"Adjunct Professor, Institute for Water, Environment and Health (UNU-INWEH), United Nations University; Technical University of Hamburg"}],"pub":"2026-10-30T13:13:12Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Turkey’s central Anatolian plateau is one of the country’s most important agricultural regions, producing wheat, maize, sugar beet and other crops. Yet beneath its cultivated fields, the ground is becoming increasingly unstable."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Large sinkholes","https://www.bbc.com/future/article/20260624-droughts-are-transforming-the-turkish-landscape-with-massive-sinkholes"],", some tens of metres wide and deep, have appeared across the Konya basin, swallowing farmland, and threatening nearby ",["roads and settlements","https://theconversation.com/uk/search?q=sinkholes"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["These collapses can occur suddenly, sometimes in fields that have been cultivated for generations. Around 20 are ",["opening up","https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0013795225005769"]," every year, according to a recent study."]},{"k":"p","s":["Known locally as obruks, sinkholes are not a new geological phenomenon. They have existed in the Konya basin for thousands of years, but they have become far more frequent over recent decades."]},{"k":"p","s":["Konya’s sinkholes are consequently both a geological hazard and evidence of a wider water-management problem. The cavities beneath the fields are the product of geological processes extending over thousands of years. Their recent instability, however, is occurring within a groundwater system profoundly altered by human activity and increasingly ",["exposed to drought","https://www.kcl.ac.uk/research/green-energies-on-the-ground-across-the-mediterranean/turkeys-climate-crossroads-from-drought-to-the-global-stage"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["As representatives of countries all over the world prepare to head to Turkey to discuss climate change at the UN’s Cop 31 conference, Ankara continues to grapple with this escalating environmental disaster at home."]},{"k":"p","s":["The nation’s disaster and emergency management authority (AFAD) has recently documented ",["684 sinkholes","https://www.turkiyetoday.com/lifestyle/konya-closed-basin-records-684-sinkholes-as-turkiye-updates-regional-risk-maps-3211133"]," across Konya, Karaman and Aksaray in Turkey’s agricultural heartlands."]},{"k":"h","s":["Why are they there?"]},{"k":"p","s":["The growing number of sinkholes is often attributed to ",["drought and climate change","https://www.reuters.com/sustainability/climate-energy/sinkholes-turkeys-agricultural-heartland-fuel-farmers-concerns-2025-12-23/"],". But intensive groundwater extraction for agriculture can also increase the risk of collapse."]},{"k":"p","s":["Decades of intensive ",["agricultural irrigation","https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/feb/28/i-live-in-constant-fear-surge-in-giant-sinkholes-threatens-turkeys-farmers"]," have altered the conditions beneath the basin’s surface. Groundwater, which is the layer of water below the Earth’s surface, is also not being replenished during long, dry periods, which adds to the problem."]},{"k":"p","s":["Konya is a ",["closed drainage basin","https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10040-008-0358-2"],". This means water entering the basin does not flow towards the sea. It is stored underground, and accumulates in lakes and wetlands, or returns to the atmosphere through evaporation and plant transpiration."]},{"k":"p","s":["Rainfall is relatively low here, and much of it falls outside the main growing season. Groundwater has, therefore, become indispensable to agriculture, particularly for irrigated maize, sugar beet and fodder crops."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Subsidence claims: after drought, ground can shrink, swell or even collapse when it rains – causing damage to homes","https://theconversation.com/subsidence-claims-after-drought-ground-can-shrink-swell-or-even-collapse-when-it-rains-causing-damage-to-homes-294511"]]},{"k":"p","s":["The difficulty is that demand for water has grown beyond the rate at which the aquifers, a body of porous rock or sediment saturated with groundwater, can recover. A recent regional ",["study","https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/15481603.2021.2000349"]," estimated an average annual loss of groundwater storage, equivalent to 3.4 centimetres of water. This figure clearly points to a system under sustained pressure."]},{"k":"p","s":["Part of the problem is that Turkey ",["experienced its most severe drought","https://www.mgm.gov.tr/eng/Yearly-Climate/State_of_the_Climate_in_Turkey_in_2025.pdf"]," for decades in 2025, putting more pressure on farmers."]},{"k":"p","s":["Farmers often respond by extracting more groundwater, causing underground water levels to fall. This reduces the pressure exerted by water within the pores and fractures of rocks and sediments, potentially destabilising existing underground cavities and increasing the risk of ",["collapse","https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0013795225005769"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The consequences extend beyond water scarcity, because groundwater also puts stress on underground geological formations. The Konya basin contains extensive carbonate rocks, including limestone. Over long periods, groundwater circulating through fractures dissolves minerals and enlarges openings. This process, known as ",["karstification","https://www.usgs.gov/publications/effects-karst-and-geologic-structure-circulation-water-and-permeability-carbonate"],", can produce underground channels, caves and cavities. Sinkholes form when the material above such voids becomes unstable."]},{"k":"p","s":["Lower groundwater levels can also change the movement of water and sediment through existing underground cavities, allowing loose material to shift downwards. Where the roof of a cavity is already weak, these changes may eventually lead to collapse."]},{"k":"p","s":["But the response is highly dependent on local conditions. The depth and shape of underground cavities, the thickness and strength of the layers of rock and sediment above them, the distribution of fractures and the history of groundwater fluctuations all matter."]},{"k":"p","s":["This helps explain an ",["important finding","https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0013795225005769"]," from a study on sinkhole formation in the Konya basin between 2000 and 2024. The researchers identified a sharp increase in the annual formation rate, from approximately three sinkholes a year during 2000-10 to 32 during 2016-19. Yet the rate subsequently declined to around 22 a year after 2020, despite continuing groundwater depletion."]},{"k":"p","s":["If falling groundwater is responsible, why would fewer sinkholes form while water levels continue to decline? One possible explanation is that the most vulnerable cavities in some areas have already collapsed. Sinkhole formation depends on the number of unstable underground structures, not simply on the volume of water extracted."]},{"k":"h","s":["Land is breaking down"]},{"k":"p","s":["The basin is also experiencing another type of ground deformation, known as land subsidence, in which the surface gradually sinks as underground sediments compact. This can cause cracks in the ground and damage to roads and buildings, although the sinking is often too gradual to notice without satellite measurements."]},{"k":"p","s":["Satellite radar ",["measurements","https://www.mdpi.com/2076-3263/14/1/5"]," revealed widespread land subsidence in the area, of up to 90 millimetres per year. Unlike sudden sinkhole collapse, this can develop as groundwater withdrawal increases stress on the land and compresses sediments in the ground."]},{"k":"p","s":["The problem is not unique to Turkey. A global ",["analysis","https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2023GL104497"]," estimated that over 6.3 million square kilometres of land are subsiding by more than five millimetres annually. The researchers identified groundwater extraction as the most influential factor worldwide."]},{"k":"p","s":["In Konya, the pressure on groundwater is closely connected to ",["agricultural production","https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S2352801X25001377"],". Farmers cultivate crops for established markets and processing industries, often under policies that have favoured high levels of production, rather than water conservation."]},{"k":"p","s":["Irrigation provides a way for farmers to maintain yields of crops during dry years, but it also allows production to continue at levels that the basin’s renewable water supply may not sustain."]},{"k":"p","s":["However, restricting how much groundwater is extracted without providing support for farmers could impose substantial economic pressure on them, as well as on the nation’s food supply. But continued groundwater depletion could progressively undermine the agricultural production that made the region economically important in the first place."]},{"k":"p","s":["More efficient irrigation could help, but is not enough. If water saved through improved technology is used to expand the area being irrigated, total groundwater consumption may remain unchanged or even increase."]},{"k":"p","s":["A long-term response would require reliable monitoring of groundwater levels and withdrawals, enforceable extraction limits, agricultural incentives aligned with local water availability and detailed mapping of geological hazards. Satellite measurements can help identify areas under pressure."]},{"k":"p","s":["The most immediate danger is that another field, road or building may collapse, putting lives at risk."]},{"k":"p","s":["Preventing the next sinkhole is difficult. The government could address the problem. But it needs to introduce agricultural policies that treat groundwater as a finite resource, rather than a permanent substitute for rainfall."]}],"chars":7435},"https://theconversation.com/us-foreign-policy-leaders-say-america-should-take-an-active-role-in-world-affairs-but-no-consensus-on-whether-trumps-policies-are-working-296039":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T17:32Z","sha":"49f7bf63236aad7bf15fa5a94fcc4717b395b9579f2c64f0d30f97f598a4b6ac","read":"https://theconversation.com/us-foreign-policy-leaders-say-america-should-take-an-active-role-in-world-affairs-but-no-consensus-on-whether-trumps-policies-are-working-296039","bytes":188539,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"US foreign policy leaders say America should take an active role in world affairs – but no consensus on whether Trump’s policies are working","by":[{"n":"Joshua Busby","r":"Professor of Public Affairs, The University of Texas at Austin"},{"n":"Jonathan Monten","r":"Lecturer in Political Science and Director of the International Public Policy Program, UCL"},{"n":"Jordan Tama","r":"Professor, American University School of International Service"}],"pub":"2026-11-17T13:40:15Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["In the wake of the U.S. midterms, ",["Vice President JD Vance blamed","https://x.com/JDVance/status/2118004988433641835?a=MKXEzUOFuRP7aprHqPc&s=20"]," the Iran war for the election result. Affordability, ",["Vance pointed out","https://x.com/JDVance/status/2118004988433641835?a=MKXEzUOFuRP7aprHqPc&s=20"],", appeared to be central to voters’ choices, with foreign policy decisions such as the Iran war generating higher fuel prices and rates of inflation. Polling before the election ",["confirmed voters’ concerns","https://foreignpolicy.com/2026/10/27/trump-polling-midterms-foreign-policy/"]," – nearly two-thirds of Americans ",["disapproved of President Donald Trump’s foreign policy","https://www.politico.com/news/2026/09/22/trump-foreign-policy-approval-rating-poll-01087383"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["But do foreign policy experts share Americans’ concerns?"]},{"k":"p","s":["To answer that question, ",["the University of Texas at Austin","https://lbj.utexas.edu/faculty"],", in partnership with the ",["the Chicago Council on Global Affairs","https://globalaffairs.org/"],", recently surveyed 449 U.S. foreign policy leaders from the executive branch, Congress, think tanks, interest groups, media and academia."]},{"k":"p","s":["Their responses matter because as the United States struggles to end the Iran war and navigate the ",["fallout of tariff policies","https://budgetmodel.wharton.upenn.edu/p/2025-04-10-the-economic-effects-of-president-trumps-tariffs/"],", these experts will be tasked with finding solutions to those pressing problems. These foreign policy experts are also likely to be advising presidential candidates in the run-up to the 2028 elections."]},{"k":"h","s":["Areas of consensus and disagreement"]},{"k":"p","s":["On some issues, there is a consensus."]},{"k":"p","s":["We found strong bipartisan agreement on the need for the U.S. to take an active role in the world, the importance of supporting NATO, and the use of force to support European allies if they are attacked."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ninety-three percent of experts want the United States to take an active part in the world. That includes 83% of Republican experts, 98% of Democrats and 90% of independents. More than 70% of Democrats and more than 80% of Republicans and independents among foreign policy experts we surveyed agree that military power has been very important to American influence in the world. And more than 90% of experts of all partisan stripes agree that economic power has been very important."]},{"k":"p","s":["However, these points of agreement mask key differences."]},{"k":"p","s":["On the Iran war, 98% of Democrats and 73% of independent experts say war was the wrong decision, while 58% of Republican leaders say it was correct. While experts of all stripes recognized that ",["tariffs would raise costs for Americans","https://finance.yahoo.com/economy/policy/articles/tariffs-cost-average-u-household-170108552.html"],", there were stronger splits on ",["whether tariffs were good for the U.S. economy","https://budgetlab.yale.edu/research/tracking-economic-effects-tariffs"],". One hundred percent of Democrats and 81% of independents say they were bad, while 53% of Republicans say they were good."]},{"k":"h","s":["America First"]},{"k":"p","s":["These answers largely rally around partisan identities, but responses to philosophical questions about how the U.S. should pursue its interests proved more varied."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Trump administration has challenged the foundations of U.S. foreign policy through its ",["America First agenda","https://www.cfr.org/articles/america-first-policies-leave-america-alone-and-disadvantaged"],", which ",["favors U.S. domestic and economic interests","https://www.brookings.edu/articles/what-is-trumps-america-first-trade-policy-agenda/"]," over international agreements and global alliances."]},{"k":"p","s":["On ",["tariffs","https://www.cnbc.com/2026/11/08/trump-tariffs-democrats-congress-canada.html"],", efforts to expand U.S. territory and the use of force, the Trump administration used coercion to achieve its ends, including with close allies."]},{"k":"p","s":["The ",["Biden administration used tariffs","https://www.commerce.gov/news/fact-sheets/2024/05/fact-sheet-president-biden-takes-action-protect-american-workers-and"]," to counter China’s dominance in areas such as critical minerals and batteries. The Trump administration has ",["applied tariffs","https://www.csis.org/analysis/liberation-day-tariffs-explained"]," to rivals such as China and traditional allies alike, including in Europe and Asia."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Trump administration also expressed interest in territorial expansion through the ",["acquisition of Greenland","https://www.cfr.org/articles/greenlands-independence-what-would-mean-us-interests"]," and even ",["Canada as a possible 51st state","https://time.com/article/2026/10/16/trump-canada-trump-annexation-threat-carney-canada-separatist-referendum-warning/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Besides military operations to ",["depose and capture the Venezuelan president","https://www.nytimes.com/2026/01/03/world/americas/venezuela-maduro-capture-trump.html"]," and ",["war with Iran","https://www.cfr.org/global-conflict-tracker/conflict/confrontation-between-united-states-and-iran"],", the Trump administration has ",["struck boats in the Caribbean","https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2025/10/29/us/us-caribbean-pacific-boat-strikes.html"]," suspected of running drugs."]},{"k":"h","s":["The downsides of coercion"]},{"k":"p","s":["We asked foreign policy leaders to assess the sources of U.S. power and whether there are downsides to a coercive strategy of American dominance. Specifically, we asked them: “In order to achieve U.S. foreign policy goals internationally, do you think it is more important for the U.S. to be feared or admired around the world?”"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sixty-two percent of Republican leaders suggested it is more important to be feared, while 97% of Democrats said it’s more important to be admired. Independents were closer to Democrats, with 81% saying it’s better to be admired."]},{"k":"p","s":["We also asked whether countries have options to oppose U.S. coercion: “The Trump administration has used coercion, tariffs, punitive sanctions, and threats against many other countries, including traditional allies,” we said. Then we asked, “Which of these best captures your view?”"]},{"k":"p","s":["The respondents had three options to choose from. Thirty-nine percent of Republican experts agreed that “Other countries largely have to accept what the U.S. dictates.” No Democrats and 11% of independents agreed with that sentiment."]},{"k":"p","s":["Fifty-five percent of Democrats and 54% of independents chose the second option: “Other countries will accept what the U.S. dictates in the short run but will distance themselves from United States order in the longer run.” A large percentage of Republicans – 48% – agreed with that sentiment. This suggests a recognition by Republicans that coercive power alone may have its limits."]},{"k":"p","s":["A further 44% of Democrats and 35% of independents chose option three, “Other countries have viable options in the short and long run to resist U.S. coercion,” compared to only 13% of Republicans."]},{"k":"p","s":["These partisan gaps suggest some strong cleavages about the foundations of U.S. power in the world. They also raise questions about how best the U.S. can achieve its interests on the world stage."]},{"k":"p","s":["A subsequent U.S. president may have to engage in more vigorous dialogue with the American public about the sources of U.S. influence and power. The Trump administration’s coercive turn has some adherents, but many leaders see major costs to that approach and may be open to a new approach to U.S. foreign policy."]},{"k":"p","s":["Enough ",["damage to the existing world order","https://thehill.com/opinion/international/6204917-congressional-pushback-iran-war/"]," has been done by the Trump administration, we believe, that a return to establishment internationalism of old is not an option."]},{"k":"p","s":["Our survey suggests a ripe moment for new ideas and wide-ranging conversation about the U.S. role in the world."]}],"chars":5902},"https://theconversation.com/democrats-agenda-will-be-set-by-their-ability-to-organize-and-compromise-not-by-the-socialist-progressive-or-centrist-factions-all-claiming-victory-296014":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T17:32Z","sha":"118490a75c9186594d641c23657758943c909b04ed552380fd68ce9c5a75e013","read":"https://theconversation.com/democrats-agenda-will-be-set-by-their-ability-to-organize-and-compromise-not-by-the-socialist-progressive-or-centrist-factions-all-claiming-victory-296014","bytes":188717,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Democrats’ agenda will be set by their ability to organize and compromise — not by the socialist, progressive or centrist factions all claiming victory","by":[{"n":"SoRelle Wyckoff Gaynor","r":"Assistant Professor of Public Policy and Politics, University of Virginia"}],"pub":"2026-11-10T19:52:39Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["The ",["massive Democratic majority","https://www.npr.org/2026/11/04/nx-s1-6022216/midterms-democrats-trump-republicans-analysis"]," in the U.S. House and Senate that was ushered in by a ",["historic blue midterm vote","https://www.rutgers.edu/news/what-drove-historic-blue-wave-2026-midterms"]," is an ",["ideologically diverse one","https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/05/congress-midterms-diverse"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Candidates spent much of the past year differentiating their positions from the mainstream Democratic coalition. The result is a freshman class filled with as many ",["progressive liberals as moderate problem solvers","https://www.politico.com/news/2019/12/10/stephanie-murphy-moderate-progressive-freshman-democrats-080087"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["By the morning after Election Day, pundits and current Democratic members across the political spectrum were quick to claim their ideologically aligned candidates as the “ ",["majority makers","https://prospect.org/2026/09/14/oct-2026-the-new-majority-makers/"],"” – the group most responsible for the large victory."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Centrist Democrats","https://www.thirdway.org/memo/center-left-democrats-overperformed-and-delivered-the-majority"]," pointed to pragmatic moderates flipping Trump-won seats. ",["Liberal voices","https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=DoN2gy6oR5g"]," highlighted the enthusiasm and turnout driven by a new, progressive vision."]},{"k":"p","s":["As a result, days after the election the focus had turned toward January: Who will become the majority maker within Congress?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Party caucus leaders have already started ",["building their roster","https://www.politico.com/news/2026/11/04/democrats-house-majority-agenda-01150963"],": The Progressive Caucus ",["claims at least 25 new members","https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/09/progressives-us-house-flipped-seats"]," in their ranks, growing their membership to over 100 Democratic members. The moderate ",["Blue Dog Caucus doubled in size","https://www.politico.com/news/2026/11/04/democrats-house-majority-agenda-01150963"],", from 10 to 20 new members. And in the middle, the center-left ",["New Dems are projecting a caucus of over 140","https://www.newdemactionfund.com/news/what-theyre-saying-new-dems-deliver-the-house-majority-and-prepare-to-lead"]," members."]},{"k":"p","s":["I’m a ",["political scientist who has worked in and now studies Congress","https://sorellewg.com/"],". Figuring out the dynamics and direction of the 120th Congress requires looking at more than the ideological positions of the candidates who won. Instead, focusing on the number of candidates who won can provide insight into the direction of the party as a whole."]},{"k":"p","s":["The large – and at the time of writing, still growing – margins of Democratic control in the 120th Congress are the ",["biggest since 1993","https://www.caseyburgat.com/p/five-midterm-takeaways-with-pictures"],", before Congress became consistently competitive and increasingly polarized. Those large margins provide essential context for understanding how this new ideological coalition will work in Congress."]},{"k":"h","s":["Size matters"]},{"k":"p","s":["While history demonstrates that an ",["ideologically diverse party can be hard to wrangle","https://theconversation.com/from-the-freedom-caucus-to-the-democratic-socialists-small-groups-inside-parties-can-wreak-havoc-with-leaders-agenda-in-congress-289362"],", the size of the new Democratic majority provides some breathing room for policy negotiation and procedural debates."]},{"k":"p","s":["Unlike the current Republican Caucus that is ",["reliant on keeping historically narrow majorities together","https://www.pewresearch.org/short-reads/2024/12/17/slim-majorities-have-become-more-common-in-the-us-house-and-senate/"]," to pass party goals, future Democratic leadership can stand to lose a few votes. With a minimum of ",["254 seats in the House and 54 seats in the Senate","https://ballotpedia.org/Election_results,_2026:_U.S._Congress"],", small-scale Democratic defections are irrelevant."]},{"k":"p","s":["This breathing room provides the potential for negotiation, while also limiting any mandate an ideological group may claim."]},{"k":"p","s":["For instance, the 120th Congress will have eight members in the House who are ",["backed or affiliated with the Democratic Socialists of America","https://www.npr.org/2026/11/03/g-s1-150034/2026-midterm-election-dsa-candidates"],", known as the DSA. In raw terms of political power, when the majority has at least 36 votes to spare on any given party-line bill, this group may not matter in policymaking."]},{"k":"p","s":["But big numbers do matter."]},{"k":"p","s":["If a group – say, the entirety of the Progressive Caucus’ 100-plus membership – decides to stick together, leadership will be forced to listen. Thus, the potential power of ideological factions depends not only on their ideas but their own organizational skills."]},{"k":"p","s":["When ",["groups in Congress develop practices","https://press.uchicago.edu/ucp/books/book/chicago/D/bo249663334.html"]," such as confidential meetings or binding rules that require members vote together on certain votes, the legitimacy of group demands can be strengthened. This is a strategy that has been employed with relative success ",["by the far-right Republican Freedom Caucus","https://theconversation.com/from-the-freedom-caucus-to-the-democratic-socialists-small-groups-inside-parties-can-wreak-havoc-with-leaders-agenda-in-congress-289362"]," since it was formed in 2014."]},{"k":"h","s":["Details matter"]},{"k":"p","s":["The overarching policy goals for newly elected Democrats are consistent across the ideological spectrum: lowering the cost of living and rooting out corruption."]},{"k":"p","s":["This was highlighted in acceptance speeches by Democrats from ",["South Carolina","https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gGe0WMQOx6I"]," to ",["Texas","https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cK8wzjBpEoQ"]," to ",["Michigan","https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Btos5P_O2EY"],". All emphasized the same policy-focused promise: Instead of fighting left versus right, the fight should focus on the top versus the bottom."]},{"k":"p","s":["This shared vision is no doubt important. My research has shown that a ",["cohesive message","https://press.uchicago.edu/ucp/books/book/chicago/E/bo280067639.html"]," is a key part of winning and maintaining majority control."]},{"k":"p","s":["However, the “blue tsunami” was powered by voters with very specific policy demands. And as is always the case with policymaking, the details matter. Does healthcare reform mean reinstating the Obamacare subsidies set to expire on Jan. 1, 2027? Or does it mean something bolder, such as ",["Medicare for All","https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/3069"],"?"]},{"k":"p","s":["While there is power in numbers, the organizational strength and ultimate success of ideological groups in Congress depends on how unified they can be around specific policy goals and proposals."]},{"k":"h","s":["First hurdle: Pick a leader"]},{"k":"p","s":["This means that who is doing the unifying also matters."]},{"k":"p","s":["The success of any potential legislative package heavily relies on congressional leaders’ knowledge of ",["congressional rules","https://www.congress.gov/crs-product/R42843"]," and their willingness to incorporate member viewpoints."]},{"k":"p","s":["This necessity of having leadership in place to get legislation moving is epitomized by the order of operations for a new congressional session. In the coming weeks, ",["both parties will hold closed-door, secret-ballot elections","https://abcnews.com/Politics/congress-returns-crowded-lame-duck-session-hegseth-impeachment/story?id=137918357"]," to ",["select their new party leaders","https://www.house.gov/the-house-explained"],". That’s well before any legislation is even drafted."]},{"k":"p","s":["With a Democratic caucus filled with anti-establishment candidates across the ideological spectrum, and external pressure from ",["political pundits to dump current Democratic leadership","https://www.independent.co.uk/bulletin/culture/jon-stewart-chuck-schumer-midterms-b3080679.html"],", the future of the Democratic Party has been ",["projected onto this otherwise ritualistic vote","https://apnews.com/article/democratic-future-2028-progressives-moderates-7890426d2bbd6bbc2c6f8b72e6f9a54f"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["But the power and success of congressional leadership lies in its procedural acumen, not its ideological vision. ",["Some already in Congress","https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=DoN2gy6oR5g"]," have noted New York Democratic Rep. Hakeem Jeffries’ experience and working relationships in discussions of whether he should be house speaker. Furthermore, groups can extract concessions during leadership selection in exchange for their support, such as seats on powerful committees or an agreement on policy agenda items."]},{"k":"p","s":["Sen. Chuck Schumer, the longtime New York lawmaker aiming to lead Senate Democrats again, ",["faces more public criticism from his party","https://edition.cnn.com/2026/11/07/politics/senate-democrats-new-majority-leader"],". While no one has yet stepped up as an alternative, momentum is building for ",["Maryland Sen. Chris Van Hollen","https://thehill.com/homenews/campaign/6209487-van-hollen-senate-majority-leader/"],", who has said he is “in listening mode.”"]},{"k":"h","s":["Credit to all"]},{"k":"p","s":["To external observers, the selection of party leadership seems like a defining point for the party. But whether a new caucus translates to new leaders or new rules ultimately depends on the organizational power of new members and their already-serving co-workers – and what a party leader can offer them in terms of policy goals and procedural capabilities. Who is chosen as leader is not necessarily a signal of what the party’s policy goals will be."]},{"k":"p","s":["That picture is not yet clear – and it may not be for some time. After all, the new Democratic margins in Congress are a result of a collection of majority makers. The margins of victory tell a story about more than presidential backlash. Across the country, progressive enthusiasm and moderate appeal ",["turned voters toward the Democratic Party","https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2026/11/04/us/elections/midterms-swing-voters-democrats.html"],". And while everything is local, national enthusiasm matters, too."]},{"k":"p","s":["The 120th Congress will include progressives and moderates and the establishment candidates in the middle that are all required parts of the same whole. Or as political scientist E.E. Schattschneider argued in 1960 in his seminal work “ ",["The Semisovereign People","https://www.amazon.com/clp/0030133661?lv=shuf&channelId=500"],",” it would be a mistake to give credit to one group for the success of an election. Rather, achieving a consequential majority in America requires coalition building – and maintenance."]}],"chars":7443}};
